ev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/fffb378cb2ffe93ed9ee8b6044db137b415b76a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T08:21:30Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"Aidan P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T08:21:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ext): qualify [connect] tool names so the Datasources kind projects (#222)\n\n`project_connect` compared the manifest''s BARE connect tool name\n(`mcp:connection.create:call`) against the install''s granted caps, which\nare always QUALIFIED (`mcp:<ext>.connection.create:call`). The two can\nnever match, so no native extension''s `[connect]` block ever projected:\n`ext.list` reported `connect: null` and rubix-ai''s Datasources page\nsilently never offered the kind (seen with uart; ESR, ros and pdnsw use\nthe same shape).\n\nThe host owns the `<ext>.` prefix, so both halves are now qualified: the\ngrant check tests `mcp:<ext>.<tool>:call`, and `ExtConnect` carries the\ncallable `<ext>.<tool>` names — the ones the Datasources page passes to\n`mcp.call` and looks up in `tools.catalog`. Manifests are unchanged (the\nloader still binds bare names to `[[tools]]`). All-or-nothing still holds,\nand a bare grant does not satisfy the check.\n\nTests: ui_decl_connect_tests.rs (6). lb-host lib 599/599; ext_boot_spawn,\next_lifecycle, ext_publish, ext_ui, install_record, native,\nnative_install_grant_durability, native_republish all green. Verified live\non a rubix-ai node: `ext.list` now returns uart''s connect block.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"670942c4513516933b7d73d6cbfc6609ef0453e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/670942c4513516933b7d73d6cbfc6609ef0453e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/fffb378cb2ffe93ed9ee8b6044db137b415b76a5","verification":{"payload":"tree 670942c4513516933b7d73d6cbfc6609ef0453e6\nparent 32f07bbb75b0abf06a555a9c14ced6b96a36e665\nauthor Aidan P <aidan@enviroservices.com.au> 1790238090 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790238090 +0800\n\nfix(ext): qualify [connect] tool names so the Datasources kind projects (#222)\n\n`project_connect` compared the manifest''s BARE connect tool name\n(`mcp:connection.create:call`) against the install''s granted caps, which\nare always QUALIFIED (`mcp:<ext>.connection.create:call`). The two can\nnever match, so no native extension''s `[connect]` block ever projected:\n`ext.list` reported `connect: null` and rubix-ai''s Datasources page\nsilently never offered the kind (seen with uart; ESR, ros and pdnsw use\nthe same shape).\n\nThe host owns the `<ext>.` prefix, so both halves are now qualified: the\ngrant check tests `mcp:<ext>.<tool>:call`, and `ExtConnect` carries the\ncallable `<ext>.<tool>` names — the ones the Datasources page passes to\n`mcp.call` and looks up in `tools.catalog`. Manifests are unchanged (the\nloader still binds bare names to `[[tools]]`). All-or-nothing still holds,\nand a bare grant does not satisfy the check.\n\nTests: ui_decl_connect_tests.rs (6). lb-host lib 599/599; ext_boot_spawn,\next_lifecycle, ext_publish, ext_ui, install_record, native,\nnative_install_grant_durability, native_republish all green. Verified live\non a rubix-ai node: `ext.list` now returns uart''s connect block.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtN2KCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYjoQAHmdCHrZF1oqhnH3HjgJQuH5\ncCsPBTYYx+CW5Wyr8RsMHGipXbwZT