:"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/d109b016c81ea10be48ad79cf90675b8cae8d884","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKGQxMDliMDE2YzgxZWExMGJlNDhhZDc5Y2Y5MDY3NWI4Y2FlOGQ4ODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/8f7ac7501b42275dd583a676eacd564f83718a52","sha":"8f7ac7501b42275dd583a676eacd564f83718a52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/8f7ac7501b42275dd583a676eacd564f83718a52"}],"sha":"d109b016c81ea10be48ad79cf90675b8cae8d884","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/d109b016c81ea10be48ad79cf90675b8cae8d884"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/8f7ac7501b42275dd583a676eacd564f83718a52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T09:25:09Z","email":"49853921+brabeem@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brabeem sapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T09:25:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(store): upgrade to SurrealDB 3 / surrealkv 0.21 (#195)\n\n* feat(store): upgrade to SurrealDB 3 / surrealkv 0.21\n\nEngine-enforced read-only store.query, retrying reads, boot guard removed.\n\n* fix(store): visibility on the split-out response and SQL modules\n\n* fix(store): persist the last compaction; record a SurrealDB 3 index range defect\n\n* fix(ingest): (series, ts) index is opt-in — SurrealDB 3 datetime range defect\n\n* fix: retry every pure read; give the 100k-sample cap test real headroom\n\n* test(federation): gate read concurrency on slot occupancy, not the clock\n\n* test: tighten the rewritten budget-driver notes\n\n* ci: install gdb so a wedged test binary yields a backtrace\n\n* chore: drop two probes superseded by the final design\n\n* feat(store): name the cause when a SurrealDB 2 store cannot be opened\n\n* refactor(store): move the engine-open helpers out of open.rs\n\n* test(ingest): measure what the staging hop costs\n\n* fix(store): status must measure the LSM store, not the dead clog dir\n\n* test(bus): await the queryable instead of racing the routed call\n\n* docs(store): report the LSM engine as it is, not the old commit log\n\n* fix(ingest): the schema pass must survive a restart with data\n\n* fix(store): repair FLEXIBLE fields at boot; export the value macro\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: brabeemsapkota <claude.binod@codeduolabs.com>","tree":{"sha":"4b1abdd5a4caea33aa16f9d944b57c2f2d6bcf49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/4b1abdd5a4caea33aa16f9d944b57c2f2d6bcf49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/8f7ac7501b42275dd583a676eacd564f83718a52","verification":{"payload":"tree 4b1abdd5a4caea33aa16f9d944b57c2f2d6bcf49\nparent e3c60ada62f96521aeb8c833a325102d4a236b99\nauthor Brabeem sapkota <49853921+brabeem@users.noreply.github.com> 1788773109 +0545\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788773109 +0545\n\nfeat(store): upgrade to SurrealDB 3 / surrealkv 0.21 (#195)\n\n* feat(store): upgrade to SurrealDB 3 / surrealkv 0.21\n\nEngine-enforced read-only store.query, retrying reads, boot guard removed.\n\n* fix(store): visibility on the split-out response and SQL modules\n\n* fix(store): persist the last compaction; record a SurrealDB 3 index range defect\n\n* fix(ingest): (series, ts) index is opt-in — SurrealDB 3 datetime range defect\n\n* fix: retry every pure read; give the 100k-sample cap test real headroom\n\n* test(federation): gate read concurrency on slot occupancy, not the clock\n\n* test: tighten the rewritten budget-driver notes\n\n* ci: install gdb so a wedged test binary yields a backtrace\n\n* chore: drop two probes superseded by the final design\n\n* feat(store): name the cause when a SurrealDB 2 store cannot be opened\n\n* refactor(store): move the engine-open helpers out of open.rs\n\n* test(ingest): measure what the staging hop costs\n\n* fix(store): status must measure the LSM store, not the dead clog dir\n\n* test(bus): await the queryable instead of racing the routed call\n\n* docs(store): report the LSM engine as it is, not the old commit log\n\n* fix(ingest): the schema pass must survive a restart with data\n\n* fix(store): repair FLEXIBLE fields at boot; export the value macro\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: brabeemsapkota <claude.binod@codeduolabs.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnoL1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjXUQABGOh+swLrvl8VmdPpn31+Vw\nQ8K3qgBl6v6jdaOHCA0RbjNLsmGaKVMpcsAaRCxn2YYuGvCbta28o0Tp9yWN5i8A\ntxgB2HkafShfAgBt5WFjN9NRS6TiFjklkq6SslHjNXMqXKfNyWDtqmd+At+t2iL9\nsLro+MmmLpCMsu4U+Sjs4VyRQIfgrzwXC8jqSUaXPq4FKvrWUtPxHqN/rb/9SjYy\nxq+aczhjqrkYjqrXAFSJZHPhTQBAgNO0dNsdbbr3d0a1RWstG25dO9qqq4AZleD8\nOIhDloz7HYYo/q4Cjvm8BXCvID5Y2UHmX3FlVe8nRkVLUxLPfCiqq283K/yCENKx\nPgekd7I1uyu0w+Mg7wEtqywKLxVdOIN3UF4aQ5Tu0M5jZdyNK75xNudwNrGnMFbK\nxsr++Q9IwU72Kg32VyNKsXU/ZqkWLn7eBV7hz/LpuCnvWfwM65lSIwhlE9XctpG1\n5DMQVix1lnksABwtxkv7RND3sZhuTNS6jqyL+sd2L4YRqfUk80hDdcg9qVZcLKg5\nXKLhdMIiNWL9tjzklCyPOkK2sjp0mWrQ52xkxmfDl0rHIeyFbN+bRIKSKtpDoo9h\n8Xn6et8BdtlrOr0g28TTYEfP1RaPPWBUoaqVCYq8dXEknI9UIY4+y3hf042sGnBd\niBb4lqJkvtKnXHwfxqYP\n=oBfI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T09:25:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/8f7ac7501b42275dd583a676eacd564f83718a52","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDhmN2FjNzUwMWI0MjI3NWRkNTgzYTY3NmVhY2Q1NjRmODM3MThhNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/e3c60ada62f96521aeb8c833a325102d4a236b99","sha":"e3c60ada62f96521aeb8c833a325102d4a236b99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/e3c60ada62f96521aeb8c833a325102d4a236b99"}],"sha":"8f7ac7501b42275dd583a676eacd564f83718a52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/8f7ac7501b42275dd583a676eacd564f83718a52"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/e3c60ada62f96521aeb8c833a325102d4a236b99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T05:18:28Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"Aidan P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T05:18:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(reports): authored page breaks + a typed export-options contract (#193)\n\n* feat(reports): authored page breaks + a typed export-options contract\n\nTwo additive things and the refactor they both need.\n\n`Cell.pageBreakBefore` — an author-set page break, honoured by `paginate`\nahead of its fit rule, so a report author states what goes on a page\ninstead of dragging panels until the row arithmetic happens to agree. It\nis a MARKER, not a page number: numbers are absolute on a relative board\nand rot on the first insert, while a boolean on the band that starts a\npage survives dragging and composes with the fit rule. Markers collapse\nacross a row with OR, so marking any tile of a KPI row breaks before the\nwhole row.\n\n`ExportOptions` on BOTH doors — the HTTP route and the `report.export`\nMCP arm take the same type, deliberately, because two doors onto one\nexport must not grow two option vocabularies. Paper, orientation,\nmargins, scale, pageNumbers, index. The last two had rendered for months\nwith nothing setting them; `report_export` sets them now, which is the\nline that turns two finished renderer features on. Validation is loud: an\nunknown paper/orientation, a bad margin/scale, or margins that swallow\nthe page are each a BadInput naming the field, raised BEFORE the record\nread so a typo costs no dashboard read, brand resolve or Typst compile.\n\nThe six hardcoded `A4_*` consts become one `PageGeometry` threaded\nthrough pagination, placement and the Typst template — landed first as a\npure refactor with the round-trip test green, exactly as the scope\nordered, since it touches the files that define the cross-repo contract.\n`geometry.rs` would have gone past the FILE-LAYOUT ceiling, so placement\nmoved to `cell_rect.rs`: three questions (which paper, which page, where\non it), three files, one shared page box.\n\nThe trap the scope flagged was real. `paginate` never sees `Cell` — it\nlays out over the client''s rendered panels, which carry no marker — so\n`Placed` carries it and `panels_to_place` resolves it by id, a repeat\nclone inheriting its source''s. That resolution is now one `cell_for` used\nby both the title and the marker; two copies would have drifted silently,\na clone keeping its title but losing its page break.\n\nBACKWARD COMPATIBILITY IS MEASURED, NOT ASSERTED. The scope asks for\n\"options absent => byte-identical PDF to the current implementation\",\nwhich no test inside the branch can prove. Verified against master\ndirectly: same board (including a band at row 26, the flow case),\nexported on both, sha256 18ce9828... on each, `cmp` clean — despite\n`#set page` moving from `paper: \"a4\"` to explicit millimetres.\n\nAlso repairs a PRE-EXISTING breakage, called out rather than folded in:\n`cargo test -p lb-host --lib` did not compile on master, because\n`grafana/bind.rs`''s test fixture was never updated when\n`Target::show_when` was added. It blocks every unit test in the crate,\nincluding the ones added here.\n\nNot tagged. Publishing a `node-v*` tag is a release decision and is what\nunblocks rubix-ai''s report-builder-ux Phase 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012boor1p7U4PXeoyiN55z6u\n\n* style(tests): rustfmt dashboard_show_when_test\n\nThe `fmt` CI job has been red since #192 landed: two `call_dashboard_tool`\ncalls in this test exceed the width rustfmt allows for a chained\n`.await.expect(..)` tail, so `cargo fmt --all --check` reported two diffs\non master and on every branch cut from it. A gate that is red for a reason\nunrelated to the branch under review reports nothing, so take the\nformatter''s output as-is. Formatting only — no test behaviour changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QmjRJux86pZuMwPFjnzsHd\n\n* refactor(layout): split the three files over the 400-line limit\n\nThe `file-layout` ratchet reported three files past the flat limit that no\nbaseline covers, and a fourth entry it could drop. Fix the movement in the\nwrong direction rather than re-baselining it — the script''s whole contract is\nthat the backlog may only shrink.\n\n- `report_export_media_test.rs` (603, and grown by THIS branch from 480): one\n  file was carrying four separate claims. Split by what each asserts — the\n  media round trip (here), bridge-vs-route byte parity, the malformed-bundle\n  refusals, and the mandatory deny + workspace-isolation categories — with the\n  real-infra fixture they share moved to `tests/support/report_media.rs`,\n  `#[path]`-included exactly as the `series.producer.health` suites do. No test\n  was dropped, weakened or added: the same 8 assertions run, in 4 files.\n- `nav/model.rs` (422): the RESOLVED shapes (`ResolvedNav`/`ResolvedItem`/\n  `ResolvedSource`) are the resolver''s OUTPUT contract, not the stored record,\n  and they change for resolver reasons. Moved to `nav/resolved.rs`.\n- `gateway routes/nav.rs` (417): `/nav/pref` is the member-owned pick, the\n  gateway twin of the host''s own `nav/pref.rs`. Moved to `routes/nav_pref.rs`.\n\nThe baseline loses only `rust/extensions/ros/src/ros_fake.rs`, whose file is\ndeleted. Trimmed BY HAND on purpose: `--update` would also RAISE twelve caps to\nmatch master''s grown files, which is the re-baselining the ratchet forbids.\n\nThose twelve remain red and are untouched here — they are master''s backlog from\nother PRs, not this branch''s, and each needs its own split.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QmjRJux86pZuMwPFjnzsHd\n\n* fix(tests): seed the reminder author''s grant the way the store keys it\n\n`build-and-test (rest)` has been red since #176 on one test:\n`a_due_reminder_fires_from_the_boot_spawned_tick`. Red on master too — it is\nnot this branch''s — and red for a reason the assertion could not show.\n\n#176 fixed `fire_reminder` to strip the `user:` prefix before re-resolving the\nauthor''s caps, because grants are stored under the BARE user name: every\nshipped write path (`membership_add`, the gateway grant routes, invite accept)\nstrips it, and `mint_session` strips it to read them back. That fix was right;\nthis fixture still seeded `Subject::User(\"user:alice\")` and\n`membership_add_raw(.., \"user:alice\", ..)` — rows no production path writes.\n\nSo the fire-time re-resolve found ZERO caps, `outbox.enqueue` denied, and the\nreactor did what a denial does since #176: rescheduled to the next slot and\nwent quiet. Nothing was delivered, `eventually` timed out at 20s, and the panic\nsaid only that the tick \"must fire\" — pointing at the reactor, which was\nworking perfectly the whole time.\n\nSeed both rows under the bare handle. The principal keeps its prefixed `sub`\n(that is the identity every gate and audit row records); only the grant lookup\nwants the bare one, which is precisely what the code under test does.\n\n    running 4 tests\n    test a_due_reminder_fires_from_the_boot_spawned_tick ... ok\n    test result: ok. 4 passed; 0 failed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QmjRJux86pZuMwPFjnzsHd\n\n* refactor(dashboard): take model.rs off the file-size backlog\n\n`dashboard/model.rs` was 1109 lines against a 1056 baseline — this branch had\nalready pushed it there, and the `exportProfiles` field that follows would push\nit further. Growing a baseline entry is the one direction the ratchet forbids,\nso shrink it instead of adding to the backlog.\n\n`Cell` and its binding types are the obvious seam: `Cell` changes for\npanel-model reasons (a new render field, a new grid knob) while `Dashboard`\nchanges for page-settings ones, and the two have never needed to be read\ntogether. So:\n\n- `cell.rs` (264) — the grid cell, its two serde predicates, and the\n  explicit-null regression test that belongs to it;\n- `binding.rs` (129) — `Source`/`Action`/`Target`/`QueryOptions`, what a cell\n  binds to;\n- `null_default.rs` (17) — the serde adapter all three now share, which none of\n  them owns.\n\n`model.rs` drops to 745, comfortably under its baseline, and the gate stops\nreporting it. Re-exported from `model.rs`, so every `super::model::Cell` path\nand the `mod.rs` barrel resolve exactly as before — not one call site changed.\nPure code motion: no behaviour change, 530 lib tests green either side.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QmjRJux86pZuMwPFjnzsHd\n\n* feat(dashboard): store a report''s export profiles on the board\n\nReverses this scope''s \"no stored export profiles here\" non-goal. That non-goal\nassumed \"the client stores it\" was an available option, and on this record it is\nnot: `Dashboard` has no `#[serde(flatten)]` catch-all and DROPS unknown\ntop-level keys on save, so a client-authored `exportProfiles` survives until the\nnext layout save and then silently vanishes — a control that appears to work and\nforgets. There is nowhere else on the record for a profile to live, so \"lb\nstores nothing\" and \"an admin can save a profile\" cannot both hold.\n\nThat is the same mechanical reason `heading`, `headingSize`, `icon`, `color`,\n`varsDisplay`, `reportIds`, `width` and `compact` are typed lb fields whose only\nreader is the client. \"State without a reader\" does not survive that precedent —\nthe reader is the client, and the fourth layer of the shipped preserve-on-omit\n`meta` pattern is a typed lb field.\n\n- `ExportProfile { id, name, options }` in its own `report/profile.rs`, reusing\n  `ExportOptions` VERBATIM: a profile IS a named set of the options the export\n  already takes, so there stays exactly one option vocabulary. A second spelling\n  of \"what a PDF should look like\" could only drift from the first.\n- `Dashboard.export_profiles` (`exportProfiles`), riding `reportIds`'' contract\n  exactly — absent PRESERVES, `[]` CLEARS, empty stays off the wire — through\n  all four layers: model field, save schema + `PageMeta` merge, tool arg,\n  gateway body. A pack may declare them too.\n\n**lb still never reads a profile.** `report.export` takes no profile id; the\nclient picks one and sends that profile''s `options` on the call. Storage and\nserde, nothing more — said so in the doc comments, so the next reader does not\ngo hunting for the consumer.\n\nBoth contract directions are tested, in their own names so a failure says which\none broke — `export_profiles_preserve_on_omit` (a panel drag must not delete an\nadmin''s profiles) and `export_profiles_clear_on_empty` (deleting the last\nprofile must actually get back to the default) — plus a wire-shape test over the\nreal tool boundary, which is the claim the typed field exists to make.\n\n`pack/apply.rs` would have crossed its own baseline taking the new key, so its\npage-settings vocabulary moved to `pack/page_meta.rs`, where a page setting is\nnow one line beside the schema it mirrors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QmjRJux86pZuMwPFjnzsHd\n\n* docs(dashboard): model.rs says what it now holds\n\nThe module doc still opened \"the dashboard record + cell types\" a commit after\nthe cell types moved out. A stale first line is the one line every reader trusts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QmjRJux86pZuMwPFjnzsHd\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2c85883b92c70c3f9f54b700787651adb9e6c79f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/2c85883b92c70c3f9f54b700787651adb9e6c79f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/e3c60ada62f96521aeb8c833a325102d4a236b99","verification":{"payload":"tree 2c85883b92c70c3f9f54b700787651adb9e6c79f\nparent aa183d16a05ded5f01c8fe3da476ca748cd5374a\nauthor Aidan P <aidan@enviroservices.com.au> 1788153508 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788153508 +1000\n\nfeat(reports): authored page breaks + a typed export-options contract (#193)\n\n* feat(reports): authored page breaks + a typed export-options contract\n\nTwo additive things and the refactor they both need.\n\n`Cell.pageBreakBefore` — an author-set page break, honoured by `paginate`\nahead of its fit rule, so a report author states what goes on a page\ninstead of dragging panels until the row arithmetic happens to agree. It\nis a MARKER, not a page number: numbers are absolute on a relative board\nand rot on the first insert, while a boolean on the band that starts a\npage survives dragging and composes with the fit rule. Markers collapse\nacross a row with OR, so marking any tile of a KPI row breaks before the\nwhole row.\n\n`ExportOptions` on BOTH doors — the HTTP route and the `report.export`\nMCP arm take the same type, deliberately, because two doors onto one\nexport must not grow two option vocabularies. Paper, orientation,\nmargins, scale, pageNumbers, index. The last two had rendered for months\nwith nothing setting them; `report_export` sets them now, which is the\nline that turns two finished renderer features on. Validation is loud: an\nunknown paper/orientation, a bad margin/scale, or margins that swallow\nthe page are each a BadInput naming the field, raised BEFORE the record\nread so a typo costs no dashboard read, brand resolve or Typst compile.\n\nThe six hardcoded `A4_*` consts become one `PageGeometry` threaded\nthrough pagination, placement and the Typst template — landed first as a\npure refactor with the round-trip test green, exactly as the scope\nordered, since it touches the files that define the cross-repo contract.\n`geometry.rs` would have gone past the FILE-LAYOUT ceiling, so placement\nmoved to `cell_rect.rs`: three questions (which paper, which page, where\non it), three files, one shared page box.\n\nThe trap the scope flagged was real. `paginate` never sees `Cell` — it\nlays out over the client''s rendered panels, which carry no marker — so\n`Placed` carries it and `panels_to_place` resolves it by id, a repeat\nclone inheriting its source''s. That resolution is now one `cell_for` used\nby both the title and the marker; two copies would have drifted silently,\na clone keeping its title but losing its page break.\n\nBACKWARD COMPATIBILITY IS MEASURED, NOT ASSERTED. The scope asks for\n\"options absent => byte-identical PDF to the current implementation\",\nwhich no test inside the branch can prove. Verified against master\ndirectly: same board (including a band at row 26, the flow case),\nexported on both, sha256 18ce9828... on each, `cmp` clean — despite\n`#set page` moving from `paper: \"a4\"` to explicit millimetres.\n\nAlso repairs a PRE-EXISTING breakage, called out rather than folded in:\n`cargo test -p lb-host --lib` did not compile on master, because\n`grafana/bind.rs`''s test fixture was never updated when\n`Target::show_when` was added. It blocks every unit test in the crate,\nincluding the ones added here.\n\nNot tagged. Publishing a `node-v*` tag is a release decision and is what\nunblocks rubix-ai''s report-builder-ux Phase 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012boor1p7U4PXeoyiN55z6u\n\n* style(tests): rustfmt dashboard_show_when_test\n\nThe `fmt` CI job has been red since #192 landed: two `call_dashboard_tool`\ncalls in this test exceed the width rustfmt allows for a chained\n`.await.expect(..)` tail, so `cargo fmt --all --check` reported two diffs\non master and on every branch cut from it. A gate that is red for a reason\nunrelated to the branch under review reports nothing, so take the\nformatter''s output as-is. Formatting only — no test behaviour changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QmjRJux86pZuMwPFjnzsHd\n\n* refactor(layout): split the three files over the 400-line limit\n\nThe `file-layout` ratchet reported three files past the flat limit that no\nbaseline covers, and a fourth entry it could drop. Fix the movement in the\nwrong direction rather than re-baselining it — the script''s whole contract is\nthat the backlog may only shrink.\n\n- `report_export_media_test.rs` (603, and grown by THIS branch from 480): one\n  file was carrying four separate claims. Split by what each asserts — the\n  media round trip (here), bridge-vs-route byte parity, the malformed-bundle\n  refusals, and the mandatory deny + workspace-isolation categories — with the\n  real-infra fixture they share moved to `tests/support/report_media.rs`,\n  `#[path]`-included exactly as the `series.producer.health` suites do. No test\n  was dropped, weakened or added: the same 8 assertions run, in 4 files.\n- `nav/model.rs` (422): the RESOLVED shapes (`ResolvedNav`/`ResolvedItem`/\n  `ResolvedSource`) are the resolver''s OUTPUT contract, not the stored record,\n  and they change for resolver reasons. Moved to `nav/resolved.rs`.\n- `gateway routes/nav.rs` (417): `/nav/pref` is the member-owned pick, the\n  gateway twin of the host''s own `nav/pref.rs`. Moved to `routes/nav_pref.rs`.\n\nThe baseline loses only `rust/extensions/ros/src/ros_fake.rs`, whose file is\ndeleted. Trimmed BY HAND on purpose: `--update` would also RAISE twelve caps to\nmatch master''s grown files, which is the re-baselining the ratchet forbids.\n\nThose twelve remain red and are untouched here — they are master''s backlog from\nother PRs, not this branch''s, and each needs its own split.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QmjRJux86pZuMwPFjnzsHd\n\n* fix(tests): seed the reminder author''s grant the way the store keys it\n\n`build-and-test (rest)` has been red since #176 on one test:\n`a_due_reminder_fires_from_the_boot_spawned_tick`. Red on master too — it is\nnot this branch''s — and red for a reason the assertion could not show.\n\n#176 fixed `fire_reminder` to strip the `user:` prefix before re-resolving the\nauthor''s caps, because grants are stored under the BARE user name: every\nshipped write path (`membership_add`, the gateway grant routes, invite accept)\nstrips it, and `mint_session` strips it to read them back. That fix was right;\nthis fixture still seeded `Subject::User(\"user:alice\")` and\n`membership_add_raw(.., \"user:alice\", ..)` — rows no production path writes.\n\nSo the fire-time re-resolve found ZERO caps, `outbox.enqueue` denied, and the\nreactor did what a denial does since #176: rescheduled to the next slot and\nwent quiet. Nothing was delivered, `eventually` timed out at 20s, and the panic\nsaid only that the tick \"must fire\" — pointing at the reactor, which was\nworking perfectly the whole time.\n\nSeed both rows under the bare handle. The principal keeps its prefixed `sub`\n(that is the identity every gate and audit row records); only the grant lookup\nwants the bare one, which is precisely what the code under test does.\n\n    running 4 tests\n    test a_due_reminder_fires_from_the_boot_spawned_tick ... ok\n    test result: ok. 4 passed; 0 failed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QmjRJux86pZuMwPFjnzsHd\n\n* refactor(dashboard): take model.rs off the file-size backlog\n\n`dashboard/model.rs` was 1109 lines against a 1056 baseline — this branch had\nalready pushed it there, and the `exportProfiles` field that follows would push\nit further. Growing a baseline entry is the one direction the ratchet forbids,\nso shrink it instead of adding to the backlog.\n\n`Cell` and its binding types are the obvious seam: `Cell` changes for\npanel-model reasons (a new render field, a new grid knob) while `Dashboard`\nchanges for page-settings ones, and the two have never needed to be read\ntogether. So:\n\n- `cell.rs` (264) — the grid cell, its two serde predicates, and the\n  explicit-null regression test that belongs to it;\n- `binding.rs` (129) — `Source`/`Action`/`Target`/`QueryOptions`, what a cell\n  binds to;\n- `null_default.rs` (17) — the serde adapter all three now share, which none of\n  them owns.\n\n`model.rs` drops to 745, comfortably under its baseline, and the gate stops\nreporting it. Re-exported from `model.rs`, so every `super::model::Cell` path\nand the `mod.rs` barrel resolve exactly as before — not one call site changed.\nPure code motion: no behaviour change, 530 lib tests green either side.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QmjRJux86pZuMwPFjnzsHd\n\n* feat(dashboard): store a report''s export profiles on the board\n\nReverses this scope''s \"no stored export profiles here\" non-goal. That non-goal\nassumed \"the client stores it\" was an available option, and on this record it is\nnot: `Dashboard` has no `#[serde(flatten)]` catch-all and DROPS unknown\ntop-level keys on save, so a client-authored `exportProfiles` survives until the\nnext layout save and then silently vanishes — a control that appears to work and\nforgets. There is nowhere else on the record for a profile to live, so \"lb\nstores nothing\" and \"an admin can save a profile\" cannot both hold.\n\nThat is the same mechanical reason `heading`, `headingSize`, `icon`, `color`,\n`varsDisplay`, `reportIds`, `width` and `compact` are typed lb fields whose only\nreader is the client. \"State without a reader\" does not survive that precedent —\nthe reader is the client, and the fourth layer of the shipped preserve-on-omit\n`meta` pattern is a typed lb field.\n\n- `ExportProfile { id, name, options }` in its own `report/profile.rs`, reusing\n  `ExportOptions` VERBATIM: a profile IS a named set of the options the export\n  already takes, so there stays exactly one option vocabulary. A second spelling\n  of \"what a PDF should look like\" could only drift from the first.\n- `Dashboard.export_profiles` (`exportProfiles`), riding `reportIds`'' contract\n  exactly — absent PRESERVES, `[]` CLEARS, empty stays off the wire — through\n  all four layers: model field, save schema + `PageMeta` merge, tool arg,\n  gateway body. A pack may declare them too.\n\n**lb still never reads a profile.** `report.export` takes no profile id; the\nclient picks one and sends that profile''s `options` on the call. Storage and\nserde, nothing more — said so in the doc comments, so the next reader does not\ngo hunting for the consumer.\n\nBoth contract directions are tested, in their own names so a failure says which\none broke — `export_profiles_preserve_on_omit` (a panel drag must not delete an\nadmin''s profiles) and `export_profiles_clear_on_empty` (deleting the last\nprofile must actually get back to the default) — plus a wire-shape test over the\nreal tool boundary, which is the claim the typed field exists to make.\n\n`pack/apply.rs` would have crossed its own baseline taking the new key, so its\npage-settings vocabulary moved to `pack/page_meta.rs`, where a page setting is\nnow one line beside the schema it mirrors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QmjRJux86pZuMwPFjnzsHd\n\n* docs(dashboard): model.rs says what it now holds\n\nThe module doc still opened \"the dashboard record + cell types\" a commit after\nthe cell types moved out. A stale first line is the one line every reader trusts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QmjRJux86pZuMwPFjnzsHd\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlQ6kCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAefkQAA8NHZjjFXaYJtaZxK8UDq2H\ngUVANfuFilsciWpspdOPslSYr/aNqpKsW65G0HCHgOd+aDkR3pR4Vq3Y/oTOPc2T\nkPLN8Z1EL8gyTxHbsvXTwmItH7QxcUFFesgN14SNjnCMX5JB4YRGj8+aajT46ZDD\nK+rQ3Ba/AdJOPdNmDZseM1NByS9O1WONz2Jh05RIOCmjDC0d64+D0PkPitdnvAfs\ntUP5cCoAABkQoE6w4VIYeBvgLsqjrfY6rprA