ubscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/9b81f2943ec75820ad9d89903b7e659ea59508ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T01:42:01Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T01:42:01Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"message":"docs(reports): session doc + scope note for report.export on the bridge\n\nRecords the shape and the two measurements that decided it (the /mcp/call 2 MiB\ncap; the media store''s complete absence of a reaping seam), the contract decision\nthat changed mid-session (`snapshots` is a REQUIRED key — a document missing it is\na wire bug, not \"no captures\"), and the four follow-ups, of which the tag is the\none that blocks every downstream consumer.\n\nDeliberately NOT promoted to doc-site: no released node serves the verb yet, and a\npublic page describing one would document something that does not exist. It goes\npublic with the node-v* tag.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019yLo4kXPR8Ne893yQMHZHS","tree":{"sha":"76c1e4f876774b1f7155b07840930121bbf4b14f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/76c1e4f876774b1f7155b07840930121bbf4b14f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/9b81f2943ec75820ad9d89903b7e659ea59508ce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/9b81f2943ec75820ad9d89903b7e659ea59508ce","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDliODFmMjk0M2VjNzU4MjBhZDlkODk5MDNiN2U2NTllYTU5NTA4Y2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/44d80de09018e1b56c65a1ca6bdc769574495a8d","sha":"44d80de09018e1b56c65a1ca6bdc769574495a8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/44d80de09018e1b56c65a1ca6bdc769574495a8d"}],"sha":"9b81f2943ec75820ad9d89903b7e659ea59508ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/9b81f2943ec75820ad9d89903b7e659ea59508ce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/44d80de09018e1b56c65a1ca6bdc769574495a8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T01:11:22Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T01:11:22Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"message":"reports(Track A): report.export over the MCP bridge, trading media ids\n\n`report.export` was deliberately absent from MCP dispatch — it is a gateway\nbinary route, and an extension page has no bearer token and no bytes seam. So an\nextension could create, read, share and list reports and could not export one:\neverything but the point. This is the same caller, the same wall and the same\nanswer as `media/read.rs`.\n\nThe shape is measured, not chosen. `/mcp/call` carries a deliberate 2 MiB\nblast-radius cap against the export route''s 32 MiB, and the comment beside it\nrefuses exactly the widening this would have asked for. So the verb trades IDS:\n\n    { id, snapshotMediaId? }  ->  { pdfMediaId, bytes, mime }\n\nsnapshots up through the shipped media.upload_* path, PDF down through the\nshipped media.read. Two of the three steps already existed. It also removes a\nproblem rather than moving one: the PDF is composed once and STORED, so there is\nno byte cache, no digest key and no TTL-on-a-cache.\n\nNew: `report/export_media.rs` — the media-id envelope around `report_export`.\nIt adds NO authorization: `report_export` authorizes `mcp:report.export:call`\nfirst and re-runs `dashboard_get`''s three gates under the same principal. The\nPDF is stored under the CALLER''s own `mcp:media.upload:call`, so the verb cannot\nmint a record its caller can''t read back.\n\nCap aliasing: `report.export` needs no `gate_tool_for` arm — it falls through to\nits own concrete cap, which IS in AUTHOR_CAPS. `report_gate_tests` pins that\nfall-through, because an alias added later would silently widen export to\neveryone who can read a report.\n\nContract decision: the bundle''s `snapshots` key is REQUIRED. A caller who wants\nthe skeleton omits `snapshotMediaId`; a document missing the key is a wire bug,\nand defaulting it to empty would answer a half-written blob with a\nplausible-looking PDF of error tiles while the UI reported success.\n\nTests — real store, real media store, real Typst, no mocks:\n  report_export_media_test  8 passed  (round trip, PARITY with the route byte\n                                       for byte, deny x2 + negative control,\n                                       ws isolation x2, origin tag, refusals)\n  report_bridge_test        5 passed  (POST /mcp/call: reachability under a REAL\n                                       member''s role-bundle caps, the mandatory\n                                       deny over the bridge, ws isolation,\n                                       plain-dashboard refusal)\n  report_test 29 · report_export_test 3 · media_test 8 · report_routes_test 6\n\nThe reachability test is the one that matters: `tool_gate.rs` documents four\nverbs that shipped, catalogued and unusable, every one invisible to tests that\ncalled the host fn directly.\n\nRefs NubeIO/ext-ros#6 (Track A).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019yLo4kXPR8Ne893yQMHZHS","tree":{"sha":"9c451bd29453bc2bb940dccc72741fcdb673f646","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/9c451bd29453bc2bb940dccc72741fcdb673f646"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/44d80de09018e1b56c65a1ca6bdc769574495a8d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https: