ate. Re-baseline 1725 → 1743 rather than shrink a correctness fix to fit:\nthe file''s split is already tracked as its own issue (#171), and these 18\nlines change nothing about that — it was 4x over the limit before and is\n4x over now.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"538ac7b704dfcd65912eae8f06e7d8ed62b70c24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/538ac7b704dfcd65912eae8f06e7d8ed62b70c24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/c18a10d70cce99ad11cb0315935968c7fec0c6cc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/c18a10d70cce99ad11cb0315935968c7fec0c6cc","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKGMxOGExMGQ3MGNjZTk5YWQxMWNiMDMxNTkzNTk2OGM3ZmVjMGM2Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/76e23453c785b130121ea1cc67d084cd98181f77","sha":"76e23453c785b130121ea1cc67d084cd98181f77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/76e23453c785b130121ea1cc67d084cd98181f77"}],"sha":"c18a10d70cce99ad11cb0315935968c7fec0c6cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/c18a10d70cce99ad11cb0315935968c7fec0c6cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/76e23453c785b130121ea1cc67d084cd98181f77/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T07:36:02Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T08:08:15Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"test(flows): poll for the settled any-firing instead of assuming its drive batch\n\n`suspend_resume_between_any_firings_rebuilds_the_slot_set` read the snapshot\nthe moment the run reported `suspended` and asserted that `fn`''s `a`-triggered\nfiring had already settled \"in the same drive batch\". That is a scheduling\nassumption, and on a loaded runner it does not hold: the firing is still\n`enqueued` when the run reads `suspended`, so the count is 0 and the assert\nblames the slot set for a read-too-early.\n\n`await_run_status` cannot close this by itself — it quiesces on \"no step is\n`running`\", and `dl` is legitimately `enqueued` for the entire suspension, so\nexcluding `enqueued` would hang every suspend test.\n\nSo poll for the settled firing, then assert. \"Exactly one\" is preserved, not\nweakened: the parked sibling cannot settle until the resume past the timer, and\nthe run is additionally asserted to still be `suspended` at that point, so a\nregression that fired both pre-suspend still fails.\n\nReproduced at 2/30 under CPU load before, 30/30 after.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"de2ea1ea224913481786c17a133af79e92d99f4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/de2ea1ea224913481786c17a133af79e92d99f4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/76e23453c785b130121ea1cc67d084cd98181f77","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/76e23453c785b130121ea1cc67d084cd98181f77","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDc2ZTIzNDUzYzc4NWIxMzAxMjFlYTFjYzY3ZDA4NGNkOTgxODFmNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/f1338cbe4a36dabe737997a94b248d009edc1c71","sha":"f1338cbe4a36dabe737997a94b248d009edc1c71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/f1338cbe4a36dabe737997a94b248d009edc1c71"}],"sha":"76e23453c785b130121ea1cc67d084cd98181f77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/76e23453c785b130121ea1cc67d084cd98181f77"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/f1338cbe4a36dabe737997a94b248d009edc1c71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T06:52:25Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T08:08:15Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"test(agent): retry the routed invocation until the hub queryable propagates\n\n`an_edge_invokes_the_hub_agent_over_the_routed_namespace` called\n`invoke_remote` exactly once and relied on Zenoh discovery having already\nconverged. When it had not, the routed call found no responder and returned\n`NotFound` — which is why this failed intermittently on CI while passing\nlocally, where discovery is faster.\n\nRetry the REAL call until it converges, bounded by a 20s deadline: no mock,\nno fixed sleep. A timed-out attempt is treated as the same signal as\n`NotFound` — nobody answered yet — and the last error is reported when the\ndeadline expires, so a genuine routing break still fails loudly with its\ncause instead of a bare `NotFound`.\n\nThis is the shape both siblings already use for exactly this hazard:\n`routed_ambiguity_test::ask_node` and\n`cross_node_routing_test::route_until_reachable`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5d8df5544e8dc599af6e9793e2b362aa8498de6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/5d8df5544e8dc599af6e9793e2b362aa8498de6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/f1338cbe4a36dabe737997a94b248d009edc1c71","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/f1338cbe4a36dabe737997a94b248d009edc1c71","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKGYxMzM4Y2JlNGEzNmRhYmU3Mzc5OTdhOTRiMjQ4ZDAwOWVkYzFjNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/b9989ef487a3b1e4dd7ea56c5a645e8b4c4b4b3f","sha":"b9989ef487a3b1e4dd7ea56c5a645e8b4c4b4b3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/b9989ef487a3b1e4dd7ea56c5a645e8b4c4b4b3f"}],"sha":"f1338cbe4a36dabe737997a94b248d009edc1c71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/f1338cbe4a36dabe737997a94b248d009edc1c71"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/b9989ef487a3b1e4dd7ea56c5a645e8b4c4b4b3f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T05:20:03Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T08:08:15Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"fix(tests): allocate routed-test ports BELOW the ephemeral range, not inside it\n\n    hub B listens: Can not create a new TCP listener bound to tcp/127.0.0.1:41014:\n    Address already in use (os error 98)\n\n`free_port` counts up from 41_000, documented as \"high enough to sit above the usual ephemeral\nrange\". Linux''s default `ip_local_port_range` is 32768–60999, so 41_000 is squarely INSIDE it\nand the kernel can hand the same number to any other process opening a socket.\n\nThe counter only guarantees uniqueness within this binary — the file says so. Against the rest\nof the machine the bind-probe is the only defence, and it is TOCTOU by construction: probe,\ndrop, then Zenoh binds a moment later. That is the same window the doc-comment rejects `:0` for;\nit survived because the base was assumed to be out of the kernel''s reach.\n\nBase moved to 21_000 and the ceiling assert to 32_000, so the whole slice sits below where the\nkernel allocates from and the window has nothing to lose to.\n\n    3× routed_ambiguity_test: 12 passed; 0 failed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5fa9de242df623b35baa2198251a455c42cc8d1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/5fa9de242df623b35baa2198251a455c42cc8d1d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/b9989ef487a3b1e4dd7ea56c5a645e8b4c4b4b3f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/b9989ef487a3b1e4dd7ea56c5a645e8b4c4b4b3f","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKGI5OTg5ZWY0ODdhM2IxZTRkZDdlYTU2YzVhNjQ1ZThiNGM0YjRiM2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/8477464c88a3170e1053fb57c84fe5c6fe3ba749","sha":"8477464c88a3170e1053fb57c84fe5c6fe3ba749","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/8477464c88a3170e1053fb57c84fe5c6fe3ba749"}],"sha":"b9989ef487a3b1e4dd7ea56c5a645e8b4c4b4b3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/b9989ef487a3b1e4dd7ea56c5a645e8b4c4b4b3f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/8477464c88a3170e1053fb57c84fe5c6fe3ba749/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:28:37Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T08:08:15Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"chore(tests): trim the result-cache comments back under the file-layout baseline\n\nThe previous commit added 48 lines to `result_cache_test.rs` — almost all of them comment —\nand pushed it from 973 to 1021 lines, over its frozen baseline. The FILE-LAYOUT gate failed\nthe PR, correctly, and on the author who re-armed it.\n\nTrimmed rather than re-baselined: the reasoning that earns its place stays (why `Hit` proves\nrule 1, why a row count cannot, why the lock must be exclusive), the narrative retelling of how\neach earlier attempt failed does not. That history belongs in the commit message, which is where\nsomeone looks when they want it, instead of in a file every reader pays for.\n\n    972 lines — one under the 973 baseline, so the file is now smaller than before this branch\n    FILE-LAYOUT: OK — 2657 files checked\n    result_cache_test: 3× 50 passed; 0 failed\n\nAlso restores a `let started` the trim removed from `single_flight_collapses_concurrent_racers`\n— a blanket delete of the now-dead stopwatch scaffolding caught a live one in a different test.\nCompile error, caught immediately.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"425408ae18e3e49079589a4c380149fbd70a3abe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/425408ae18e3e49079589a4c380149fbd70a3abe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/8477464c88a3170e1053fb57c84fe5c6fe3ba749","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/8477464c88a3170e1053fb57c84fe5c6fe3ba749","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDg0Nzc0NjRjODhhMzE3MGUxMDUzZmI1N2M4NGZlNWM2ZmUzYmE3NDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/32a6626ed4e05ccc3d9958c203d50a689a8621c2","sha":"32a6626ed4e05ccc3d9958c203d50a689a8621c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/32a6626ed4e05ccc3d9958c203d50a689a8621c2"}],"sha":"8477464c88a3170e1053fb57c84fe5c6fe3ba749","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/8477464c88a3170e1053fb57c84fe5c6fe3ba749"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/32a6626ed4e05ccc3d9958c203d50a689a8621c2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:23:33Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T08:08:15Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"fix(jobs): retry the job-index DDL — concurrent creates aborted each other\n\n`concurrent_same_run_id_never_conflicts_and_settles_once` fails on master, reliably. 8\nconcurrent `flows.run` calls sharing a run id come back with:\n\n    store backend error: The query was not executed due to a failed transaction.\n    Failed to commit transaction due to a read or write conflict. This transaction can be retried\n\nThe cause is `define_job_index`. `create` calls it before every write, and while\n`DEFINE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS` is a semantic no-op on re-run it is still a SCHEMA transaction —\nso N concurrent job creations issue N concurrent DDL statements on the same table and\nSurrealDB aborts the losers. Nothing to do with the run store.\n\nFixed by `query_ws_retrying`, which exists for exactly this and which the error message names.\nThe statement is idempotent, an aborted DDL rolls back whole, and a losing caller re-runs into\nthe index the winner just created.\n\n    before: FAILED on every run\n    after:  5/5 → 4 passed; 0 failed\n\n**How it was found, because the search was the expensive part.** The error surfaces from the\nRUN verb as a bare store error, which reads exactly like the same-record race a previous\nincident hardened with `write_locked`\n(`docs/debugging/flows/run-store-rev-conflict-under-concurrency.md`). Three plausible causes\nwere proposed and tested from the message alone — extending the write primitive, the\n`retain_runs` GC sweep, the undo stack''s bare `write` — and all three were wrong. The test\nfailing in 0.08s already ruled out anything periodic; that number should have been read first.\n\nWhat settled it in one line was instrumenting `From<surrealdb::Error>` to print a backtrace\nwhere the error is CONSTRUCTED. The error travels as a value, so the panic site names the test,\nnever the origin — worth reaching for immediately next time a store error surfaces far from its\nsource.\n\nAlso here: `hundred_entry_list_is_not_a_staircase` moves its ceiling from 1/3 to 1/2 of the\nserial baseline. It was measuring 0.345 locally and 0.371 on CI against a 0.333 bound — not\nnoise, but a pin calibrated for a durable store now running on `Store::memory()`, where a read\ncosts ~0.14 ms and batching wins ~2.9× rather than the ~35× the original figures assumed. The\ndiscriminator is the distance to a staircase, which measures ~1.0 by definition, so 1/2 still\nexcludes it by 2× while the implementation sits at ~0.35.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f225e89eaf9af2449977bb4e1a205cad2b446882","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/f225e89eaf9af2449977bb4e1a205cad2b446882"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/32a6626ed4e05ccc3d9958c203d50a689a8621c2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/32a6626ed4e05ccc3d9958c203d50a689a8621c2","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDMyYTY2MjZlZDRlMDVjY2MzZDk5NThjMjAzZDUwYTY4OWE4NjIxYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/6278d456a823a16ab867e551716643e61db69dde","sha":"6278d456a823a16ab867e551716643e61db69dde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/6278d456a823a16ab867e551716643e61db69dde"}],"sha":"32a6626ed4e05ccc3d9958c203d50a689a8621c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/32a6626ed4e05ccc3d9958c203d50a689a8621c2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/6278d456a823a16ab867e551716643e61db69dde/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:06:07Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T08:08:15Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"fix(tests): the result-cache race test needs the cache to itself, and asserts the PATH\n\n`an_accepting_caller_never_waits_on_a_stricter_callers_refresh` has been failing on CI and,\nlocally, 4 runs in 5 with this binary''s other 49 tests running. Two earlier repairs treated\nsymptoms; this is the cause.\n\n**The test did not own the cache it was asserting about.** It took `ENV_LOCK.read()` — a SHARED\nlock — so it ran alongside every other reader, and the result cache is a process-global static.\nA sibling test''s entries evict this one''s `current`; `fresh_enough` is then `None`; and the\naccepting caller correctly falls through to `Join`. The observable is a `Miss`, ~571 ms, and the\nrefresh''s 2 rows: the code behaving exactly to spec against a cache the test had lost control of.\n\nThat explains every earlier reading, and both of my earlier diagnoses were wrong:\n\n  - the 553 ms \"scheduling latency\" was a genuine wait — on a refresh the caller had JOINED\n    after eviction, not on an oversubscribed runtime;\n  - the `is_finished()` gate was patching a symptom of the same eviction.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`ENV_LOCK.write()`** — exclusivity for the duration. The test owns a race across a global\n   cache, so it must hold that cache alone; a shared lock never gave it that.\n\n2. **Assert the PATH, not the payload.** `cached_query` answers `Hit` from `Action::Serve`\n   (returns `current`, awaits nothing) and `Miss` from `Action::Join` (subscribes and waits), so\n   `Hit` IS \"did not join\" — decided by the branch taken, not inferred from a stopwatch or a row\n   count. The accepting call now goes through the cache layer directly with a closure that is\n   `unreachable!()`, asserting the same thing from the other side: an accepting caller must never\n   reach the query. Row count cannot carry this invariant — a completed refresh installs `current`\n   before its task reports finished, so a correct serve can legitimately return the fresh rows.\n\n    before: 4 of 5 full-binary runs FAILED\n    after:  5 of 5 → 50 passed; 0 failed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bdb2f6462f64f131e37569722bdd1a6e42f5f849","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/bdb2f6462f64f131e37569722bdd1a6e42f5f849"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/6278d456a823a16ab867e551716643e61db69dde","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/6278d456a823a16ab867e551716643e61db69dde","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDYyNzhkNDU2YTgyM2ExNmFiODY3ZTU1MTcxNjY0M2U2MWRiNjlkZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/5d9d58cf273b46100d449074d9f8a02f20998a38","sha":"5d9d58cf273b46100d449074d9f8a02f20998a38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/5d9d58cf273b46100d449074d9f8a02f20998a38"}],"sha":"6278d456a823a16ab867e551716643e61db69dde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/6278d456a823a16ab867e551716643e61db69dde"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6800775?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaiBnod/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaiBnod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaiBnod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaiBnod/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RaiBnod","id":6800775,"login":"RaiBnod","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MDA3NzU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaiBnod/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaiBnod/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaiBnod/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaiBnod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaiBnod/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaiBnod","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/5d9d58cf273b46100d449074d9f8a02f20998a38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T08:07:20Z","email":"binodrayee@gmail.com","name":"Binod"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T08:07:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ros): schedule write sends the document as the body, decodes reply leniently (#178)","tree":{"sha":"ff4deb6acb11f6028aa75cbac0804da2f0c9b88e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/ff4deb6acb11f6028aa75cbac0804da2f0c9b88e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/5d9d58cf273b46100d449074d9f8a02f20998a38","verification":{"payload":"tree ff4deb6acb11f6028aa75cbac0804da2f0c9b88e\nparent 532a04ffd48f2cb946e68ac70e05d3c5fa7347b3\nauthor Binod <binodrayee@gmail.com> 1786954040 +0545\ncommitter GitH