arse per-slot deltas\n\n* fix(ros): scope host by X-Host header, nest device/point lists\n\n* fix(ros): timeout box HTTP calls so a stall can''t wedge sidecar\n\n* feat(ros): scope writes with optional host_uuid via X-Host\n\n* fix(outbox): ts-guard marks so a newer enqueue is never lost","tree":{"sha":"f2a4118089ef7dfc20c71f0a5f9f773ad84d3765","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/f2a4118089ef7dfc20c71f0a5f9f773ad84d3765"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/c50df08859c05c11babb97862720d619c1a7734a","verification":{"payload":"tree f2a4118089ef7dfc20c71f0a5f9f773ad84d3765\nparent 0b94203544e3061f03dfd36435849f1dadc76942\nauthor Binod <binodrayee@gmail.com> 1786747848 +0545\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786747848 +1000\n\nROS write path: host scoping, sidecar hardening, outbox last-write-wins (#174)\n\n* fix(mcp): key the re-entrant dispatch guard on same-instance, not \"is nested\"\n\n* fix(ros): send priority writes as sparse per-slot deltas\n\n* fix(ros): scope host by X-Host header, nest device/point lists\n\n* fix(ros): timeout box HTTP calls so a stall can''t wedge sidecar\n\n* feat(ros): scope writes with optional host_uuid via X-Host\n\n* fix(outbox): ts-guard marks so a newer enqueue is never lost","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqf5vICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARmsQAJXesNJEVC37ZKMTjR+3z6/T\nmkCkpjT4MAz+vTeHGGq8i/L9qJD6XopVP76HHnbDEjwwXxAH6onVv4N70a1t0eSb\n9Ko1tg0E04H1Rj1xsFXbnDLDSECjmPCNziBM0rkzM9EOKHHyv2W1XSnP8U3RqJm7\n+QLARIIfM3cfZSdUV/+KSlYINFEYYYG655rwa6f7HUgaqo8rsrmj8JROw6rK9S2H\nc14JUmnwDxWR0azJQBeoHV1rEbSli7fQjzzMTN5mScRq2cA0OFQpD2Y471nzn5rY\nq2rEqAOJXe9SkbxwNvU8oiXw1qGcigEhlPpZWfxRgJ3Cf5iZ+PH1SJJzsG+21I/z\niP5OJctRS+EqMxKwdXj4v0E4NpPjo6IuW5fve7KpLY+Orn9z0wdBsicoYkboM+k4\n4uhZB/bySlUzgR3NN2v05OQh7c/lvW6LPdw6cu3pquVAzgalMgytb4nniGMxs6ww\nN7WcnT68NgbmJM1JAql38E1uwMyqrhSPZ6oEBgVcA339VAJBex/oyYGp5qVjFrhJ\nUC+emMpFr4OPTlY5m+Vgstrti02QLwPp16jO8KEWYk5iFwxZEoRu5fAiUxOEBaAY\n+F5ilgUzPtUhWn8JlsvYCe8yyu3qZt6LfBftSMyiyrVJTlhcYste6nm5jfc4b4a3\naUcyKenGz04JxcZyKoyv\n=r/y5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T22:50:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/c50df08859c05c11babb97862720d619c1a7734a","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKGM1MGRmMDg4NTljMDVjMTFiYWJiOTc4NjI3MjBkNjE5YzFhNzczNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/0b94203544e3061f03dfd36435849f1dadc76942","sha":"0b94203544e3061f03dfd36435849f1dadc76942","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/0b94203544e3061f03dfd36435849f1dadc76942"}],"sha":"c50df08859c05c11babb97862720d619c1a7734a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/c50df08859c05c11babb97862720d619c1a7734a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/0b94203544e3061f03dfd36435849f1dadc76942/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T22:38:16Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"Aidan P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T22:38:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(federation): a numeric column no longer takes its scale from row 1 (#166) (#173)\n\nThe Postgres connector builds ONE Arrow Decimal128 column per result and fixes its\nscale from the FIRST non-null row, then rescales every later row down to it — a lossy\nround. A result whose first row happens to be a whole number truncates the whole\ncolumn: `20, 17.685, 15.334` decoded as `20.0, 18.0, 15.0`, while the identical values\nreordered decoded exactly. Single-row results are always right, so the loss stayed\ninvisible until a chart or a threshold read a window whose newest sample had no\ndecimals.\n\nOnly unconstrained `numeric` is exposed — but `max()`, `min()`, `avg()` and any\narithmetic over a numeric column all return unconstrained `numeric`, which is most of\nwhat a panel or a rule selects.\n\nThe only place a scale can be chosen safely is the server, which sees every row before\nit sends any: the direct path now prepares the statement, and when the result carries a\n`numeric` (or `numeric[]`) column it re-runs it wrapped in a positional projection that\ncasts those columns to `float8`. Positional (`lb_numeric(c0, c1, …)`) with the original\nnames restored as aliases, so duplicate or unnamed columns still wrap. No loss — these\ncells become f64 on the way out to JSON regardless; what is dropped is a rounding that\ndepended on row order. Any failure in the rewrite yields the original SQL, so a broken\nquery fails exactly as before.\n\nRegression test `numeric_scale_pg_test` runs against a real Postgres, with fixtures\ndeliberately ordered WHOLE-NUMBER FIRST — ordered the other way they pass against the\nbroken code. Verified failing before the fix (`row 1 came back 18, not 17.685`) and\npassing after.\n\nAlso splits the Arrow→JSON cell conversion out of postgres.rs into pg_cells.rs\nunchanged, so the new numeric handling has somewhere to sit.\n\nUpstream root cause: datafusion-contrib/datafusion-table-providers#719.","tree":{"sha":"eeaa19db7b39be8cd281d117f15fc3c608657cb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/eeaa19db7b39be8cd281d117f15fc3c608657cb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/0b94203544e3061f03dfd36435849f1dadc76942","verification":{"payload":"tree eeaa19db7b39be8cd281d117f15fc3c608657cb0\nparent d9e037654e501ae1f5503c21dd5af8ffea1ef816\nauthor Aidan P <aidan@enviroservices.com.au> 1786747096 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786747096 +1000\n\nfix(federation): a numeric column no longer takes its scale from row 1 (#166) (#173)\n\nThe Postgres connector builds ONE Arrow Decimal128 column per result and fixes its\nscale from the FIRST non-null row, then rescales every later row down to it — a lossy\nround. A result whose first row happens to be a whole number truncates the whole\ncolumn: `20, 17.685, 15.334` decoded as `20.0, 18.0, 15.0`, while the identical values\nreordered decoded exactly. Single-row results are always right, so the loss stayed\ninvisible until a chart or a threshold read a window whose newest sample had no\ndecimals.\n\nOnly unconstrained `numeric` is exposed — but `max()`, `min()`, `avg()` and any\narithmetic over a numeric column all return unconstrained `numeric`, which is most of\nwhat a panel or a rule selects.\n\nThe only place a scale can be chosen safely is the server, which sees every row before\nit sends any: the direct path now prepares the statement, and when the result carries a\n`numeric` (or `numeric[]`) column it re-runs it wrapped in a positional projection that\ncasts those columns to `float8`. Positional (`lb_numeric(c0, c1, …)`) with the original\nnames restored as aliases, so duplicate or unnamed columns still wrap. No loss — these\ncells become f64 on the way out to JSON regardless; what is dropped is a rounding that\ndepended on row order. Any failure in the rewrite yields the original SQL, so a broken\nquery fails exactly as before.\n\nRegression test `numeric_scale_pg_test` runs against a real Postgres, with fixtures\ndeliberately ordered WHOLE-NUMBER FIRST — ordered the other way they pass against the\nbroken code. Verified failing before the fix (`row 1 came back 18, not 17.685`) and\npassing after.\n\nAlso splits the Arrow→JSON cell conversion out of postgres.rs into pg_cells.rs\nunchanged, so the new numeric handling has somewhere to sit.\n\nUpstream root cause: datafusion-contrib/datafusion-table-providers#719.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqf5jYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcpUQAKXmjzRRsivrZNJkFsuRJ/8c\nPEQdjhustrS/DUfO7CwipZCEInnlwmW0GMa87A4zutlzRZkiIj+l4VCnuV4hOR8p\n4ZnBg5Dr5u6GyW/7TgX7cJxeFRO3SH9ufPna0QmVlqPJUBkg65H/sK329xmabTnA\ntIija0v4R56lU+a2BrH0qPPdgHBih98cSKgDsW5pYkA34As1mW2yND0sHYksp2Ov\nnCF2rliAprI9LXrIcvG3XV1yDyQnCLDRrXRsBHmnO1ujteBxl191M+1VkPXJd6GM\nFd6J1cV/P7w1QtXVSygVPDZ7CrWrjAuhBkGQvPaIgULXunPmU9Giyzg60TBPSi2y\nPSyd5ti15BhIIMRRAnmJVCULyWBcfmHu+C/w5nj6iqueqoEQYaBs26vLsMCgzEWm\nVODf126WBThX4De6w12HUodEH6PRL7D78HB362Doi4Kijp5WAGFG7QBB2DMqDyw0\npR266juBqM5VQNIUAQnaqB2PeIH