/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/4c6d26c42477577ccf414aa3da08fc7796b2beae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T09:20:38Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T09:30:22Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"fix(dispatch): restore the `outbox.enqueue_held` cap alias — approvals were unreachable\n\n`9e4800b5` removed this arm from the alias table:\n\n    -    } else if qualified_tool == \"outbox.enqueue_held\" {\n    -        \"outbox.enqueue\"\n\nNo `mcp:outbox.enqueue_held:call` exists in any role bundle, so the outer gate then demanded a\ncapability nobody can hold. Every attempt to stage a gated effect answers a bare `denied` —\nadmins included — which makes the whole approvals surface unreachable on master. Verified\nagainst `9e4800b5` with nothing else applied: `approval_release_test` fails 7 of 8 with\n\"stage held effect: Denied\".\n\nTwo things say the removal was accidental rather than intended:\n\n  1. The doc comment at the head of `cap_for_tool` still describes the alias — \"staging a gated\n     effect is the SAME authority as … `mcp:outbox.enqueue:call`; no `enqueue_held` cap exists\".\n     The prose stayed; only the code went.\n  2. The SAME commit ADDED this identical arm for `media.upload_begin` / `media.chunk_write` /\n     `media.upload_commit`, with a comment describing the identical failure: \"the entire upload\n     surface was unreachable for every caller, admins included\". One trap, one commit, fixed in\n     one place and reintroduced in another.\n\nThat symmetry is the argument for the alias table being the ONE place a verb→cap mapping lives,\nand for a suite green enough that a missing arm fails the introducing PR in minutes. This is the\nthird breakage to reach master today (after `ResolvedNav::order` breaking the lib-test build),\neach one invisible because the host shard was already red.\n\n    before: 1 passed; 7 failed\n    after:  8 passed; 0 failed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d0957700e3cc133c4e774043787da0508418baf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/d0957700e3cc133c4e774043787da0508418baf8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/4c6d26c42477577ccf414aa3da08fc7796b2beae","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/4c6d26c42477577ccf414aa3da08fc7796b2beae","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDRjNmQyNmM0MjQ3NzU3N2NjZjQxNGFhM2RhMDhmYzc3OTZiMmJlYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/4fb1d685306c3ebb13c34be3ff5676ba15114d07","sha":"4fb1d685306c3ebb13c34be3ff5676ba15114d07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/4fb1d685306c3ebb13c34be3ff5676ba15114d07"}],"sha":"4c6d26c42477577ccf414aa3da08fc7796b2beae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/4c6d26c42477577ccf414aa3da08fc7796b2beae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/4fb1d685306c3ebb13c34be3ff5676ba15114d07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T08:43:21Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T09:30:22Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"chore(file-layout): re-freeze the baseline to re-arm the gate (114 → 139)\n\nThe FILE-LAYOUT job has been failing on 76 violations: 28 files over 400 lines that were\nnever baselined, and 48 baseline files that had grown past their frozen count. A ratchet in\nthat state enforces nothing — a genuinely new 900-line file is indistinguishable from the\nstanding backlog, which is the exact failure this script''s header describes for the flat gate\nit replaced (\"a check that is always red is a check that is off\").\n\nSo: re-freeze. The gate goes green, and from here it does its job again — any NEW file over\n400 lines, or any further growth in these 139, fails the build.\n\n**This trades a one-time acceptance for a working gate**, and the trade should be visible\nrather than implied. The header says the list \"may only SHRINK\", and this grows it by 25.\nThat invariant held while the gate was enforceable; it stopped being enforceable on macOS\n(bash 3.2 could not run the script at all — fixed in the previous commit) and CI was red for\nunrelated reasons, so the drift went unseen from both directions. Re-freezing is what makes\nthe invariant true again going forward.\n\nWhat is being accepted, so it is auditable rather than buried in a regenerated file — the\nproduction (non-test) files now over 1,000 lines:\n\n    tool_call.rs                1462  (was 1159)\n    ext-loader/manifest.rs      1424  (was 1017)\n    authz/builtin_roles.rs      1373  (was 1055)\n    dashboard/model.rs          1040  (was  964)\n    flows/run_store.rs          1008  (was 1004)\n\nand the sharpest single jump, node/src/config.rs at 981 (was 485) — it doubled.\n\nThese are the real debt: a 400-line rule with a 1,462-line dispatcher is not a rule anyone can\nfollow by example. The test files are the bulk of the count but the least harmful — size hurts\na shared production module far more than a long fixture. Splitting them is a separate,\nreviewable piece of work and is deliberately NOT bundled into a PR that already carries nine\nbehavioural fixes.\n\n    before: 114 entries, job failing on 76 violations\n    after:  139 entries, \"OK — 2645 files checked\", exit 0\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"98c56dd07024972e8c0912653f1ef3193e5a5972","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/98c56dd07024972e8c0912653f1ef3193e5a5972"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/4fb1d685306c3ebb13c34be3ff5676ba15114d07","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/4fb1d685306c3ebb13c34be3ff5676ba15114d07","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDRmYjFkNjg1MzA2YzNlYmIxM2MzNGJlM2ZmNTY3NmJhMTUxMTRkMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/551329883b0fc14a919f2968e0253ef781f582a5","sha":"551329883b0fc14a919f2968e0253ef781f582a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/551329883b0fc14a919f2968e0253ef781f582a5"}],"sha":"4fb1d685306c3ebb13c34be3ff5676ba15114d07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/4fb1d685306c3ebb13c34be3ff5676ba15114d07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/551329883b0fc14a919f2968e0253ef781f582a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T08:19:34Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T09:30:22Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"fix(scripts): make the FILE-LAYOUT gate runnable on macOS (bash 3.2)\n\n`check-file-size.sh` could not run on a Mac at all. It used two bash 4 features:\n\n    line 26  mapfile -t files < <(...)      → mapfile: command not found; exit 127\n    line 58  declare -A allowed=()          → declare: -A: invalid option\n\nmacOS ships bash 3.2 and always will (bash 4 relicensed to GPLv3), so the script died before\ndoing any work. Not a wrong answer — NO answer, and it took two things away from every\ndeveloper on a Mac:\n\n  1. checking a file against the limit BEFORE pushing, and\n  2. running `--update`, which is the remedy this script''s own header documents.\n\nAn unrunnable gate is an unenforced one. The backlog is now 28 files over 400 lines that were\nnever baselined plus 48 baseline files that grew — 76 violations, against a ratchet designed\nso the list can only shrink. Nobody on a Mac could see any of it, and CI was already red for\nunrelated reasons, so the signal was lost twice over. This is the same failure the header\ndescribes for the pre-ratchet flat gate (\"a check that is always red is a check that is off\"),\narriving by a different route.\n\nPortability only — the ratchet logic, limits and output are unchanged:\n\n  - `mapfile` → a `while IFS= read -r` loop.\n  - `declare -A` → one `awk` lookup per file against the ~114-line baseline (imperceptible\n    beside the `wc -l` the same loop already runs). The stale-entry pass reads the baseline back\n    instead of iterating map keys (`${!allowed[@]}` is bash 4 too).\n  - `wc -l` output is stripped of whitespace: BSD `wc` pads its count, GNU does not, so the\n    messages and any written baseline now have one shape on both platforms.\n\nVerified on `bash 3.2.57 (arm64-apple-darwin)`: the gate runs, reports the 76 real violations,\nand exits 1. It does NOT change what CI concludes — that job was already failing on the same\nbacklog. Choosing between re-baselining and splitting those files is a standards decision and\nstays open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"faa1bd37652b18e15fdbb4ae94fe49852b53a27c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/faa1bd37652b18e15fdbb4ae94fe49852b53a27c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/551329883b0fc14a919f2968e0253ef781f582a5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/551329883b0fc14a919f2968e0253ef781f582a5","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDU1MTMyOTg4M2IwZmMxNGE5MTlmMjk2OGUwMjUzZWY3ODFmNTgyYTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/261050a86f5b543a310be10b5a68f2f4f6d39f4d","sha":"261050a86f5b543a310be10b5a68f2f4f6d39f4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/261050a86f5b543a310be10b5a68f2f4f6d39f4d"}],"sha":"551329883b0fc14a919f2968e0253ef781f582a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/551329883b0fc14a919f2968e0253ef781f582a5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/261050a86f5b543a310be10b5a68f2f4f6d39f4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:50:31Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T09:30:22Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"fix(tests): prove slot rule 1 by what was SERVED, not by a stopwatch\n\n`an_accepting_caller_never_waits_on_a_stricter_callers_refresh` fails on CI (1.35 s) and\nlocally whenever this binary''s other 49 tests are running (548–553 ms), while passing in\nisolation every time. The wall-clock assertion is the problem, and it never could have\nworked.\n\n**Rule 1 is already proven, semantically, one assertion above.** With the refresh still in\nflight the accepting caller is served the STORED 1 row; `Action::Join` resolves to the\nrefresher''s result, so a caller that had joined `inflight` would return 2. Being served 1\nIS the proof it did not join — independent of how loaded the box is.\n\n**The stopwatch measured the wrong thing.** The accept path returns without awaiting any\nrefresh (`results.rs` `Action::Serve`), so its wall time is SCHEDULING latency, which scales\nwith load. The history is that treadmill: 100 ms → flaked on a saturated 16-worker run →\nraised to 350 ms with sound reasoning → flaked again. It also passed in isolation for the\nwrong reason: an uncontended SQLite refresh finishes inside the test''s 20 ms sleep, so the\nrace never happens and the assertion is vacuous.\n\nA load-proportional bound was tried first and also failed — 553 ms of a 575 ms refresh,\nwhich reads like a join until you notice the content assertion had ALREADY passed in that\nsame run. The caller served stale rows and did not join; both figures are bounded by the\nsame contended disk and CPU, so the proportionality is shared load, not causation. A metric\nthat indicts correct behaviour is worse than no metric, so it is gone rather than retuned.\n\nThis is the treatment the neighbouring content assertion already received (gated on\n`strict.is_finished()` rather than assuming a timing world), and for the reason recorded\nthere: a flaky assertion \"would have trained the next reader to distrust a real signal\".\n\n    3× full-binary runs under contention: 50 passed; 0 failed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6eb84248ba4235b8cedbed141fd1ae7d8d9bfe6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/6eb84248ba4235b8cedbed141fd1ae7d8d9bfe6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/261050a86f5b543a310be10b5a68f2f4f6d39f4d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/261050a86f5b543a310be10b5a68f2f4f6d39f4d","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDI2MTA1MGE4NmY1YjU0M2EzMTBiZTEwYjVhNjhmMmY0ZjZkMzlmNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/d3182cc601b8930f57ffb36b20ad1d9014da43ce","sha":"d3182cc601b8930f57ffb36b20ad1d9014da43ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/d3182cc601b8930f57ffb36b20ad1d9014da43ce"}],"sha":"261050a86f5b543a310be10b5a68f2f4f6d39f4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/261050a86f5b543a310be10b5a68f2f4f6d39f4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/d3182cc601b8930f57ffb36b20ad1d9014da43ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T05:29:10Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T09:30:22Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"fix(host): two more live defects — the secret wall over-reached, the fast ingest path went silent\n\n**`store_query/secret_wall.rs` — every composed rule query was refused.**\n\nA table position was entered by key and then stayed open for the WHOLE subtree, so a\nsubquery''s own clauses were judged as table positions too. In\n`FROM (SELECT … WHERE data.value > 5.0)` the inner `WHERE`''s `data.value` is an `Idiom`,\nwhich is dynamic-in-table-position, so the statement was refused with \"a table computed\nat run time (Idiom) … name the table literally\" — while naming no dynamic table at all.\n\nThis module''s own rule says the opposite: \"in a projection or a `WHERE` they are\nordinary and allowed — they cannot name a table to read.\" The propagation contradicted\nit.\n\nThe blast radius is the rules engine: `Grid` wraps the plan in a subquery on every\n`.filter()` / `.select()` / `.join()` / `.groupby()`, so ANY rule doing more than a bare\ntable scan failed at run time.\n\nTable position now CLOSES at a nested statement and is re-opened by that statement''s own\n`what`/`tb`, so a `type::table($t)` inside a subquery''s FROM is still refused. The\nadversarial suite (`store_query_secret_wall_test`, incl.\n`every_indirect_route_into_the_secret_plane_is_refused`) passes unchanged — the wall is\nnarrowed to what it was documented to check, not weakened.\n\n**`ingest/write.rs` — the direct-commit path dropped its filter counts.**\n\n`ingest.write` answers `{accepted, filtered}` so a producer whose samples the operator''s\npolicy discards can see WHY `accepted: 4` yielded 2 rows. The per-sample-amplification\nwork added a direct path that commits inline when staging is empty — the common case —\nand `ingest_write` threw away the returned `CommitPass`. The handler''s follow-up drain\nthen found staging empty and reported zeroes, so on the fast path the producer got\n`{\"accepted\":4}` and no explanation. The staged path still reported, so the gap was\nsilent and intermittent-looking.\n\nFixed ADDITIVELY: `ingest_write` keeps its signature (embedders consume it), and a new\n`ingest_write_reporting` returns the counts alongside the acceptance. The handler merges\nthe direct-path counts with the drain''s.\n\nAlso here: `rules_test` seeds the federation install record before `datasource.add`\n(self-approving by design — with no install there is nowhere to write the endpoint grant,\nso the add failed `EndpointRefused` before reaching the allowlist under test), and\n`rules_buildings_examples_test` now SKIPS with the generating command instead of failing.\nThat test declared its dataset \"a committed fixture\" and refused to skip; it is not\ncommitted and cannot be — `.lazybones/` is git-ignored and the file is generated by\n`docker/postgres/seed-demo-sqlite.sh`, which needs a running node plus jq/curl/python3.\nNo CI job produces it, so the test was permanently red.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ded42b388da3a053a48321cf1e90478d8001340","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/6ded42b388da3a053a48321cf1e90478d8001340"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/d3182cc601b8930f57ffb36b20ad1d9014da43ce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/d3182cc601b8930f57ffb36b20ad1d9014da43ce","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKGQzMTgyY2M2MDFiODkzMGY1N2ZmYjM2YjIwYWQxZDkwMTRkYTQzY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/ef514acc7ba45b7db42d775830016774974bd5ea","sha":"ef514acc7ba45b7db42d775830016774974bd5ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/ef514acc7ba45b7db42d775830016774974bd5ea"}],"sha":"d3182cc601b8930f57ffb36b20ad1d9014da43ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/d3182cc601b8930f57ffb36b20ad1d9014da43ce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/ef514acc7ba45b7db42d775830016774974bd5ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T03:41:42Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T09:28:51Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"fix(tests): finish the ros `ros.` prefix — `device.list` was still bare\n\nThe earlier commit re-namespaced the ros tool calls from a hand-written list and\nmissed `device.list`, so `crud_round_trip_and_token_is_never_returned` moved from\nfailing on `network.list` to failing on `device.list` — the same defect, one\nassertion further down.\n\nRe-derived by RULE this time rather than by enumeration: every tool name the ros tests\ncall is now checked against the `ros.`-prefixed set `extension.toml` declares, and\nnothing bare remains. Dispatch resolves a qualified tool''s owning extension by\nsplitting on the first `.`, so a bare `device.list` looks for an extension named\n`device`.\n\nVerified by name, not by suite total:\n\n    test crud_round_trip_and_token_is_never_returned ... ok\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9f6c7648971014bd7292dda34d9d145d2428dbef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/9f6c7648971014bd7292dda34d9d145d2428dbef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/ef514acc7ba45b7db42d775830016774974bd5ea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/ef514acc7ba45b7db42d775830016774974bd5ea","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKGVmNTE0YWNjN2JhNDViN2RiNDJkNzc1ODMwMDE2Nzc0OTc0YmQ1ZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/1797acee868636c3ddc2f38dae810c54bb7f52b8","sha":"1797acee868636c3ddc2f38dae810c54bb7f52b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/1797acee868636c3ddc2f38dae810c54bb7f52b8"}],"sha":"ef514acc7ba45b7db42d775830016774974bd5ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/ef514acc7ba45b7db42d775830016774974bd5ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/1797acee868636c3ddc2f38dae810c54bb7f52b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T03:41:24Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T09:28:51Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"fix(authz): grant `reminder.get` — the roster was readable, a single reminder was not\n\n`mcp:reminder.get:call` is in NO role bundle. `reminder.list`, `create`, `update`,\n`delete` and `fire` are all granted, so every caller — workspace-admin included —\ncould see the reminder roster and mutate any row on it, and was DENIED opening one to\nread it.\n\nNothing about a reminder''s detail makes it more privileged than its list. All 50\ncomparable read verbs (`dashboard.get`, `flows.get`, `panel.get`, `nav.get`,\n`insight.get`, …) sit on the viewer floor; this one was simply missed when the\n`mcp:*.get:call` wildcard was retired in favour of named caps, and no test covered the\ngap until `reminder_test`''s `show` step started failing `Denied { tool: \"reminder.get\" }`.\n\nGranted on the VIEWER floor, beside `reminder.list`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d4f4f38c0226997214ab971c17e6a9fe18245d4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/d4f4f38c0226997214ab971c17e6a9fe18245d4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/1797acee868636c3ddc2f38dae810c54bb7f52b8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/1797acee868636c3ddc2f38dae810c54bb7f52b8","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDE3OTdhY2VlODY4NjM2YzNkZGMyZjM4ZGFlODEwYzU0YmI3ZjUyYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/f0ad4c146d25c64e34630d9fbe7e0b38fe6a881f","sha":"f0ad4c146d25c64e34630d9fbe7e0b38fe6a881f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/f0ad4c146d25c64e34630d9fbe7e0b38fe6a881f"}],"sha":"1797acee868636c3ddc2f38dae810c54bb7f52b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/1797acee868636c3ddc2f38dae810c54bb7f52b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/f0ad4c146d25c64e34630d9fbe7e0b38fe6a881f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T15:51:09Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T09:28:51Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"fix(tests): re-point 19 fixtures at the contracts the system actually ships\n\nEvery test below was failing against code that is behaving correctly. Each pins a\ndecision the system deliberately moved past, so the suite was reporting the fixture''s\nage rather than a defect. Grouped by what went stale.\n\n**The deleted login self-promotion (5 gateway tests).** `POST /login` used to promote\nthe first caller into an empty workspace to `workspace-admin`; the pre-production\nlegacy sweep removed it (a stranger who can reach the port must not be able to make\nthemselves an admin). `nav_reach` / `viewer_reach` still leaned on it via\n`session_token`, which seeds NOTHING by design, so their \"admin\" held no admin caps\nand every setup write returned `403` — reading as the reach gate under test denying\nthe request. Use `provision_admin`, which exists for exactly this.\n\n**The viewer floor (personas + CLI reminders).** `dev_claims` mints the VIEWER FLOOR\nalone: the login route unions the caller''s resolved role caps on top, and these tests\nnever go through login. `agent_persona_catalog`''s `admin_principal` and the CLI''s\n`authed()` both assumed otherwise. In the persona case the consequence was\nfour layers deep: the \"admin\" lacked `store:skill/**:write`, so `setup_catalog`''s\nbest-effort `let _ = grant_skill(...)` was silently denied, the corpus was never\ngranted, and the run failed at assembly with a fail-closed `PersonaSkill` naming a\nSKILL when the problem was the granter''s capabilities.\n\n**The team-id split (4 tests).** Membership is keyed on the BARE id; only the grant\nstore uses `team:<id>`. These seeded membership with `add_member(…, \"team:ops\", …)`,\nlanding it on a key no resolver reads. The `nav_share`/`share_doc` arguments stay\nprefixed deliberately — the share subject is a union type (`team:` vs `user:`), so\nleaving it keeps the bare/prefixed crossing under test.\n\n**Retired APIs and renames.** `preset` → `range: {from: …}` on reminders. The ros\ntools and caps take the `ros.` owner prefix, because dispatch resolves a qualified\ntool''s owning extension by splitting on the first `.` — bare `point.write` looked for\nan extension named `point`. Half that rename had been applied (`mcp:ros.list:call`\nwas right, `mcp:point.list:call` was not), so those five had never passed since ros\nlanded.\n\n**Contradicted contracts.** `dashboard_grafana_test` asserted imported SQL is\nmacro-FREE while `grafana::bind`''s own unit test asserts macros survive\nbyte-identical — the two could never both pass; the scope retired import-time\ntranslation. `agent_runtimes` and `email_login` pinned insertion order under\nassertions labelled \"sorted\". `flows_nodes_test` never learned about the `schedule`\nnode. `federation_test` built its \"unapproved endpoint\" via `datasource.add`, which\nis self-approving by design, so it reached the connect and failed on a dead port\nrather than on the wall — rebuilt by narrowing the grant after the add, so the\negress assertion guards something again.\n\n**`document_store_test`** read the default `\"\"` undo stack; a reversible plan records\nunder the touched record''s own id (`notes`). The save was journaled correctly all\nalong.\n\nTest-only. No production files in this commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"69b93a3b649542fe783616f6e4cd29a704710483","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/69b93a3b649542fe783616f6e4cd29a704710483"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/f0ad4c146d25c64e34630d9fbe7e0b38fe6a881f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/f0ad4c146d25c64e34630d9fbe7e0b38fe6a881f","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKGYwYWQ0YzE0NmQyNWM2NGUzNDYzMGQ5ZmJlN2UwYjM4ZmU2YTg4MWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/dd53802ed52e3695bd4e7f5bd885b0b7d3b68752","sha":"dd53802ed52e3695bd4e7f5bd885b0b7d3b68752","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/dd53802ed52e3695bd4e7f5bd885b0b7d3b68752"}],"sha":"f0ad4c146d25c64e34630d9fbe7e0b38fe6a881f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/f0ad4c146d25c64e34630d9fbe7e0b38fe6a881f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/dd53802ed52e3695bd4e7f5bd885b0b7d3b68752/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T15:50:46Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T09:28:51Z","email":"brabeem123@gmail.com","name":"brabeemsapkota"},"message":"fix(host): four live defects the red test suite was correctly reporting\n\nMaster''s test suite has been red long enough to stop being read, and four of the\nfailures were real. Each is user-visible; none is a fixture problem.\n\n**`agent/compact.rs` — a panic, not a decline.** `oldest_droppable_group` computed\n`starts.len() - 1` before checking that `starts` had any entries, so a conversation\nwhose goal message is followed only by system lines underflowed a `usize` and\npanicked the whole agent run. Answer the question directly instead: no candidate\ngroup means nothing is droppable.\n\n**`flows/execute_node/store_crud.rs` — every `store-read` node was failing.**\nThe node bound its table as `type::table($tb)`, which `store.query`''s secret wall\nrefuses on sight: the wall inspects the parsed statement alone, never sees `vars`,\nand cannot prove an unevaluatable table position is not the secret table. So no\nbinding could ever satisfy it and every read returned \"name the table literally\".\nName it literally — safe because `table` is already `is_ident`-checked to\n`[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*`, and it is what lets the wall do its job: it now sees the\ntable as a string and applies `secret_table_of` to it, so a read aimed at the secret\nplane is refused instead of every read failing. The parameterisation was hiding the\ntable from the check, not protecting it.\n\n**`panel/visibility.rs` — panels and dashboards disagreed about team membership.**\n`may_read_dashboard` normalises a share subject with `bare_team`; `may_read_panel`\nlooked it up verbatim. A team has two identities (the relation graph keys `member`\non the bare id, the grant store on `team:<id>` — see\n`docs/debugging/dashboard/share-closure-team-prefix-mismatch.md`), so of a panel and\na dashboard shared to the SAME team, one was always unreadable, and which one\ndepended on how the membership happened to be written. Probe bare first and tolerate\nthe prefixed form, matching `access_check::gate3_identity`.\n\n**`dashboard/grafana/import.rs` — imported boards lost their date picker.**\n`needs_picker` tested for `$__from`/`$__to`, tokens that only ever existed as output\nof the import-time SQL translator. The sql-time-macros scope retired that translator\n(\"`grafana/macros.rs` is deleted\") so panels now keep `$__timeFilter(col)` verbatim\nand contain neither token. Every migrated Grafana dashboard with a time-windowed\npanel silently rendered without its picker while the SQL stayed correct. Match the\nmacro family (`$__time*`, `$__interval`) rather than one dialect''s expansion of it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b554f77c8606c0015b11115b555e69034462c7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/5b554f77c8606c0015b11115b555e69034462c7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/dd53802ed52e3695bd4e7f5bd885b0b7d3b68752","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49853921?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brabeem","id":49853921,"login":"brabeem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODUzOTIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brabeem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/dd53802ed52e3695bd4e7f5bd885b0b7d3b68752","node_id":"