https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/9a9bcd74528e16449f09370c2d49cc7a6d0a773e","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDlhOWJjZDc0NTI4ZTE2NDQ5ZjA5MzcwYzJkNDljYzdhNmQwYTc3M2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/c6d2fb58bfa08e7552a987a87e0ee3191a1ce66e","sha":"c6d2fb58bfa08e7552a987a87e0ee3191a1ce66e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/c6d2fb58bfa08e7552a987a87e0ee3191a1ce66e"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/771735e6ac593d632804f3c5ac60d772ee057dc5","sha":"771735e6ac593d632804f3c5ac60d772ee057dc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/771735e6ac593d632804f3c5ac60d772ee057dc5"}],"sha":"9a9bcd74528e16449f09370c2d49cc7a6d0a773e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/9a9bcd74528e16449f09370c2d49cc7a6d0a773e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/c6d2fb58bfa08e7552a987a87e0ee3191a1ce66e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:57:31Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"Aidan P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:57:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(rules): scheduled rules fire under the reactor''s own authority (#167) (#169)\n\nA `#[schedule(...)]` rule saved, compiled the right cron, built its managed\n`cron → rule` flow and fired dead on the minute — with the `rule` step `denied`\non every fire. A manual `rules.run` rides the caller''s token; a scheduled fire\nruns as the fixed system principal `node:reactor`, minted from `reactor_caps()`.\n\nThe deny moved as it was fixed. #168 granted `mcp:rules.eval:call` plus the\n`insight.raise`/`ack`/`resolve` trio, which left an ALERTING rule denied one\nverb deeper: `route_alerts` fans every `alert()` finding to inbox + outbox at\nthe end of a successful eval, under the same principal, and that deny fails the\nwhole `rules.eval`. Granted `mcp:inbox.record:call` + `mcp:outbox.enqueue:call`\n— named verbs, blanket `mcp:*.*:call` still refused for `ext-call`, so a\nscheduled rule calling `<ext>.<tool>` remains the run-as-owner follow-up.\n\nAlso: `rules.delete` tombstoned only the rule record and left\n`flow:{ws}:schedule:{id}` firing forever at a rule that no longer exists. It now\nruns the same `sync_schedule(.., None)` teardown a directive-less re-save runs —\none derived-state reconciler, idempotent (which also self-heals an existing\norphan), and an honest `pending` on a flow-write deny rather than a failed\ndelete.\n\nTests mint `Principal::routed(\"node:reactor\", ws, reactor_caps())` from the\nproduction function, never a copied list — the suite was green through six\nfailing live fires precisely because it drove the flow with the author''s FULL\nprincipal. Both new tests revert-checked.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d214f60a7d847045b0ea20e45b0449b8270fd544","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/d214f60a7d847045b0ea20e45b0449b8270fd544"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/c6d2fb58bfa08e7552a987a87e0ee3191a1ce66e","verification":{"payload":"tree d214f60a7d847045b0ea20e45b0449b8270fd544\nparent 428539c39722be53104b0fbf55844d80e42b31a6\nauthor Aidan P <aidan@enviroservices.com.au> 1786694251 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786694251 +1000\n\nfix(rules): scheduled rules fire under the reactor''s own authority (#167) (#169)\n\nA `#[schedule(...)]` rule saved, compiled the right cron, built its managed\n`cron → rule` flow and fired dead on the minute — with the `rule` step `denied`\non every fire. A manual `rules.run` rides the caller''s token; a scheduled fire\nruns as the fixed system principal `node:reactor`, minted from `reactor_caps()`.\n\nThe deny moved as it was fixed. #168 granted `mcp:rules.eval:call` plus the\n`insight.raise`/`ack`/`resolve` trio, which left an ALERTING rule denied one\nverb deeper: `route_alerts` fans every `alert()` finding to inbox + outbox at\nthe end of a successful eval, under the same principal, and that deny fails the\nwhole `rules.eval`. Granted `mcp:inbox.record:call` + `mcp:outbox.enqueue:call`\n— named verbs, blanket `mcp:*.*:call` still refused for `ext-call`, so a\nscheduled rule calling `<ext>.<tool>` remains the run-as-owner follow-up.\n\nAlso: `rules.delete` tombstoned only the rule record and left\n`flow:{ws}:schedule:{id}` firing forever at a rule that no longer exists. It now\nruns the same `sync_schedule(.., None)` teardown a directive-less re-save runs —\none derived-state reconciler, idempotent (which also self-heals an existing\norphan), and an honest `pending` on a flow-write deny rather than a failed\ndelete.\n\nTests mint `Principal::routed(\"node:reactor\", ws, reactor_caps())` from the\nproduction function, never a copied list — the suite was green through six\nfailing live fires precisely because it drove the flow with the author''s FULL\nprincipal. Both new tests revert-checked.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfsprCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtSQQABkqeYJH0+/iZXEmjxmFiTAs\niRwP/SXfzo02aLGzlLDCit7bIT9+Yny0d+YAib1h0nvQQsGOXsZXNP1pJcPvWfLc\n0yqUAsZ19Ob8hNVH8XcBfllz2/GEuetrxImdpfHANVySDXSPbQOkek6CYVXm+uvw\nCagcUJPh/bNnoPMfOKRWp8uG6nzKoVoIgfqHv9M/ffpQcxh+uDeE5AGotdn+jGru\nKl3F3X+HOXY64cxPlNM4817JgbJDFziPpAbcbJynLTNuUhOtHIM1o6EUlzqSp7im\nmTdtAHo/b/8avcuaKin9e0JRgJRoskPFZ3zqGK/Kn4CBPT/6U3feHKVPOn7ELOUy\nWdU3qYkahFEeGTqcQ2f5IZfQ4HzYdzXzZnCsLhe3M4+jjjkC9LsSsPij0MI7wY7I\nG23TDNta0vV9mvx370o8hfnNa4SjlxP+KoKXtqdG/AdkQVdt67tKip/YQWuEj+Po\nBJXHXYGbDw3LxELFVpn5qScs/bFyXAFKjeFK6autEsmdz3LkG37RgL1qLPxGzYJO\nPE8TbdzSODalm8lJZN/n6GEmyK+Gh731r09f/636VzfFxtn+OAHuIC5Y1eFh9LSE\nZEaJewUb7bjDye5rkUE+AJOHRCom7InIxgDPLsSar86Lxmx6Wrw3XMbTRcPzTjBq\nHbN5flqbeqIjRAwXk4DA\n=xlnA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T07:57:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/c6d2fb58bfa08e7552a987a87e0ee3191a1ce66e","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKGM2ZDJmYjU4YmZhMDhlNzU1MmE5ODdhODdlMGVlMzE5MWExY2U2NmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/428539c39722be53104b0fbf55844d80e42b31a6","sha":"428539c39722be53104b0fbf55844d80e42b31a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/428539c39722be53104b0fbf55844d80e42b31a6"}],"sha":"c6d2fb58bfa08e7552a987a87e0ee3191a1ce66e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/c6d2fb58bfa08e7552a987a87e0ee3191a1ce66e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/428539c39722be53104b0fbf55844d80e42b31a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:51:16Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"Aidan P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:51:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(store): stop the secret wall refusing composed and parameterised reads (#170)\n\nThe secret-plane wall (9fd99175) refused two ordinary shapes. Both come from\none rule in secret_wall.rs::walk — a dynamic construct in a table position is\nrefused — and two different edges of it.\n\n1. The table position never closed. It is entered by key (`what`/`tb`) and was\n   inherited for the whole subtree, so that a type::table($t) nested inside\n   FROM (…) is still caught. But a subquery is a STATEMENT: every field\n   reference in its projection/WHERE/ORDER BY serialised as an Idiom and read\n   as a runtime-computed table. That is every rules grid\n   (history(...).filter(...)) and the wrapper store_query_run itself applies\n   for the row cap. The position now ends at a nested Select — the subquery\n   re-opens it through its own `what`, so a nested or correlated secret read\n   still refuses.\n\n2. \"Cannot be proven\" was not true. store.query takes {sql, vars} and the\n   binding that chooses the table arrives in the same request; the gate was\n   never handed it. So the wall rejected the one caller doing the safest thing:\n   the store-read/write/delete flow nodes parameterise their table precisely so\n   no user text is spliced into SQL — all three have been broken for ten days.\n   A dynamic table position is now resolved against the request''s own bindings\n   (exactly FROM $tb and FROM type::table(<literal|$tb>), string bindings only)\n   and judged by name.\n\nThe wall gets stronger, not weaker: a binding that chooses the secret plane was\na generic \"cannot be proven\" rejection and is now SecretTable(\"secret\"), named,\nby the same rule that catches the literal. ensure_read_only_with_vars carries\nthe bindings; the var-less ensure_read_only stays and delegates with an empty\nslice, which can only refuse more.\n\nAlso: registered_datasource_is_in_the_rule_allowlist seeds the federation\ninstall record datasource.add appends its endpoint grant to — without it the\nadd is EndpointRefused before the allowlist under test is reached.\n\na_dynamic_table_expression_is_refused_even_when_innocent encoded the\nover-refusal as the intended contract, so it is replaced by a deliberately\nwider test. Both halves of the fix revert-checked independently, the resolution\nhalf against the four product-level store-CRUD node tests.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d41c9eced357d15a4c5a9a0d3f5c4a8afc053fd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/d41c9eced357d15a4c5a9a0d3f5c4a8afc053fd9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/428539c39722be53104b0fbf55844d80e42b31a6","verification":{"payload":"tree d41c9eced357d15a4c5a9a0d3f5c4a8afc053fd9\nparent 9e4800b52727e039ef952d8cc1c8c6b077641271\nauthor Aidan P <aidan@enviroservices.com.au> 1786693876 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786693876 +1000\n\nfix(store): stop the secret wall refusing composed and parameterised reads (#170)\n\nThe secret-plane wall (9fd99175) refused two ordinary shapes. Both come from\none rule in secret_wall.rs::walk — a dynamic construct in a table position is\nrefused — and two different edges of it.\n\n1. The table position never closed. It is entered by key (`what`/`tb`) and was\n   inherited for the whole subtree, so that a type::table($t) nested inside\n   FROM (…) is still caught. But a subquery is a STATEMENT: every field\n   reference in its projection/WHERE/ORDER BY serialised as an Idiom and read\n   as a runtime-computed table. That is every rules grid\n   (history(...).filter(...)) and the wrapper store_query_run itself applies\n   for the row cap. The position now ends at a nested Select — the subquery\n   re-opens it through its own `what`, so a nested or correlated secret read\n   still refuses.\n\n2. \"Cannot be proven\" was not true. store.query takes {sql, vars} and the\n   binding that chooses the table arrives in the same request; the gate was\n   never handed it. So the wall rejected the one caller doing the safest thing:\n   the store-read/write/delete flow nodes parameterise their table precisely so\n   no user text is spliced into SQL — all three have been broken for ten days.\n   A dynamic table position is now resolved against the request''s own bindings\n   (exactly FROM $tb and FROM type::table(<literal|$tb>), string bindings only)\n   and judged by name.\n\nThe wall gets stronger, not weaker: a binding that chooses the secret plane was\na generic \"cannot be proven\" rejection and is now SecretTable(\"secret\"), named,\nby the same rule that catches the literal. ensure_read_only_with_vars carries\nthe bindings; the var-less ensure_read_only stays and delegates with an empty\nslice, which can only refuse more.\n\nAlso: registered_datasource_is_in_the_rule_allowlist seeds the federation\ninstall record datasource.add appends its endpoint grant to — without it the\nadd is EndpointRefused before the allowlist under test is reached.\n\na_dynamic_table_expression_is_refused_even_when_innocent encoded the\nover-refusal as the intended contract, so it is replaced by a deliberately\nwider test. Both halves of the fix revert-checked independently, the resolution\nhalf against the four product-level store-CRUD node tests.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfsj0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxA4QACgkU7b6mR1dMIVB4D2zlhNX\n9lBOfnmIVtEeZhw8HXwlV7Ss5VeFWDYDZ4EjK8DPQbHmkqgXsxUhbR18vOhnLKBY\nYRluPiilI6TUDR49w+aw+saVCge6A022wLg1qhOi1u5ZGdtKQDpHGW1Ww23b/JNZ\nyr74ke2hQxsmOAQf5L1ymBxdinMcfJW0mJyJ5VbtRjulbSa3W3oFkZfmKo5edvcl\nTcy7di75qYBf5Yk/Sd3eEqJmyRSECF+XaouVju5jp8gX30Ta94lWgf776Dsx3tpp\nZmUZZRIiJEloyJ52D3TDgkT5xBo4yprqLAzzz5aap7lKPe+jUAM+HNamuBML7TK3\nZ5GcZRcPpcfSaDPQ6AemRUuC3ZsBGe3CSevBgZ/CYO0jmwRVqmEP87xl6InE8HMR\nWJain0a