:"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/3983cf11da4911a418239fa0ac5cb2382bef28e6","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDM5ODNjZjExZGE0OTExYTQxODIzOWZhMGFjNWNiMjM4MmJlZjI4ZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/ac080373427dcaf14ef6e97142b8d5b6b6ef3ae1","sha":"ac080373427dcaf14ef6e97142b8d5b6b6ef3ae1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/ac080373427dcaf14ef6e97142b8d5b6b6ef3ae1"}],"sha":"3983cf11da4911a418239fa0ac5cb2382bef28e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/3983cf11da4911a418239fa0ac5cb2382bef28e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/ac080373427dcaf14ef6e97142b8d5b6b6ef3ae1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T06:23:35Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"Aidan P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T06:23:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(packages): the shared substrate moved to NubeDev/lb-ui-kit (#157)\n\nlb''s `ui/` was retired (678503f) but `packages/*` stayed — so this repo kept\npublishing a competing copy of a substrate whose LIVE, diverged versions are\nelsewhere. Left alone, \"one substrate\" actually means three homes (lb''s, the\nkit''s, and any `file:` dep someone points at an lb checkout), and that third one\nis not hypothetical: `rubix-ai-extensions/extensions/thecrew` carries\n`\"@nube/source-picker\": \"file:../../../../lb/packages/source-picker\"` today.\n\nDeprecate-or-delete, decided per package by what lb itself still references\n(rubix-ai `docs/scope/ui/ext-ui-kit-scope.md` §11.6, risk 7; NubeIO/rubix-ai#152):\n\n- **Deleted** — `source-picker`, `insights`, `panel`, `nav-rail`. Nothing in lb''s\n  build or tests depends on any of them; they have been dormant since `ui/` went.\n  The live copies now ship from NubeDev/lb-ui-kit as `@nube/dash-kit`.\n- **Kept with a `DEPRECATED.md`** — `dashboard` and `genui`, each for a concrete\n  reason rather than caution. `@nube/dashboard` has a REAL external consumer\n  (`NubeIO/ems` pins `github:NubeDev/lb#dashboard-v0.2.2&path:/packages/dashboard`\n  in two of its UIs) and carries its own `timerange.ts`, overlapping territory the\n  kit now owns — the scope requires that relationship be STATED before Tier 2, and\n  deleting the artifact would silently decide it. `genui` IS the kit''s Tier 2,\n  which is deliberately unstarted; removing it would delete the thing the decision\n  is about.\n- **Untouched** — `ce-wiresheet`, `minimal-shell`, `thecrew`. These are lb''s own\n  demos and test beds, not shared substrate.\n\nAdds `packages/README.md` — where the substrate went, how to pin it, and an\nexplicit \"do not `file:` into an lb checkout\" so the temptation path is signposted\ndead rather than merely unused.\n\n`make build-packages` becomes a no-op with an explanatory echo. It existed solely\nto build `@nube/nav-rail`''s `dist/` for the deleted in-tree shell; kept as a\ntarget (not removed) so `build-ui`''s dependency edge and any muscle memory keep\nworking instead of failing with \"No rule to make target\".\n\nNo `node-v*` tag and no rubix-ai pin bump — nothing in the Rust node changes.\n\nVerified: `pnpm -r --filter \"./packages/*\" --filter \"!@nube/minimal-shell\" run test`\ngreen (genui 42, dashboard 32, ce-wiresheet 153), `make build-packages` clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c1b64380d5dd6834dab50fafcc96ff5c38c49677","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/c1b64380d5dd6834dab50fafcc96ff5c38c49677"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/ac080373427dcaf14ef6e97142b8d5b6b6ef3ae1","verification":{"payload":"tree c1b64380d5dd6834dab50fafcc96ff5c38c49677\nparent 90e49d42b6fe5722f4b3537b446918c875f9dbd4\nauthor Aidan P <aidan@enviroservices.com.au> 1786602215 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786602215 +1000\n\nchore(packages): the shared substrate moved to NubeDev/lb-ui-kit (#157)\n\nlb''s `ui/` was retired (678503f) but `packages/*` stayed — so this repo kept\npublishing a competing copy of a substrate whose LIVE, diverged versions are\nelsewhere. Left alone, \"one substrate\" actually means three homes (lb''s, the\nkit''s, and any `file:` dep someone points at an lb checkout), and that third one\nis not hypothetical: `rubix-ai-extensions/extensions/thecrew` carries\n`\"@nube/source-picker\": \"file:../../../../lb/packages/source-picker\"` today.\n\nDeprecate-or-delete, decided per package by what lb itself still references\n(rubix-ai `docs/scope/ui/ext-ui-kit-scope.md` §11.6, risk 7; NubeIO/rubix-ai#152):\n\n- **Deleted** — `source-picker`, `insights`, `panel`, `nav-rail`. Nothing in lb''s\n  build or tests depends on any of them; they have been dormant since `ui/` went.\n  The live copies now ship from NubeDev/lb-ui-kit as `@nube/dash-kit`.\n- **Kept with a `DEPRECATED.md`** — `dashboard` and `genui`, each for a concrete\n  reason rather than caution. `@nube/dashboard` has a REAL external consumer\n  (`NubeIO/ems` pins `github:NubeDev/lb#dashboard-v0.2.2&path:/packages/dashboard`\n  in two of its UIs) and carries its own `timerange.ts`, overlapping territory the\n  kit now owns — the scope requires that relationship be STATED before Tier 2, and\n  deleting the artifact would silently decide it. `genui` IS the kit''s Tier 2,\n  which is deliberately unstarted; removing it would delete the thing the decision\n  is about.\n- **Untouched** — `ce-wiresheet`, `minimal-shell`, `thecrew`. These are lb''s own\n  demos and test beds, not shared substrate.\n\nAdds `packages/README.md` — where the substrate went, how to pin it, and an\nexplicit \"do not `file:` into an lb checkout\" so the temptation path is signposted\ndead rather than merely unused.\n\n`make build-packages` becomes a no-op with an explanatory echo. It existed solely\nto build `@nube/nav-rail`''s `dist/` for the deleted in-tree shell; kept as a\ntarget (not removed) so `build-ui`''s dependency edge and any muscle memory keep\nworking instead of failing with \"No rule to make target\".\n\nNo `node-v*` tag and no rubix-ai pin bump — nothing in the Rust node changes.\n\nVerified: `pnpm -r --filter \"./packages/*\" --filter \"!@nube/minimal-shell\" run test`\ngreen (genui 42, dashboard 32, ce-wiresheet 153), `make build-packages` clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfWLnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQv8QAAgiJRd1pUa+XHR9MLtSYIoC\ngpKdkWvFusrnVDwG0d5Byw5ISc+OXzWdzJn3ZE8JxZULEHclNR5NTZpMDevLVCBl\nSazgvkJANtsLgEufyiFRE7fmBtOLSObVzER2g3/Wl0BHtWhgMLAlfUPtSEsZkvsK\nq+u1E88MGcekWpp+q05pR/qbWnj6Nkv6nHc45WOIH+FTKHqC63rmkNr9W38Kh+zq\naFvuCHv60EOZDEVyrP21xa9yYjA1lc4H31Tazov6NHBa8Hpm30NpdWICYOQE7apl\n74KI2HJAZVvNkcKXPKPmoHHiQzWytBM1X4GvxpAuR/0c3Vnwcx2i1OOFnZ8wNz3Z\n+oFDVIj95jypvMwSgS+hL+dDcTe/9YSzGScOyPeE8ZwcmejP2ay0tuHvk9JDciUQ\n13pqhpfGNP5PHbA5qT/rsK2ylK9f3PgybtEo2ZfaSOZwrClABKZV13HFRbQqZlEb\nkreYJ40I6hsSzDXinR7qGXTujJEu5taBl3qTFnKGd6WLA2zd1gvuP3lVfcYPDbWP\nYFL9CoMfJxETYnqBw6aYPxdufIskTU4b0JCjLKxfNWxEEnrj7x7W6h8zGAneMQnM\n5jdXe1tmIUv+H+ThsPNwCE/+Bzr1YjXBr7k64Z0AxPOJCsB43d8Tum+xdRGD5UIv\nUwKOD8kAgbsRM0pMeJXW\n=4UpX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T06:24:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/ac080373427dcaf14ef6e97142b8d5b6b6ef3ae1","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKGFjMDgwMzczNDI3ZGNhZjE0ZWY2ZTk3MTQyYjhkNWI2YjZlZjNhZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/90e49d42b6fe5722f4b3537b446918c875f9dbd4","sha":"90e49d42b6fe5722f4b3537b446918c875f9dbd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/90e49d42b6fe5722f4b3537b446918c875f9dbd4"}],"sha":"ac080373427dcaf14ef6e97142b8d5b6b6ef3ae1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/ac080373427dcaf14ef6e97142b8d5b6b6ef3ae1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/90e49d42b6fe5722f4b3537b446918c875f9dbd4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T05:43:51Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"Aidan P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T05:43:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ext): narrow a `[ui] scope` by the cap that GATES a verb, not its namesake (#158)\n\n* fix(ext): narrow a [ui] scope by the cap that GATES a verb, not its namesake\n\n`ui_decl::narrow_scope` kept a declared `[ui] scope` entry only if\n`mcp:<tool>:call` was in the install''s granted caps. But several shipped verbs\nare deliberately ALIASED onto an existing grant, because they are a fan-in of the\nsame authorized read rather than a new privilege:\n\n    viz.query_batch      → mcp:viz.query:call\n    series.latest_many   → mcp:series.latest:call\n    series.rollup.read   → mcp:series.read:call\n    federation.schema/sample/profile_get → mcp:federation.query:call\n\nNo `mcp:viz.query_batch:call` exists in any role bundle, so it can never be\ngranted — and the namesake-only intersection therefore dropped every such verb\nfrom the served scope of EVERY install.\n\nThat is not cosmetic. The shell''s extension bridge builds its allow-set from\nexactly this list (`makeBridge(ui.scope)` → `allowed.has(tool)`), so the page''s\nown bridge refused the call `out_of_scope` BEFORE it reached the gate that would\nhave allowed it. The failure is silent: panels render empty, nothing errors, and\nthe manifest looks correct. It is the \"shipped but unusable\" state the aliases\nwere added to prevent, reappearing one layer up.\n\nThe fix asks the same question the runtime gate asks — WHICH capability gates\nthis verb? — through the existing `gate_tool_for`, which is already the one place\nthat mapping lives. Nothing is widened: a surviving verb rides a capability the\nadmin already approved, and the host re-checks that same capability on every\ncall. `drops_an_aliased_verb_whose_gating_cap_is_not_granted` pins that the\nnarrowing stays \"is the real gate granted?\", never \"is anything related granted?\".\n\nFound by the acceptance run for `@nube/dash-kit` (NubeIO/rubix-ai#152 §9) — a\nreal extension published to a real node, whose granted scope came back missing\n`viz.query_batch`. No headless suite could have caught it: every layer''s own\ntests pass in isolation.\n\nVerified on that node: with this change the served scope is\n`[viz.query, viz.query_batch, series.read, series.latest, series.find, …]` and a\nreal 4-panel `viz.query_batch` returns 4 results of 60 points each.\n`cargo test -p lb-host --lib ui_decl` — 8 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: split ui_decl''s tests into a sibling file (FILE-LAYOUT ≤400)\n\nThe two regression tests took `ui_decl.rs` from 311 to 404 lines, one over lb''s\nhard 400-line cap — a NEW violation on top of master''s existing backlog, and mine\nto fix rather than add to.\n\nThe tests move to `ui_decl_tests.rs`, included with `#[cfg(test)] #[path = …]` so\nthey remain a child module of `ui_decl` and keep reaching its `pub(crate) project`.\nSame split the host''s own test suites already use.\n\n`ui_decl.rs` is now 128 lines. Verified against master: 70 file-size violations on\nboth branches — this branch adds none.\n\n`cargo test -p lb-host --lib` — 446 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style: rustfmt the extracted ui_decl tests\n\nThe split moved the test bodies out of a `mod tests { … }` block, so they kept\none level of indentation they no longer need. `cargo fmt --all --check` clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3737b6b88d59d3078b74fb3df5e2fa71ea978158","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/3737b6b88d59d3078b74fb3df5e2fa71ea978158"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/90e49d42b6fe5722f4b3537b446918c875f9dbd4","verification":{"payload":"tree 3737b6b88d59d3078b74fb3df5e2fa71ea978158\nparent 0c936cc11fabb3ccf48fb4fec20d026bdec67033\nauthor Aidan P <aidan@enviroservices.com.au> 1786599831 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786599831 +0700\n\nfix(ext): narrow a `[ui] scope` by the cap that GATES a verb, not its namesake (#158)\n\n* fix(ext): narrow a [ui] scope by the cap that GATES a verb, not its namesake\n\n`ui_decl::narrow_scope` kept a declared `[ui] scope` entry only if\n`mcp:<tool>:call` was in the install''s granted caps. But several shipped verbs\nare deliberately ALIASED onto an existing grant, because they are a fan-in of the\nsame authorized read rather than a new privilege:\n\n    viz.query_batch      → mcp:viz.query:call\n    series.latest_many   → mcp:series.latest:call\n    series.rollup.read   → mcp:series.read:call\n    federation.schema/sample/profile_get → mcp:federation.query:call\n\nNo `mcp:viz.query_batch:call` exists in any role bundle, so it can never be\ngranted — and the namesake-only intersection therefore dropped every such verb\nfrom the served scope of EVERY install.\n\nThat is not cosmetic. The shell''s extension bridge builds its allow-set from\nexactly this list (`makeBridge(ui.scope)` → `allowed.has(tool)`), so the page''s\nown bridge refused the call `out_of_scope` BEFORE it reached the gate that would\nhave allowed it. The failure is silent: panels render empty, nothing errors, and\nthe manifest looks correct. It is the \"shipped but unusable\" state the aliases\nwere added to prevent, reappearing one layer up.\n\nThe fix asks the same question the runtime gate asks — WHICH capability gates\nthis verb? — through the existing `gate_tool_for`, which is already the one place\nthat mapping lives. Nothing is widened: a surviving verb rides a capability the\nadmin already approved, and the host re-checks that same capability on every\ncall. `drops_an_aliased_verb_whose_gating_cap_is_not_granted` pins that the\nnarrowing stays \"is the real gate granted?\", never \"is anything related granted?\".\n\nFound by the acceptance run for `@nube/dash-kit` (NubeIO/rubix-ai#152 §9) — a\nreal extension published to a real node, whose granted scope came back missing\n`viz.query_batch`. No headless suite could have caught it: every layer''s own\ntests pass in isolation.\n\nVerified on that node: with this change the served scope is\n`[viz.query, viz.query_batch, series.read, series.latest, series.find, …]` and a\nreal 4-panel `viz.query_batch` returns 4 results of 60 points each.\n`cargo test -p lb-host --lib ui_decl` — 8 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: split ui_decl''s tests into a sibling file (FILE-LAYOUT ≤400)\n\nThe two regression tests took `ui_decl.rs` from 311 to 404 lines, one over lb''s\nhard 400-line cap — a NEW violation on top of master''s existing backlog, and mine\nto fix rather than add to.\n\nThe tests move to `ui_decl_tests.rs`, included with `#[cfg(test)] #[path = …]` so\nthey remain a child module of `ui_decl` and keep reaching its `pub(crate) project`.\nSame split the host''s own test suites already use.\n\n`ui_decl.rs` is now 128 lines. Verified against master: 70 file-size violations on\nboth branches — this branch adds none.\n\n`cargo test -p lb-host --lib` — 446 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style: rustfmt the extracted ui_decl tests\n\nThe split moved the test bodies out of a `mod tests { … }` block, so they kept\none level of indentation they no longer need. `cargo fmt --all --check` clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfVmXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAN90QAFxx4q/oNBItXkvfrEZH1eEH\nSsiOvuGyBLPbeMOGtjJUbkSLK1vZzLN9GOo+uFjNHGIw0UlXx9hoIO0khglxYOm2\nNTNmzBkAWRER59cGm6loe/E46UkBE8GzrtD822zmeCdpm/9ExyZ5hs2IeBqQinoT\nks38xuTtwQ3EKOStdvFVvTeim1wnKLZuQqTQdvCv6rIC/jejpOXtk6gTAeZBUM/7\nGaoHbjqgHZy8XTpQkGuAnBAHlYRwGyYqHvTNAQ0xBmw+1pzFjSIVFElpy7ER+xVD\nkETKmZQ7EUzsf6rH04u+4Z6yC3a68OyIK6sLoBHYJgy9xE55DL8kzwyRKndqYD58\nThiwJmYUKui9je9UPlLiLcQDkynJ6UccJkG0ouP0WvTpCrFlEzBOrynF5Bcf5lBj\nS4V0wBKQE+MLNJ9T9Fkm52DH2biU5jZafeCRHHFyX/xEJugJALAGp6fSxOEob8/+\nynzP7Apw5zFRQkb+qB3afUbvDyH1GcGiQ8toVjl4YZnwg