"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/b1c365e7b357787722dfb937d9829adbddbc7bb0","sha":"b1c365e7b357787722dfb937d9829adbddbc7bb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/b1c365e7b357787722dfb937d9829adbddbc7bb0"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/6ff1bc076976123f48802600493d559a6c375984","sha":"6ff1bc076976123f48802600493d559a6c375984","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/6ff1bc076976123f48802600493d559a6c375984"}],"sha":"0c936cc11fabb3ccf48fb4fec20d026bdec67033","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/0c936cc11fabb3ccf48fb4fec20d026bdec67033"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/6ff1bc076976123f48802600493d559a6c375984/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T01:25:01Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T01:25:01Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"message":"perf(ingest,store): cut per-sample log amplification 3x→1; instrument and shorten the compaction pause\n\nDriven by a live RC-6 incident (armv7, 959 MB RAM, 2026-08-08): every hourly\nbudget-driven `store.compact` pass held the store''s write guard for ~94 s, every\n`ingest.write` blocked past the modbus extension''s 5 s push budget, and ~90 s of\n`must-deliver` meter samples were dropped per network per pass.\n\nLever 1 — direct commit (the amplification half):\n\n  `lb_ingest::commit_direct` commits a caller''s live batch straight to the series\n  plane, and the host caller path picks it iff staging is EMPTY. Three commit-log\n  record writes per sample (staging UPSERT, series UPSERT, staging DELETE\n  tombstone) become one. On an append-only engine the log is also the node''s RSS\n  high-water mark and the input to the compaction pass, so this stretches the\n  pass interval, the pass duration and the memory plateau together.\n\n  The decision lives in the host, not in `lb_ingest::write`: `write` stays the\n  staging primitive the durable-redrain crash tests are built on, and the single\n  seam that pairs write-with-drain chooses between the two primitives — covering\n  the MCP verb, the gateway route, the webhook and the federation mirror without\n  four call sites drifting. One commit engine (`commit_staged` + a `Dequeue`\n  flag) serves both paths, so exactly-once stays a single fact. The direct path\n  chunks at `DIRECT_COMMIT_BATCH` (256, matching the drain): `commit_staged`\n  builds a statement per sample, so an unchunked direct commit would put an\n  unbounded transaction on a request path.\n\n  Emptiness is the exact gate: a non-empty staging means a backlog or a\n  concurrent producer sitting ahead of this batch, so everything staging exists\n  for — bursts, offline re-appends, crash recovery — is untouched by\n  construction.\n\nLever 2 — snapshot / segment-incremental compaction: REJECTED, not deferred.\n\n  Read out of the pinned surrealkv 0.9.3: the active segment is appended in\n  place (a hard-linked snapshot keeps growing under the compactor), there is no\n  delta-replay path and segment headers validate their id (renumbering is a\n  fork, not an integration), and the `CompactedUpToSegment` watermark is\n  hardcoded to \"everything before the rotate\". The scope doc records the finding\n  with citations so it is not re-litigated.\n\nWhat shipped for the pause instead:\n\n  - `CompactionPhases` (quiesce_ms/open_ms/compact_ms/merge_ms) on every\n    `CompactionRecord`, returned by `store.compact` and persisted beside the\n    store. The 94 s splits between a full replay of the uncompacted log and a\n    scattered pread-per-value pass, and which dominates is a property of how\n    much of a node''s log is live — measurable, not arguable.\n  - A real 256 MiB value cache on the compaction-only handle. The stock\n    `max_value_cache_size` is 100_000 BYTES (surrealkv weighs it by byte), i.e.\n    a no-op in front of compaction''s per-value reads. Runtime-only, so\n    surrealdb''s own handle is unaffected.\n  - Overlapped quiesce detection. The fd-release fast path and the (size, mtime)\n    stability fallback are independent proofs and both are pure reads, but they\n    ran in series — so every real node, which never reaches fd-zero thanks to the\n    surrealdb index-builder leak, waited out the full 5 s fast-path window before\n    the 2 s stability clock could start. ~5 s off the write-guard hold per pass.\n\nGoal 1 (\"no pass blocks writers longer than a producer''s push budget\") is NOT\nmet and the scope doc says so: it is unreachable at this engine version by\nshrinking the pass. The route is vendoring surrealkv to reorder `Core::new` and\nexpose `rotate()`/`compact_up_to`.\n\nTests: `ingest_write_amplification_test` (4, real nodes, no mocks) pins the\nthree staged record writes against the direct path''s one, the backlog gate, and\nexactly-once across chunk boundaries. Assertions are STRUCTURAL on purpose — the\ncommit log cannot be metered in-process (surrealkv flushes asynchronously and\nthe index-builder leak means the handle is never fully shut down), so the same\n2400-sample run measured 667,665 B and 1,647,313 B minutes apart.\n\n`CompactionRecord` moved to its own file to stay under the 400-line\nFILE-LAYOUT limit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"26ab4005e949061867633091f1fe2b1fb7bc6a6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/26ab4005e949061867633091f1fe2b1fb7bc6a6f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/6ff1bc076976123f48802600493d559a6c375984","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/6ff1bc076976123f48802600493d559a6c375984","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDZmZjFiYzA3Njk3NjEyM2Y0ODgwMjYwMDQ5M2Q1NTlhNmMzNzU5ODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/b1c365e7b357787722dfb937d9829adbddbc7bb0","sha":"b1c365e7b357787722dfb937d9829adbddbc7bb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/b1c365e7b357787722dfb9