","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/301cb9119c7e738185bdf18d674439314288f765","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKDMwMWNiOTExOWM3ZTczODE4NWJkZjE4ZDY3NDQzOTMxNDI4OGY3NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/86d8fe3a16f81ef775ea7c0a1b12662c9751ef3a","sha":"86d8fe3a16f81ef775ea7c0a1b12662c9751ef3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/86d8fe3a16f81ef775ea7c0a1b12662c9751ef3a"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/ba2db416046f3f94ee3b4e75cbcc10d61b278e0b","sha":"ba2db416046f3f94ee3b4e75cbcc10d61b278e0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/ba2db416046f3f94ee3b4e75cbcc10d61b278e0b"}],"sha":"301cb9119c7e738185bdf18d674439314288f765","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/301cb9119c7e738185bdf18d674439314288f765"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/ba2db416046f3f94ee3b4e75cbcc10d61b278e0b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:41:17Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:41:17Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"message":"chore(prefs): default date_style to EU and refresh the prefs skill docs\n\nNot my change — committed on the author''s behalf alongside the ingest\ntime-order fix so the working tree is clean. The built-in fallback for\n`date_style` moves Iso -> Eu (`DD/MM/YYYY`, the metric-region seed),\nwith the language axis and the prefs skill doc updated to match.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d04db31533b31f185a10bd1c724e7190daa7e48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/trees/1d04db31533b31f185a10bd1c724e7190daa7e48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/git/commits/ba2db416046f3f94ee3b4e75cbcc10d61b278e0b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/ba2db416046f3f94ee3b4e75cbcc10d61b278e0b","node_id":"C_kwDOTFiyodoAKGJhMmRiNDE2MDQ2ZjNmOTRlZTNiNGU3NWNiY2MxMGQ2MWIyNzhlMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/lb/commit/c27669dad85ce365d2e570eb9e444afdb424597b","sha":"c27669dad85ce365d2e570eb9e444afdb424597b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/c27669dad85ce365d2e570eb9e444afdb424597b"}],"sha":"ba2db416046f3f94ee3b4e75cbcc10d61b278e0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/ba2db416046f3f94ee3b4e75cbcc10d61b278e0b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/lb/commits/c27669dad85ce365d2e570eb9e444afdb424597b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:40:34Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:40:34Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"message":"fix(ingest): page series.read in TIME order across a producer restart\n\n`seq` is assigned PER PRODUCER GENERATION and restarts at 0 when an\nextension restarts, so `ORDER BY seq, producer` is not time order: the\nprevious generation''s high-`seq` rows sort ABOVE the newer generation''s\nlow-`seq` rows even though they are older.\n\nThree user-visible symptoms fell out of that one clause:\n\n  1. A `direction:\"back\"` page filled with the STALE generation, so a\n     chart drew a line that jumped backwards in time at the seam.\n  2. Every window wider than the newest generation returned the SAME\n     rows — the range picker moved the URL and nothing changed. \"This\n     week\", \"last week\" and most presets were dead.\n  3. The newest sample was not the newest row, so a `limit:1` stat tile\n     could serve a stale value.\n\nMeasured live on a rubix-ai dev node: 40/40 demo series returned\nunsorted rows, each with exactly one ascending break, always at the\ngeneration seam.\n\nThe page now orders by `(ts, seq, producer)` — `ts` is the only\ncomponent monotonic across a restart; `seq`/`producer` stay as\ntiebreakers so the sort key remains unique (two samples may share a\nmillisecond, two producers may share a `seq`). The keyset cursor carries\n`ts` as `v2:<ts>:<seq>:<producer>` and the cursor comparison was widened\nto the same lexicographic key — it must match the ORDER BY or the seek\nskips or repeats rows at a page boundary. A `v1:` cursor still decodes,\nso an in-flight page chain survives the upgrade.\n\nNo performance cost: `series_ts_idx` on `(series, ts)` already exists,\nso the page stays O(page) rather than degrading to an OFFSET scan.\n\nThe `latest` pointer and the retention cap had already been fixed for\nthis same hazard; paging was the last reader on the `seq` key, and a\nrestart is required to reproduce, so the suite stayed green.\n\nAdds `a_producer_restart_that_resets_seq_still_pages_in_time_order` — a\nverified foil: reverting the ORDER BY fails it with the stale generation\nleading the page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"937829f3da30d649cd0c9f0e4e2eddf909a712b7","url":"https://api