mmit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-22T01:48:52Z","email":"colinvaughn01@gmail.com","name":"Colin Vaughn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-22T01:48:52Z","email":"colinvaughn01@gmail.com","name":"Colin Vaughn"},"message":"chore(release): v0.3.6\n\nRound-3 agent-feedback fixes on a11ycore.\n\nFixed: relative imports differing only by their ./ vs ../ prefix collapsed\ninto one phantom module stub (make_id trims leading dots), so the cross-file\nresolver could rebind only one importer and stranded the rest as unresolved\nnodes -- a unit test in __tests__/ importing ../foo was never linked to foo.ts,\nhiding the direct test from affected_tests/predict_impact. Module stubs now\nfold the relative-climb depth into their id.\n\nChanged: predict_edit gains limit/verbose + a per-section by-depth rollup\n(was uncapped); working_changes_impact gains an opt-in code_only filter; the\nserver initialize instructions now explain that speculate is enabled via\nserve --allow-exec.","tree":{"sha":"eb2519fe03889bbd8c604af4c7017fe6df3a2ecb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/git/trees/eb2519fe03889bbd8c604af4c7017fe6df3a2ecb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/git/commits/d31ab557c991bd24db401033a57d5344a1f769fb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62533138?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinVaughn","id":62533138,"login":"ColinVaughn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNTMzMTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/commit/d31ab557c991bd24db401033a57d5344a1f769fb","node_id":"C_kwDOTGqYB9oAKGQzMWFiNTU3Yzk5MWJkMjRkYjQwMTAzM2E1N2Q1MzQ0YTFmNzY5ZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/commit/799995a4a0bd0b825c896dde80101aacc9d42def","sha":"799995a4a0bd0b825c896dde80101aacc9d42def","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/commits/799995a4a0bd0b825c896dde80101aacc9d42def"}],"sha":"d31ab557c991bd24db401033a57d5344a1f769fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/commits/d31ab557c991bd24db401033a57d5344a1f769fb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62533138?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinVaughn","id":62533138,"login":"ColinVaughn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNTMzMTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/commits/799995a4a0bd0b825c896dde80101aacc9d42def/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-21T23:47:19Z","email":"colinvaughn01@gmail.com","name":"Colin Vaughn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-21T23:47:19Z","email":"colinvaughn01@gmail.com","name":"Colin Vaughn"},"message":"chore(release): v0.3.5\n\nDiscoverability follow-up to 0.3.4: surface the new functionality where an agent\nactually reads it (MCP tool schemas, server initialize instructions, the generated\nskill, and CLI --help), not just the wiki. No behavior change.\n\n- Document the name@file qualifier on every name-taking tool (get_node, get_source,\n  get_neighbors, describe_node, shortest_path, affected, find_callers, find_callees)\n  in the MCP param schemas, the server instructions, the generated skill, and the\n  explain/path/affected CLI help -- previously only predict_edit advertised it.\n- Add test_count to the god_nodes outputSchema; note in the skill that 0 test(s)\n  flags an untested hub.\n- get_neighbors documents the empty-relation_filter hint; audit_sql documents the\n  severity-then-confidence ranking.\n- Add a guard test that fails if a name-taking tool''s schema drops the @file hint\n  or god_nodes loses test_count.\n- Fix the wiki Seed-resolution section: it documented a pre-unification resolver\n  and the old \"No unique node match\" message; now describes the shared cascade,\n  the @file qualifier, and the candidate list.\n- Re-bless the 7 generated skill snapshots.","tree":{"sha":"f8558d7719c1755cb8fc59ae41a8e719b2f31105","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/git/trees/f8558d7719c1755cb8fc59ae41a8e719b2f31105"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/git/commits/799995a4a0bd0b825c896dde80101aacc9d42def","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.github