: opt-in in-place update from GitHub releases (+ checksums)\n- serve: auto-freshen the graph for files written mid-session","tree":{"sha":"1d4d8732b69fc60a20dab6ec567cc7f012f4b79f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/git/trees/1d4d8732b69fc60a20dab6ec567cc7f012f4b79f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/git/commits/79e0b75ea9b31bed8b84ba0cbcb287b7524431fc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62533138?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinVaughn","id":62533138,"login":"ColinVaughn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNTMzMTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/commit/79e0b75ea9b31bed8b84ba0cbcb287b7524431fc","node_id":"C_kwDOTGqYB9oAKDc5ZTBiNzVlYTliMzFiZWQ4Yjg0YmEwY2JjYjI4N2I3NTI0NDMxZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/commit/19fd3d145bb6924e4924618dc050f06e11ad4a47","sha":"19fd3d145bb6924e4924618dc050f06e11ad4a47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/commits/19fd3d145bb6924e4924618dc050f06e11ad4a47"}],"sha":"79e0b75ea9b31bed8b84ba0cbcb287b7524431fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/commits/79e0b75ea9b31bed8b84ba0cbcb287b7524431fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62533138?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinVaughn","id":62533138,"login":"ColinVaughn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNTMzMTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/commits/19fd3d145bb6924e4924618dc050f06e11ad4a47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-21T19:08:05Z","email":"Colinvaughn01@gmail.com","name":"Colin Vaughn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-21T19:08:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/serve auto freshen (#8)\n\n* feat(serve): auto-freshen graph for live-coded files\n\nDetect files added/changed/removed since the last extraction and run an\nincremental rebuild before answering a query, so files an agent writes\nmid-session are queryable without a separate watch/update.\n\n- synaptic-incremental: new `freshen` module (build-provenance manifest +\n  on-disk change detection via the mtime fastpath); `rebuild_with_detect`\n  reuses one scan so the serve catch-up walks the tree once.\n- serve: debounced on-query staleness gate (`needs_freshen`) + synchronous\n  incremental catch-up (`apply_freshen`) under the rebuild lock, on both the\n  stdio and HTTP transports. Opt-out via SYNAPTIC_SERVE_AUTOFRESH; tunable\n  debounce (SYNAPTIC_SERVE_AUTOFRESH_DEBOUNCE_MS) and cap\n  (SYNAPTIC_SERVE_AUTOFRESH_MAX_FILES).\n- rebuild: allow a bounded shrink on incremental rebuilds so symbol removals\n  (e.g. deleting a method) propagate; the strict shrink guard is kept for\n  full rebuilds.\n- extract/update persist the provenance manifest (reusing their existing scan).\n\n* style: apply rustfmt to auto-freshen tests\n\nWrap long assert!/call_tool lines per rustfmt so `cargo fmt --all --check`\n(the lint CI job) passes. No behavior change.\n\n* docs(readme): lead with monorepo + federated multi-repo scale\n\nSurface cross-repo federation as a top-of-README selling point: the same\nworkflow scales from a single small folder to a large monorepo or a fleet of\nseparate repositories federated into one graph with real cross-repo edges.\n\n* feat(update): synaptic-upgrade crate backing self-update\n\n* feat(update): self-update CLI command + opt-in background notice\n\n* docs(update): document self-update; publish release checksums\n\n* style: cargo fmt for self-update\n\n* docs(wiki): document the self-update system\n\n* ci(release): sync wiki/ to the GitHub wiki on release\n\n* docs(update): escape angle brackets in verify_sha256 doc comment\n\nFixes the docs CI job: rustdoc parsed `<hex>`/`<filename>` as HTML tags\nunder RUSTDOCFLAGS=-D warnings.","tree":{"sha":"f8691f8a9c014a9103661646fb17ff25d44b54e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/git/trees/f8691f8a9c014a9103661646fb17ff25d44b54e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/git/commits/19fd3d145bb6924e4924618dc050f06e11ad4a47","verification":{"payload":"tree f8691f8a9c014a9103661646fb17ff25d44b54e2\nparent f3a382aa7b08eee7d5988f89295df2cb62b31df3\nauthor Colin Vaughn <Colinvaughn01@gmail.com> 1782068885 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782068885 -0400\n\nFeat/serve auto freshen (#8)\n\n* feat(serve): auto-freshen graph for live-coded files\n\nDetect files added/changed/removed since the last extraction and run an\nincremental rebuild before answering a query, so files an agent writes\nmid-session are queryable without a separate watch/update.\n\n- synaptic-incremental: new `freshen` module (build-provenance manifest +\n  on-disk change detection via the mtime fastpath); `rebuild_with_detect`\n  reuses one scan so the serve catch-up walks the tree once.\n- serve: debounced on-query staleness gate (`needs_freshen`) + synchronous\n  incremental catch-up (`apply_freshen`) under the rebuild lock, on both the\n  stdio and HTTP transports. Opt-out via SYNAPTIC_SERVE_AUTOFRESH; tunable\n  debounce (SYNAPTIC_SERVE_AUTOFRESH_DEBOUNCE_MS) and cap\n  (SYNAPTIC_SERVE_AUTOFRESH_MAX_FILES).\n- rebuild: allow a bounded shrink on incremental rebuilds so symbol removals\n  (e.g. deleting a method) propagate; the strict shrink guard is kept for\n  full rebuilds.\n- extract/update persist the provenance manifest (reusing their existing scan).\n\n* style: apply rustfmt to auto-freshen tests\n\nWrap long assert!/call_tool lines per rustfmt so `cargo fmt --all --check`\n(the lint CI job) passes. No behavior change.\n\n* docs(readme): lead with monorepo + federated multi-repo scale\n\nSurface cross-repo federation as a top-of-README selling point: the same\nworkflow scales from a single small folder to a large monorepo or a fleet of\nseparate repositories federated into one graph with real cross-repo edges.\n\n* feat(update): synaptic-upgrade crate backing self-update\n\n* feat(update): self-update CLI command + opt-in background notice\n\n* docs(update): document self-update; publish release checksums\n\n* style: cargo fmt for self-update\n\n* docs(wiki): document the self-update system\n\n* ci(release): sync wiki/ to the GitHub wiki on release\n\n* docs(update): escape angle brackets in verify_sha256 doc comment\n\nFixes the docs CI job: rustdoc parsed `<hex>`/`<filename>` as HTML tags\nunder RUSTDOCFLAGS=-D warnings.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqODaVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbz8QACeH2xxxGRYvgX7mARahs5Xh\n+vdj3gug7oFVoms6QvE7RugSzPIlQUfG4O/7HzLAp8l4tdb4yFN5zhJ3vAoX3q8h\nMo51v3luJA5MzQtxh67uhvDHnuVV6XGTmbUGlerbeNftUOrv56WQ495/eCZAUod8\nhbsFhogzWypbaunoN4PqhFMFJ6oAD2sGlS9Vn0QW79UtLgGdK41tZEF3GlWz0F9M\n3LDbcayWAjsPVX71PA5qiv8oOhZlPSIT82YXcUk10L9GctjB+38ai+/DAcnsn0Yj\niJiwfyi+iNZP/7DGZvniiWtm42ak60oNCpOXzofrKK3nvZy6p+wzfw6woDNFtBoZ\nmCFKZ0R9UCqB6UcE+KUFVXML/fSv+4dBfvtAO9FdMobwRqMoNVExjqGloMGhZzxN\nQi3Gp4gXt6lK+fYwIng4AJujg4yU+jdSWwNkdIx2kMJ6Rt63IdoZS4kRisvanWx2\n1pLTmcVfG+QHbyZ83aqbADiMfsrbSNOp2lPEnsSZBgHd8tMinShJNitFqFIy0ESy\nX6Cr3yHDoLc9lXXLzPTbUGrQTMSzUHVJfA5l5VT9epjHZpF3lB4NxR6lLywNEWXc\nP6aDT64KGy/yVQ+/aM4VKOfXQCeA39pBnamn4eQgkNcZqJ3TkqeSaHSXF1uMuzM8\nCe0WvMkTq875bY2KHb58\n=vt4A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-27T09:02:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/we