ughn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinVaughn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/commits/adf02a53cd220557fa8129c57e1ba108f0231baf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T14:47:39Z","email":"colinvaughn01@gmail.com","name":"Colin Vaughn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T14:47:39Z","email":"colinvaughn01@gmail.com","name":"Colin Vaughn"},"message":"Release 0.2.7: MCP-Protocol-Version 400, tool-doc/schema accuracy, skill reframing\n\n- MCP Streamable HTTP now returns 400 for an unsupported MCP-Protocol-Version\n  header on a post-init request (2025-11-25); an absent header is tolerated and\n  the initialize request is exempt.\n- advise_sql declares the same typed findings schema as audit_sql.\n- Reframed the generated skill (description, intro, always-on block) as a\n  code-intelligence and change-impact layer, not just a faster search.\n- Refreshed the MCP server instructions to cover the full tool surface and stop\n  pointing at the CLI for the diff that time_travel_diff already exposes.\n- Reconciled tool descriptions/schemas with behavior: audit_sql N+1, affected\n  cross-language relations, god_nodes/shortest_path defaults, get_source span;\n  fixed wiki structured-output and tool counts and the 0.2.5 static-rule count.\n- Replaced the placeholder SECURITY.md with a real policy.","tree":{"sha":"d63feafe462ef4049034e4b95779267af693132e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/git/trees/d63feafe462ef4049034e4b95779267af693132e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IEatCodeDaily/synaptic-scip/git/commits/adf02a53cd220557fa8129c57e1ba108f0231baf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62533138?v=4","ev