tps://api.github.com/users/Koushik-Deb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Koushik-Deb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/e3fff3cb23d1c21b1fe7af542b5b0c79790f6e09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T16:00:40Z","email":"koushik.imon@gmail.com","name":"Koushik-Deb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T16:00:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(billing): close refund-policy gaps — proration, portal, state and audit trail (#12)\n\nVerification against the stated refund policy turned up three places where the\ncode did not back the policy up. All three are fixed here.\n\n1. Downgrades no longer route money outside admin review.\n\n   subscribe() picked proration_behavior: ''always_invoice'' for every plan\n   change. On a downgrade that raises an immediate negative invoice, which\n   Stripe settles onto the customer''s cash balance — money parked in a payable\n   account, created with no admin review. Upgrades keep ''always_invoice'';\n   downgrades now use ''create_prorations'', so the value becomes a credit line on\n   the next renewal invoice and never becomes cash.\n\n2. The Stripe billing portal configuration is pinned in code.\n\n   createBillingPortalLink() passed no configuration, so the portal inherited\n   the dashboard default. Left there, portal cancellation could be switched to\n   \"immediately, with prorated refund\" from the dashboard, silently overriding\n   both the access-until-period-end rule and the manual-refund rule. The\n   configuration is now resolved by metadata.service === ''postaryx'', created if\n   missing and re-applied on boot: cancel at period end with no proration, and\n   subscription_update disabled so plan changes go through our own flow.\n\n3. Subscription state, payment-failure handling and a billing audit trail.\n\n   - SubscriptionStatus (TRIALING/ACTIVE/PAST_DUE/CANCELED/EXPIRED/FAILED) on\n     Subscription, mapped from the gateway. status describes what the gateway is\n     doing with the money; whether the customer has cancelled stays in cancelAt,\n     so a cancelled-but-paid customer remains ACTIVE and entitled until that\n     date. CANCELED is reserved for the terminal state.\n   - Retiring a subscription is now a soft delete (deletedAt + terminal status)\n     instead of a hard delete, so the org''s last tier and period survive for\n     support. Read paths that lacked a deletedAt filter got one.\n   - invoice.payment_failed, charge.dispute.created and charge.dispute.closed\n     are handled. Payment failure sets PAST_DUE, records the event and notifies\n     the org with a link to the open invoice. These objects carry no\n     subscription metadata, so they are exempted from the metadata guard in\n     stripe.controller.ts and resolved by customer id instead.\n   - BillingEvent: append-only record of every subscription, payment, refund,\n     cancellation and dispute event, with the approving admin in actorUserId.\n     refundCharges() and cancelSubscription() take actorUserId through\n     IBillingProvider. Readable at GET /billing/events (superadmin) and in the\n     admin panel under the charges table.\n\nPolar gets the status mapping only — it still writes no BillingEvents and has no\npayment-failure or dispute handling. Documented as a blocker for switching\nBILLING_PROVIDER=polar.\n\nBehaviour confirmed unchanged: no code path refunds on its own. refundCharges()\nremains the only one that returns money and stays superadmin-gated.\n\nNeeds on deploy: prisma db push; add the three new events to the Stripe webhook\nendpoint.\n\nDocs: new docs/billing-refund-policy.md, cross-referenced from\ndocs/billing-current-state.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f2ebefaaa8b6cdab20798806358377807589aafc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/trees/f2ebefaaa8b6cdab20798806358377807589aafc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/commits/e3fff3cb23d1c21b1fe7af542b5b0c79790f6e09","verification":{"payload":"tree f2ebefaaa8b6cdab20798806358377807589aafc\nparent 3e495e870cb8fa5390e6b944f23d5fd30b9b3cbc\nauthor Koushik-Deb <koushik.imon@gmail.com> 1791475240 +0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791475240 +0600\n\nfeat(billing): close refund-policy gaps — proration, portal, state and audit trail (#12)\n\nVerification against the stated refund policy turned up three places where the\ncode did not back the policy up. All three are fixed here.\n\n1. Downgrades no longer route money outside admin review.\n\n   subscribe() picked proration_behavior: ''always_invoice'' for every plan\n   change. On a downgrade that raises an immediate negative invoice, which\n   Stripe settles onto the customer''s cash balance — money parked in a payable\n   account, created with no admin review. Upgrades keep ''always_invoice'';\n   downgrades now use ''create_prorations'', so the value becomes a credit line on\n   the next renewal invoice and never becomes cash.\n\n2. The Stripe billing portal configuration is pinned in code.\n\n   createBillingPortalLink() passed no configuration, so the portal inherited\n   the dashboard default. Left there, portal cancellation could be switched to\n   \"immediately, with prorated refund\" from the dashboard, silently overriding\n   both the access-until-period-end rule and the manual-refund rule. The\n   configuration is now resolved by metadata.service === ''postaryx'', created if\n   missing and re-applied on boot: cancel at period end with no proration, and\n   subscription_update disabled so plan changes go through our own flow.\n\n3. Subscription state, payment-failure handling and a billing audit trail.\n\n   - SubscriptionStatus (TRIALING/ACTIVE/PAST_DUE/CANCELED/EXPIRED/FAILED) on\n     Subscription, mapped from the gateway. status describes what the gateway is\n     doing with the money; whether the customer has cancelled stays in cancelAt,\n     so a cancelled-but-paid customer remains ACTIVE and entitled until that\n     date. CANCELED is reserved for the terminal state.\n   - Retiring a subscription is now a soft delete (deletedAt + terminal status)\n     instead of a hard delete, so the org''s last tier and period survive for\n     support. Read paths that lacked a deletedAt filter got one.\n   - invoice.payment_failed, charge.dispute.created and charge.dispute.closed\n     are handled. Payment failure sets PAST_DUE, records the event and notifies\n     the org with a link to the open invoice. These objects carry no\n     subscription metadata, so they are exempted from the metadata guard in\n     stripe.controller.ts and resolved by customer id instead.\n   - BillingEvent: append-only record of every subscription, payment, refund,\n     cancellation and dispute event, with the approving admin in actorUserId.\n     refundCharges() and cancelSubscription() take actorUserId through\n     IBillingProvider. Readable at GET /billing/events (superadmin) and in the\n     admin panel under the charges table.\n\nPolar gets the status mapping only — it still writes no BillingEvents and has no\npayment-failure or dispute handling. Documented as a blocker for switching\nBILLING_PROVIDER=polar.\n\nBehaviour confirmed unchanged: no code path refunds on its own. refundCharges()\nremains the only one that returns money and stays superadmin-gated.\n\nNeeds on deploy: prisma db push; add the three new events to the Stripe webhook\nendpoint.\n\nDocs: new docs/billing-refund-policy.md, cross-referenced from\ndocs/billing-current-state.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx74oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR9kQAJV1VjbXYd1EHAYHGPID2rm3\nEP3UclejMY3IM7STsu81q/Gm2W7WquSKgaae9HBltSSg7g0bdZnYvnLtv3UKlKMQ\nGKT17nJgPdy/I1B77c/Vlpf2q3/eHTl/VRkBYQjnR1LWaqwre3lQrTIjz6k/zv+p\nw+saMQR1IW6m9UgNIjIJOevBfVhnnVZxV/tvBr1IiAW10Eoj9vQThcrx/EjR2NY6\n0yLgZivyvm4tHn2LrEiiteZN8t0Gh7Eo+9YlZUDRCF2jg4+lN8X0OAxPisnQv+as\net4nL3EG4/L5kvVm6OW2Z9jmmDSwb0xs3nJqHGxAFFEsP+PnK+JZIgfloYHlRlG7\nozlFtLZY3RVe3oDaiAr1WUDo+xl6+waBgLztHxQPDkgkj3FnukXJSfwyKuSVQgS1\nLN1/4twPjUl8k/AYwkXE989jhIUqwKMNyHoXg+LINItPh+74xRBO0ROYlWp6OWzV\nRnq7jSdfxtIZhRqGKRW38NWCTCYdpFyvuaGelmYvmkmuy3KT5Dage3fv5UDg7bUH\npivXR8KOFkKQfcw0BoizsVxpu5uH7cZpVgviNudEUYXhI971QOPLwZuvgM5F5JfU\nprC7nw36i9QGKlmLQLdMBAEyxJnxfiCgRqQXyBJqzB/LqEyM1pnaeJB/U7A5ePOY\ng4dDNdzfl3/oScenafGg\n=IyHx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T16:00:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commit/e3fff3cb23d1c21b1fe7af542b5b0c79790f6e09","node_id":"C_kwDOTGyzLNoAKGUzZmZmM2NiMjNkMWMyMWIxZmU3YWY1NDJiNWIwYzc5NzkwZjZlMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commit/3e495e870cb8fa5390e6b944f23d5fd30b9b3cbc","sha":"3e495e870cb8fa5390e6b944f23d5fd30b9b3cbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/3e495e870cb8fa5390e6b944f23d5fd30b9b3cbc"}],"sha":"e3fff3cb23d1c21b1fe7af542b5b0c79790f6e09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/e3fff3cb23d1c21b1fe7af542b5b0c79790f6e09"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44846872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qwertyz15","id":44846872,"login":"qwertyz15","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODQ2ODcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/3e495e870cb8fa5390e6b944f23d5fd30b9b3cbc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T15:59:41Z","email":"44846872+qwertyz15@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Fahim Shahriar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T15:59:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(telegram): upload local media from disk instead of a hostless URL (#16)\n\n* fix(telegram): upload local media from disk instead of a hostless URL\n\nPosting an image failed every time with \"ETELEGRAM: 400 Bad Request:\ninvalid file HTTP URL specified: URL host is empty\". processMedia stripped\nFRONTEND_URL off the media path, so Telegram was handed \"/uploads/..\" and\nparsed it as a URL with no host.\n\nThe intent was right — Telegram fetches remote media itself and can never\nreach a local FRONTEND_URL — but the stripped value is not a usable disk\npath either, since it resolves from the filesystem root.\n\nMap the public /uploads/... URL back to the real file with the existing\nresolveUploadDirectory helper, and only substitute it when the file is\nactually there. If this process cannot see the upload volume the original\nURL is kept, which is what production needs: the media is publicly\nreachable there and Telegram can fetch it directly.\n\nAlso document TELEGRAM_TOKEN and TELEGRAM_BOT_NAME in .env.example; both\nare required to connect a channel and neither was listed.\n\nVerified against a live channel: two posts that had failed on every\nattempt published once the orchestrator picked this up.\n\n* fix(posts): skip settings validation for DTOs with no rules so Kick can post\n\n* fix(whop): send client_secret in token exchange and refresh when configured\n\n* fix(pinterest): show Pinterest''s error message instead of Unknown Error on 4xx\n\n* feat(farcaster): port upstream #2078 to replace retired SIWN with Neynar managed signers\n\n* fix(farcaster): port upstream #2080 to show the approval QR in a modal\n\n* fix(posts): redact OAuth tokens before saving post errors\n\n* Updated readme\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Koushik Deb <koushik.imon@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Nevo David <100117126+nevo-david@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"569643a1665f191afdfcf6e846b9c2c6e0b66803","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/trees/569643a1665f191afdfcf6e846b9c2c6e0b66803"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/commits/3e495e870cb8fa5390e6b944f23d5fd30b9b3cbc","verification":{"payload":"tree 569643a1665f191afdfcf6e846b9c2c6e0b66803\nparent 0cd31a3c5095c677f2236fedf87753d3a29280b5\nauthor Fahim Shahriar <44846872+qwertyz15@users.noreply.github.com> 1791475181 +0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791475181 +0600\n\nfix(telegram): upload local media from disk instead of a hostless URL (#16)\n\n* fix(telegram): upload local media from disk instead of a hostless URL\n\nPosting an image failed every time with \"ETELEGRAM: 400 Bad Request:\ninvalid file HTTP URL specified: URL host is empty\". processMedia stripped\nFRONTEND_URL off the media path, so Telegram was handed \"/uploads/..\" and\nparsed it as a URL with no host.\n\nThe intent was right — Telegram fetches remote media itself and can never\nreach a local FRONTEND_URL — but the stripped value is not a usable disk\npath either, since it resolves from the filesystem root.\n\nMap the public /uploads/... URL back to the real file with the existing\nresolveUploadDirectory helper, and only substitute it when the file is\nactually there. If this process cannot see the upload volume the original\nURL is kept, which is what production needs: the media is publicly\nreachable there and Telegram can fetch it directly.\n\nAlso document TELEGRAM_TOKEN and TELEGRAM_BOT_NAME in .env.example; both\nare required to connect a channel and neither was listed.\n\nVerified against a live channel: two posts that had failed on every\nattempt published once the orchestrator picked this up.\n\n* fix(posts): skip settings validation for DTOs with no rules so Kick can post\n\n* fix(whop): send client_secret in token exchange and refresh when configured\n\n* fix(pinterest): show Pinterest''s error message instead of Unknown Error on 4xx\n\n* feat(farcaster): port upstream #2078 to replace retired SIWN with Neynar managed signers\n\n* fix(farcaster): port upstream #2080 to show the approval QR in a modal\n\n* fix(posts): redact OAuth tokens before saving post errors\n\n* Updated readme\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Koushik Deb <koushik.imon@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Nevo David <100117126+nevo-david@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx73tCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3j8QAGdYVp2acQwP6PqhhvnOabNe\nNawBoWZr+E+4t7FTr4WFGY86PoZ40jc7ZlmxjOVt9SnO91vm/ATioGkBstA2YmiX\nKKISEeYIhf55IW1IxdROcXBSf31TcACf8Pl0+l8BJY5hiw6Jv2dWuV+x1UEV8+q2\nAfde7n1VoDw8Rs1JgzM9rGe69Mj/ybsmo1L2eqVgu33OsWL9GYa3WkmF/mwyqBF9\nHBAYUZIqel+TE5qp+YgRtGK8R4ktp3iyHvOVDiHS3EXGgjHmDKwe1aCJkEmlYBhJ\n92qrvM7MX70FUUPLMjLw0osUAPbxP5wXKWPCh8lJ6ShhvS0PSOBFr0URRICy2CBs\nHrK1hQnYY9L5n+Zn2l/zfgSevX0tMJ/8nTrQKLH+rAlH0nxopHtfZTFFY/VfKM11\nFySMKRtkJmplSOI68Ykm5/x3VD42m/U9i5JtGIKfsKNwETQdks/DY4Ek3/NqRNwd\nRJAm5QjESri4Zo+d1nBY4nLbGDzB3KCEOPy1Vgy8c0QVkcp7xjd8Ve87V6lbFvy7\nzDUk9v4sE5ZYcXy2Iw4dAUVJuglW5wlixHgXiTbu86XHjuwgSnP8gss6knvVx5hd\nsG4qYTvMwdezAGdQpwXDr/muPBWE1t7dznRuIwcuecfXo6sFyphfGMdGzVDTDa/p\nUSW1A2PFSvtcwaYyULOW\n=31+I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T15:59:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commit/3e495e870cb8fa5390e6b944f23d5fd30b9b3cbc","node_id":"C_kwDOTGyzLNoAKDNlNDk1ZTg3MGNiOGZhNTM5MGU2Yjk0NGYyM2Q1ZmQzMGI5YjNjYmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commit/0cd31a3c5095c677f2236fedf87753d3a29280b5","sha":"0cd31a3c5095c677f2236fedf87753d3a29280b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/0cd31a3c5095c677f2236fedf87753d3a29280b5"}],"sha":"3e495e870cb8fa5390e6b944f23d5fd30b9b3cbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/3e495e870cb8fa5390e6b944f23d5fd30b9b3cbc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44846872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qwertyz15","id":44846872,"login":"qwertyz15","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODQ2ODcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/0cd31a3c5095c677f2236fedf87753d3a29280b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:35:31Z","email":"44846872+qwertyz15@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Fahim Shahriar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:35:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(nostr, dev.to, moltbook): decode the hex private key before signing events (#15)\n\n* fix(nostr): decode the hex private key before signing events\n\nPosting to Nostr failed with \"expected Uint8Array, got type=string\" and\nnever reached a relay. `post()` and `comment()` read the private key out\nof the stored JWT as a hex string and handed it straight to\n`finalizeEvent`, but nostr-tools signs with the raw 32-byte key.\n\n`authenticate()` already did the conversion inline, which is why\nconnecting a channel worked while publishing did not.\n\nPull that conversion into a `hexToBytes` helper and use it at all three\ncall sites. Verified against a stored key: the old path throws the\nproduction error, the new one produces an event whose signature\nverifies and whose pubkey matches the integration''s internalId.\n\n* fix(hashnode): send tags by slug and cover as coverImage\n\nHashnode''s PublishPostTagInput dropped `id` and now requires `slug`, and\n`coverImageOptions { coverImageURL }` was replaced by `coverImage`. Every\npublish failed schema validation. Saved tags still carry the objectID, so\nmap it back to the slug via hashnode.tags.ts.\n\nGraphQL errors arrive as HTTP 200, which crashed on `data.publishPost`\nand got retried; fail once with Hashnode''s own message instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(moltbook): respect rate limits and report pending verification\n\nMoltbook allows 1 post per 30 min (2 h for new agents) and 1 comment per\n20 s, but the provider allowed 100 concurrent jobs and surfaced 429s as\nplain axios errors that Temporal retried inside the cooldown.\n\n- maxConcurrentJob 100 -> 1\n- wait out short cooldowns (<= 90 s) in the activity, fail long ones once\n  as a non-retryable BadBody with a \"try again in N minutes\" message\n- surface Moltbook''s own error text for other failures\n- send `submolt_name`, the field the API now expects\n- posts from untrusted agents come back `verification_status: pending`\n  and stay hidden; mark them `pending_verification` so the workflow sends\n  an info notification instead of \"published\"\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(devto): stop dropping images attached to the post\n\nOnly the \"Cover picture\" setting was sent; images attached to the post\nwere ignored. Use the first attached image as the cover when none is\nset and embed the rest in the markdown body. Videos are skipped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Koushik Deb <koushik.imon@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9045abbbe1d54f2767ef5f5db974e3de65e05875","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/trees/9045abbbe1d54f2767ef5f5db974e3de65e05875"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/commits/0cd31a3c5095c677f2236fedf87753d3a29280b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 9045abbbe1d54f2767ef5f5db974e3de65e05875\nparent 82339a244843cadfcbfee7225a56ecc80e4f8750\nauthor Fahim Shahriar <44846872+qwertyz15@users.noreply.github.com> 1790519731 +0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790519731 +0600\n\nfix(nostr, dev.to, moltbook): decode the hex private key before signing events (#15)\n\n* fix(nostr): decode the hex private key before signing events\n\nPosting to Nostr failed with \"expected Uint8Array, got type=string\" and\nnever reached a relay. `post()` and `comment()` read the private key out\nof the stored JWT as a hex string and handed it straight to\n`finalizeEvent`, but nostr-tools signs with the raw 32-byte key.\n\n`authenticate()` already did the conversion inline, which is why\nconnecting a channel worked while publishing did not.\n\nPull that conversion into a `hexToBytes` helper and use it at all three\ncall sites. Verified against a stored key: the old path throws the\nproduction error, the new one produces an event whose signature\nverifies and whose pubkey matches the integration''s internalId.\n\n* fix(hashnode): send tags by slug and cover as coverImage\n\nHashnode''s PublishPostTagInput dropped `id` and now requires `slug`, and\n`coverImageOptions { coverImageURL }` was replaced by `coverImage`. Every\npublish failed schema validation. Saved tags still carry the objectID, so\nmap it back to the slug via hashnode.tags.ts.\n\nGraphQL errors arrive as HTTP 200, which crashed on `data.publishPost`\nand got retried; fail once with Hashnode''s own message instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(moltbook): respect rate limits and report pending verification\n\nMoltbook allows 1 post per 30 min (2 h for new agents) and 1 comment per\n20 s, but the provider allowed 100 concurrent jobs and surfaced 429s as\nplain axios errors that Temporal retried inside the cooldown.\n\n- maxConcurrentJob 100 -> 1\n- wait out short cooldowns (<= 90 s) in the activity, fail long ones once\n  as a non-retryable BadBody with a \"try again in N minutes\" message\n- surface Moltbook''s own error text for other failures\n- send `submolt_name`, the field the API now expects\n- posts from untrusted agents come back `verification_status: pending`\n  and stay hidden; mark them `pending_verification` so the workflow sends\n  an info notification instead of \"published\"\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(devto): stop dropping images attached to the post\n\nOnly the \"Cover picture\" setting was sent; images attached to the post\nwere ignored. Use the first attached image as the cover when none is\nset and embed the rest in the markdown body. Videos are skipped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Koushik Deb <koushik.imon@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquSmzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX4AQAITJF2ITcQTArMgztqMXThEg\nVQKcZiyM6jOnu9xSnYJzLZpnOiBUVb3tRSW9JSbk7sSA/LOgt20NMnji5m0kWFGn\nm6OkfpjqX4E4Y86WAcJL7G8nmWGBD99OnEoY4tGzTzPr7NaLB+llKFjOT/vHJc+g\nR0hkASxAfZUN5oyhp37kmd2Yz2WyNOcAoa4bIdNVs8A5yQwn281IayGBVWRIluLh\n236L96JIRgxPPnjJj2c5W7WkMaCkJEoIz2Mw6q+Pz8gtoafZ1UBXx+iGwiVs2pw6\n4ixLg6Btz5qWTAKbAS5Osaypa2ZDJNKlyM1sGZheCWLDVff8XxA3NvUrzsORuTa5\na+MmMSrCe/n132BsMclU9rX7vqo8BO946m3DST2B6GXJOqnlyNjAmou07B4dzjC1\n9zVUEywpXSL6vdiSoCWWLqo1P9/BNqgRh2CPezB0h4FNA5dm3OYmS+OnKIILsVwc\nwTyh+GtZ44Letb3GCCWbhSo6j2RbLeLhTt1/FEFnpxyaRxLhjTjgmQJh+IF+4iKs\nB6Kixch5+Ad5fyevip02+QmpKwnaqPKiIbWvebgn2Ij6/xrNxnJ1LhF9BGpas5oz\nwSxdg49d2iWnHMghzuiJK+HFqzWtPJ3Wn5di7ZEV2bnpDbmkgjB/GwnRviCRgaJc\nXihLvL12h0iPjlLBVSsI\n=Ip9f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T14:35:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commit/0cd31a3c5095c677f2236fedf87753d3a29280b5","node_id":"C_kwDOTGyzLNoAKDBjZDMxYTNjNTA5NWM2NzdmMjIzNmZlZGY4Nzc1M2QzYTI5MjgwYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commit/82339a244843cadfcbfee7225a56ecc80e4f8750","sha":"82339a244843cadfcbfee7225a56ecc80e4f8750","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/82339a244843cadfcbfee7225a56ecc80e4f8750"}],"sha":"0cd31a3c5095c677f2236fedf87753d3a29280b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/0cd31a3c5095c677f2236fedf87753d3a29280b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44846872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qwertyz15","id":44846872,"login":"qwertyz15","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODQ2ODcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/82339a244843cadfcbfee7225a56ecc80e4f8750/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T19:53:52Z","email":"44846872+qwertyz15@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Fahim Shahriar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T19:53:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/cleanup #6 (#14)\n\n* feat(onboarding): drop the tutorial step and its Postiz video\n\n/launches?onboarding=true embedded youtube.com/embed/BdsCVvEYgHU, which is\nPostiz''s tutorial, not ours.\n\nIt was not a stray iframe: the modal was a two step wizard and step two was\nthe tutorial, so removing the video meant removing the step. Gone with it:\nOnboardingStep2 in full, and the \"1 Connect Channels / 2 Watch Tutorial\"\nindicator row, which says nothing once there is one step.\n\nThe modal now renders OnboardingStep1 directly and step one''s button\nfinishes instead of advancing, calling onClose, which already closes the\nmodal and drops the onboarding query param. Its label reuses keys already\npresent in all sixteen locales, so no translation file changes:\n\n  channels connected  get_started               \"Get Started\"\n  none                continue_without_channels \"Continue without channels\"\n\nStep one is otherwise untouched: AddProviderComponent, the connected\nchannel list, the copy and the orange CTA all stay as they were.\n\nAlso drops what only the removed markup used: the onSkip prop, which was\ndeclared and destructured but never referenced, and the useState and clsx\nimports.\n\nThe same video is still embedded in first.billing.component.tsx, behind the\nwatch-the-video link on the free tier billing screen. Left alone, since this\nwas scoped to the onboarding route. The three watch_tutorial* locale keys\nare orphaned for now and kept until that one is settled.\n\n* chore: remove the Postiz tutorial video from the remaining surfaces\n\nFollows 75cbec56, which took it out of onboarding. youtube.com/embed/\nBdsCVvEYgHU is Postiz''s tutorial and was still embedded in two more places.\n\nBilling screen, the free tier upsell: the showYouTube handler and the\ntrigger behind it, a YouTube icon reading \"See the power of Postaryx\n(click here)\". Drops what only that used: the modals binding and the\nuseModals and SafeImage imports.\n\nREADME: the \"Watch the YouTube Tutorials\" link, and the \"See the leading\nPostaryx features\" block, which was a clickable thumbnail with the same\nvideo behind it. That also drops an upstream github user-attachments\nimage, so if a static Postaryx screenshot is wanted there, that block is\nwhere it goes.\n\nPure deletions, 44 lines, nothing added. A repo-wide sweep for\nBdsCVvEYgHU, youtube.com/embed, youtu.be and iframe now returns nothing.\n\nThe watch_tutorial, watch_tutorial_title and watch_tutorial_description\nkeys are left orphaned in all sixteen locales plus i18n.lock. Clearing\nthem touches seventeen files including a lockfile, which is a different\nkind of change from pulling a video.\n\n* chore(i18n): drop the orphaned watch_tutorial keys\n\nCompletes 75cbec56 and 0a3590b4, which removed the Postiz tutorial video\nfrom onboarding, the billing screen and the README. The keys that labelled\nit had no call sites left:\n\n  watch_tutorial\n  watch_tutorial_title\n  watch_tutorial_description\n\nRemoved from the fifteen locales that carried them, three lines each, plus\ntheir three hashes in i18n.lock. ka_ge never had them; it is a partial\ntranslation at 505 keys against the others'' 691.\n\nLine-based removal rather than a json round trip, so formatting is\nuntouched and the diff is 48 deletions with nothing added. Every locale\nre-parses as JSON and each of the fifteen lost exactly three keys. A\nrepo-wide grep for watch_tutorial now returns nothing.\n\nLeft alone: \"back\" and \"get_started\", which the removed step also used but\nwhich are still called from third-party.media-library.tsx and the\nonboarding CTA respectively.\n\nAlso noticed but not removed: \"continue\" is now orphaned too, since\n75cbec56 moved the onboarding CTA from it to get_started. It is a generic\nlabel worth keeping for reuse, and it is outside what this change is for.\n\n* fix(billing): ground the onboarding billing copy in what the code does\n\nThe page a FREE tier user lands on at /launches?onboarding=true, which is\nFirstBillingComponent replacing the shell rather than the onboarding modal,\ncarried inherited claims. Each was checked against the implementation\nbefore rewriting.\n\nFalse, removed:\n\n- \"To confirm credit card information Postaryx will hold $2 and release it\n  immediately\". No such code exists. A specific, checkable and wrong\n  statement about charging a customer''s card, shown in sixteen languages.\n- \"Join Over 20,000+ Entrepreneurs\". Unverifiable social proof.\n- \"proudly open-source ... will live forever\". Cannot be substantiated from\n  here, and inherited from upstream.\n- \"100% No-Risk Free Trial\" and \"Pay NOTHING for the first 7-days\".\n\nTrue, and now stated plainly:\n\n  7 day trial            stripe.service.ts:473,534 trial_period_days: 7\n  card required up front checkout.sessions.create, mode: ''subscription''\n  access to period end   stripe.service.ts:356 cancel_at_period_end: true\n  Stripe processes       database.module.ts:77, Polar is parked\n  named platforms        all present in the 33 registered providers\n\nHero becomes \"Grow Your Social Presence with Postaryx\". Trial bullets state\nthe length, that a payment method is required with no charge during the\ntrial, and that cancelling is self serve. The FAQ now answers the trial\ncharge, cancellation, and trust questions factually, and gains a \"Can I\ncancel anytime?\" entry matching cancel_at_period_end.\n\nChanging only the English fallbacks would have left the other fifteen\nlanguages still serving the $2 claim, since every claim-bearing key has\nlocale values. So these use new keys and the twelve superseded ones are\ndeleted from all sixteen locales and i18n.lock. The new keys have no locale\nentries yet, so every language renders the accurate English fallback until\nthe i18n pipeline is re-run. That is deliberate: accurate English beats\ninaccurate localised billing terms.\n\nAlso drops isGeneral ? ''Postaryx'' : ''Postaryx'', dead since the rename, and\nthe useVariables import it needed.\n\nLayout, pricing cards, FAQ accordion and dark theme are untouched.\n\nThe copy now asserts things the Terms and Refund Policy should agree with.\nVerified against code, not against those pages.\n\n* feat(header): hide the Developers entry point behind a flag\n\nThe developer portal is not exposed publicly yet, so the \"Developers\" item\nin the header should not render. Nothing is deleted.\n\nGuarded inside DeveloperIconComponent with SHOW_DEVELOPER_PORTAL = false\nand an early return, rather than commenting out the call site. It mounts in\nexactly one place today, the billing and onboarding header in\nfirst.billing.component.tsx; the main app header never had it. Guarding at\nthe component keeps it hidden in any layout that mounts it later too, which\nis what hiding it consistently actually needs. Both hooks run before the\nearly return, so hook order is unchanged.\n\nFlipping the constant to true restores it.\n\nUntouched: developer.component.tsx and the modal it fills, the public API\ncomponent, apps/backend/src/public-api and its routes, API keys, OAuth apps,\nMCP and the CLI docs. Header design, logo, theme toggle, language selector\nand every other nav item are also unchanged.\n\nNot touched, and worth a decision: Settings has a second \"Developers\" entry\nat settings.component.tsx:107, gated on user.tier.public_api && isGeneral,\nwhich opens the same public API surface. This change was scoped to the\nheader, but the same reasoning applies to that tab.\n\n* style(billing): soften the FAQ card border to the app''s standard token\n\nThe FAQ accordion used border-tableBorder, which resolves through two\naliases to a value that is only heavy in dark:\n\n  tableBorder -> --color-table-border -> --new-table-border\n                                         #c2410c dark, #e7e3db light\n\nAgainst the card''s #24211c that is contrast 3.10 at 88% saturation, a hard\norange outline next to every other dark card.\n\nSwitched to newBorder, #4e2f1f dark and #e7e3db light, giving 1.34 against\nthe same background, which sits next to the canonical card''s 1.42 against\n#1f1c17. That is why the two now read as one system. newBorder is also the\nmost used border token in the app, 24 call sites against tableBorder''s 17,\nso this is reuse rather than a new FAQ-specific value.\n\nLight is byte identical: both tokens resolve to #e7e3db there.\n\nUnchanged: layout, accordion behaviour, text, spacing, typography,\nrounded-[8px], and bg-sixth, which resolves to --new-table-header, the same\nsurface the third-party and plugs cards already use. No hover or open-state\naccent was added; there is none today and adding one would be a redesign.\n\nNot touched, same defect: twenty-three other files still use\nborder-tableBorder, including the calendar, comments, date picker and the\nprovider panels, so they carry the same #c2410c outline in dark.\n\n* style(billing): bring the pricing cards onto the design system\n\nThe billing page read as an older internal layout mostly because of the\npricing card, which carried three problems in one className.\n\nRadius: rounded-[4px]. global.scss only remaps 8, 12 and 16px onto the\n--app-radius-* scale, so 4px rendered literally and every card sat almost\nsquare next to the 12px cards everywhere else. Now rounded-[12px].\n\nBorder: border-customColor6, a deprecated --color-custom* token that\nCLAUDE.md flags, resolving to #6f3f2c in dark. Against the card''s #24211c\nthat is 1.85, heavier than any other dark card. Now border-newBorder,\n#4e2f1f, 1.34, the same token and weight as the canonical card.\n\nSelected state: there was none. currentPackage was already computed for the\nbutton logic but nothing showed it. The current plan now takes\nborder-cardAccentBorder, rgba(194, 65, 12, 0.3), the same subtle accent the\nauth card uses. Orange is therefore confined to CTAs and the active state\nrather than being the default card outline.\n\nBoth tokens already existed; nothing new was introduced, and clsx was\nalready imported.\n\nThe FAQ needed nothing: this page renders the same FAQComponent fixed in\n842cd5c8, where the border went from tableBorder #c2410c at 3.10 to\nnewBorder at 1.34.\n\nLogout was checked and deliberately left alone. Spacing is not the problem,\nthere is already about 60px of separation. LogoutComponent renders a bare\ndiv with unstyled text, so it reads as stray copy, and it is shared with the\nheader, which puts a proper fix outside a presentation-only change here.\n\nNo billing logic, Stripe, checkout, pricing data, purchase action, toggle or\nFAQ content was touched; the diff is one className.\n\n* feat(nav): hide the Affiliate item from the sidebar\n\nPostaryx is not running an affiliate programme yet, so the entry should not\nrender. Nothing is deleted.\n\nThe menu already had the mechanism for this: MenuItem declares hide?:\nboolean and both filter passes, firstMenu at line 330 and secondMenu at\n358, return false on it. So this is one flag on the Affiliate entry rather\nthan commenting out fifty-eight lines, most of which are its inline svg.\nAffiliate sits in secondMenu; the flag would work in either.\n\nThat covers every nav surface. TopMenu renders once, from\nnew-layout/layout.component.tsx, and there is no separate mobile nav. The\nonly other consumer is title.tsx, which resolves the page heading by\nmatching the route against item.path, and Affiliate''s path is an external\nurl that no route matches.\n\nUntouched: analytics, media, plugs, integrations, UGC, billing, settings.\n\nTwo things found while doing this. There is no affiliate functionality to\npreserve: frontend routes, components, backend and the prisma schema are\nall empty of it, and this menu entry was the only reference in the repo\noutside the locale files. And the entry''s path points at\ngithub.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza rather than an affiliate page,\ninherited from upstream and repointed during the rename, so it needs a real\ndestination before it is ever shown again. Both are noted in the comment.\n\nThe affiliate translation key stays in all sixteen locales, unused but\nready if the item is re-enabled.\n\n* feat(settings): hide the Developers tab behind a flag\n\nCompletes 282563d3, which hid the header entry point. Settings offered a\nsecond route to the same public API surface via its Developers tab.\n\nGated the arr.push on SHOW_DEVELOPER_PORTAL = false, matching the header\nflag''s name and shape, with each comment pointing at the other so the pair\nis re-enabled together.\n\nGating the push alone is enough. tab is useState(''global_settings'') and its\nonly writer is setTab(tabKey) on a tab click, with no url sync or other\nentry point, so with ''api'' absent from the list it can never become active.\nThe tab body is left exactly as written and is simply unreachable.\n\nNothing deleted: PublicComponent, developer.component.tsx,\napps/backend/src/public-api, the tab body, API keys, OAuth apps and MCP are\nall intact. Global Settings, Teams, Webhooks, Auto Post, Sets, Signatures\nand Approved Apps are untouched.\n\nThere are now two independent SHOW_DEVELOPER_PORTAL constants, here and in\ndeveloper/developer.icon.component.tsx. Kept local rather than sharing one\nexport, since the alternatives were importing a constant from an icon\ncomponent or adding a file for a single boolean. They can drift; a small\nfeature-flags module would consolidate them if more of these appear.\n\n* docs(security): rewrite the security policy for Postaryx\n\nThe file was upstream''s verbatim. It introduced itself as \"Postiz\n(gitroomhq)\", scoped itself to github.com/gitroomhq/postiz-app, pointed\nreporters at upstream''s GitHub Security Advisories, and named an upstream\nmaintainer''s personal address, egelhaus@ennogelhaus.de, as the urgent\ncontact.\n\nThat is a security defect rather than a branding one: anyone finding a flaw\nin Postaryx would have disclosed it to a third party, and the address is\nnot ours to publish.\n\nRewritten for Postaryx, operated by Lunark Dynamics LLC. Every identifier\nasserted is one already established in the repo:\n\n  app.postaryx.com                       .env.example:45\n  api.postaryx.com                       .env.example:31\n  github.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza  22 references\n  ghcr.io/aitechnologysys-sys            docker-compose.yaml:28\n  Lunark Dynamics LLC                    docs/12-AUG-3 and docs/2.\n\nTwo judgement calls.\n\nNo security address was given, so this uses security@postaryx.com,\nfollowing the support@postaryx.com convention in .env.example:33. The\nmailbox has to exist and be monitored before this is published: a policy\npointing at a dead address is worse than none, because reporters will\nassume they have told us and may publish when we do not answer.\n\nAll response timelines are gone and nothing replaces them. Upstream\ncommitted to 72 hour acknowledgement, 7 day triage, 90 and 180 day\nremediation and 24 hour CVE publication; none of those are ours to\npromise. \"What happens next\" describes the sequence without a clock. Add\nreal numbers once we know what we can honour.\n\nScope now names our four surfaces and rules out self-hosted infrastructure\nand the third-party platforms we integrate with, which matters with 33\nproviders or researchers will send us Instagram bugs. Email is the primary\nchannel with advisories as an alternative, since advisories are useless to\nan external reporter if the repository is private. Also adds a line asking\nresearchers not to test against other users'' accounts, and an offer of\ncredit.\n\nNo application code touched.\n\n* docs(readme): clear inherited upstream references and broken links\n\nRemoved, all upstream''s and two of them untrue:\n\n- opencollective.com/postiz, a live donation link on our README paying\n  upstream. .github/FUNDING.yaml was neutralised earlier but this was\n  missed.\n- The whole Sponsor section. Its pitch claimed \"almost 3m downloads and 20k\n  views per month\" and \"Website has 20k hits\", which are upstream''s\n  numbers presented as ours, the same class of claim removed from billing\n  in be75e9fd. FUNDING.yaml is deliberately all-commented, so there is no\n  Postaryx funding destination to point at either.\n- The G2 badge, which collected product reviews for Postiz''s G2 page.\n- The Snyk badge, served from snyk-labs/secure-developer-sample-repo. That\n  is a sample repository''s badge, not a scan of this project, so it was a\n  misleading security signal.\n- \"Join Our Discord (devs only)\", which linked to postaryx.com rather than\n  any Discord, and NEXT_PUBLIC_DISCORD_SUPPORT is empty so no server\n  exists.\n\nRepointed:\n\n- The fourteen social icons. They pointed at\n  github.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/svgs/socials/*.svg, but svgs/ does\n  not exist in this repo, it is upstream''s, and that url form is not a raw\n  path in any case. A rename had swapped the org without checking the\n  target, leaving fourteen broken images. Now repo-relative paths to\n  apps/frontend/public/icons/platforms/*.png, which exist and render on\n  GitHub without depending on repo visibility or branch.\n- Star History, which charted postaryx/postiz-app. That repo does not\n  exist, so the chart was also broken. Now aitechnologysys-sys/veroza.\n- The Hostinger sponsor link, off Postiz''s landing page to hostinger.com,\n  keeping ?ref=postaryx since that suggests a real affiliate code.\n\nVerified afterwards: no Postiz or Gitroom string remains, all fifteen\nimage sources resolve, and all thirteen relative doc links resolve.\n\nLicense attribution and installation instructions are untouched.\n\nWorth confirming separately: Hostinger and Virlo were both inherited from\nupstream''s sponsor list, so the table should go if they do not actually\nsponsor Postaryx.\n\n* docs(security): point disclosures at a mailbox that exists\n\n07fae5ac used security@postaryx.com, inferred from the\nsupport@postaryx.com convention in .env.example since no address had been\ngiven. That mailbox does not exist. A disclosure policy naming a dead\naddress is worse than none: reporters assume they have told us and may\npublish when nothing comes back.\n\nOf the two addresses that do exist, admin@ rather than support@. A\nvulnerability report should not land in a customer support queue, where it\ncan be triaged as an ordinary ticket by someone without the context or\nauthority to act, and where the ticket system widens who can read an\nunpatched exploit.\n\nWorth adding later: security@ is the address researchers look for by\nconvention, and what security.txt and most disclosure tooling expect. An\nalias to admin@ costs nothing and catches anyone who guesses it.\n\n* docs(contributing): rewrite for Postaryx and drop dead upstream links\n\nEvery destination the page pointed at was upstream''s, and none has a\nPostaryx equivalent anywhere in the repo:\n\n  docs.postiz.com/developer-guide   x2, the \"read this first\" link\n  contribute.postiz.com/p/postiz    a contribution form we do not run\n  discord.postiz.com                x2, NEXT_PUBLIC_DISCORD_SUPPORT is empty\n  docs.postiz.com/support           a support page we do not run\n  git clone .../postiz.git          wrong repository name\n\nSince there is genuinely no public contribution workflow, no docs site, no\nchat and no form, the page now says so in the opening paragraph rather\nthan implying infrastructure we do not have. It then describes only what\nworks today: GitHub issues, and SECURITY.md for vulnerabilities. Links go\nto documents that exist, CLAUDE.md, docs/LOCAL-DEVELOPMENT.md and\ndocs/RUNNING-DEV-AND-PROD.md, all six verified to resolve.\n\nUpstream''s \"under 3 lines, just send it\" heuristic is replaced by asking\nfor an issue before substantial work, since that rule relied on a Discord\nwe do not run.\n\nKept: the fork, branch, pull request mechanics, with the clone url fixed\nto veroza.git, and the existing stance on AI-generated pull requests,\nreworded but not softened, since changing that policy was not asked for.\nAdded an explicit note that contributions are licensed AGPL-3.0.\n\nFlagged separately, not changed here: CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:63 still routes\nconduct reports to nevo@gitroom.com, upstream''s founder. That is the same\ndefect fixed in SECURITY.md by 07fae5ac and wants the same treatment. This\npage links to the Code of Conduct because contributors should know one\napplies.\n\n* chore(git): drop the stale gitroomhq public-api submodule\n\n.gitmodules declared a submodule at libraries/plugins/src/list/public-api\npointing at git@github.com:gitroomhq/public-api.git. Nothing in this repo\nuses it:\n\n- libraries/plugins does not exist on disk\n- no gitlink (mode 160000) in the index, and zero tracked files under\n  that path\n- .git/config has no [submodule] section and there is no .git/modules\n- git submodule status is empty\n- no source file imports @gitroom/plugins\n- no CI workflow checks out with submodules\n\nSo `git submodule update --init` was a no-op that only ever produced a\nfailed clone for anyone who ran it.\n\nLeft in place deliberately, as they are a separate concern: the dead\n@gitroom/plugins path aliases in tsconfig.base.json and\napps/orchestrator/.swcrc, and the .gitignore entry for\nlibraries/plugins/src/plugins.ts.\n\nRecorded in docs/UPSTREAM-SYNC.md so a merge that restores the file is\nresolved as a delete/modify conflict rather than silently reinstating\nthe submodule.\n\n* chore(config): drop the dead @gitroom/plugins path aliases\n\nBoth tsconfig.base.json and apps/orchestrator/.swcrc mapped\n@gitroom/plugins/* to libraries/plugins/src/*, a directory that does not\nexist in this repo. It went away with the gitroomhq/public-api submodule\nremoved in the previous commit; nothing imports through the alias, so the\nmappings only resolved to a missing path.\n\nVerified: zero occurrences of @gitroom/plugins outside these two files,\nand both `pnpm build:backend` and `pnpm build:orchestrator` succeed.\n\nStill dead, left for a separate pass: apps/orchestrator/.swcrc also\naliases @gitroom/cron and @gitroom/workers to apps/cron and apps/workers\n(neither exists) and sets baseUrl to an absolute path from an upstream\ndeveloper''s machine. The whole file is unused anyway — apps/orchestrator/\nnest-cli.json does not set the swc builder, so `nest build` compiles with\ntsc. .gitignore also still ignores libraries/plugins/src/plugins.ts.\n\n* docs(readme): drop the inherited product showcase sections\n\nThree blocks carried over from upstream, none of which describe this\nfork:\n\n- \"✨ Features\" — a 2x2 table of four upstream product screenshots\n  hosted on github.com/user-attachments.\n- \"Our Sponsors\" — Hostinger and Virlo, upstream''s sponsors rather than\n  ours. Both referral links had been caught by the blanket rename and\n  read ?ref=postaryx, a code neither company issued.\n- The \"check out Postaryx agent CLI! perfect for OpenClaw and other\n  agents\" banner. No such CLI exists here — apps/ is backend, commands,\n  extension, frontend, orchestrator, sdk, and \"OpenClaw\" appeared\n  nowhere else in the tree. Another blanket-rename artefact, pointing at\n  postaryx.com rather than at any CLI.\n\nVerified afterwards: every remaining local image and link target\nresolves on disk (14 platform icons, 15 doc/file links), and no\nreference to the removed sections survives.\n\n.github/sponsors/hostinger.png is now unreferenced; left in place as\nthis commit touches README.md only.\n\n* docs(readme): use the Postaryx logo and strip the inherited hero\n\nThe header still served the purple Postiz wordmark from\ngithub.com/user-attachments behind an alt of \"Postaryx Logo\". Both\nscheme variants now point at the logo assets already in the repo.\nRasterised both to confirm the pairing rather than trusting the\nfilenames: \"Dark\"/\"Light\" names the background the asset is drawn for,\nthe same convention the app''s logo component uses.\n\nHero link rows removed in full — \"Explore the docs\", \"Register / Public\nAPI\", and \"NodeJS SDK / N8N custom node / Make.com integration\". All\nthree entries in that last row pointed at the same apps/sdk/README.md;\nthere is no N8N node and no Make.com integration in this repo.\n\nIntro now claims only what the product does:\n\n- dropped the \"alternative to Buffer.com, Hypefury, Twitter Hunter\"\n  positioning line\n- dropped \"exchange or buy posts\" — the marketplace does not exist here,\n  no reference in the frontend nav or the backend\n- dropped \"no difference between the hosted version to the self-hosted\n  version\", which is false: isBillingEnabled() gates channel, credit and\n  team-member limits, permission checks, the public API and the\n  publisher\n- \"automation with N8N, Make.com, Zapier\" -> the public API and the\n  NodeJS SDK, which is what actually ships\n\nVerified: no occurrence of postiz, gitroom or user-attachments remains,\nall 16 local image references and all 19 link targets resolve.\n\nLicense badge, LICENSE link, Tech Stack, Quick Start, Compliance and the\ndeployment runbook are untouched.","tree":{"sha":"cede7f4af6668e62f0c95fcf30ac882eb4f21944","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/trees/cede7f4af6668e62f0c95fcf30ac882eb4f21944"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/commits/82339a244843cadfcbfee7225a56ecc80e4f8750","verification":{"payload":"tree cede7f4af6668e62f0c95fcf30ac882eb4f21944\nparent 023d7e3e2da87e295fd3377a5ff7c1e5f0d219f7\nauthor Fahim Shahriar <44846872+qwertyz15@users.noreply.github.com> 1790020432 +0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790020432 +0600\n\nFeat/cleanup #6 (#14)\n\n* feat(onboarding): drop the tutorial step and its Postiz video\n\n/launches?onboarding=true embedded youtube.com/embed/BdsCVvEYgHU, which is\nPostiz''s tutorial, not ours.\n\nIt was not a stray iframe: the modal was a two step wizard and step two was\nthe tutorial, so removing the video meant removing the step. Gone with it:\nOnboardingStep2 in full, and the \"1 Connect Channels / 2 Watch Tutorial\"\nindicator row, which says nothing once there is one step.\n\nThe modal now renders OnboardingStep1 directly and step one''s button\nfinishes instead of advancing, calling onClose, which already closes the\nmodal and drops the onboarding query param. Its label reuses keys already\npresent in all sixteen locales, so no translation file changes:\n\n  channels connected  get_started               \"Get Started\"\n  none                continue_without_channels \"Continue without channels\"\n\nStep one is otherwise untouched: AddProviderComponent, the connected\nchannel list, the copy and the orange CTA all stay as they were.\n\nAlso drops what only the removed markup used: the onSkip prop, which was\ndeclared and destructured but never referenced, and the useState and clsx\nimports.\n\nThe same video is still embedded in first.billing.component.tsx, behind the\nwatch-the-video link on the free tier billing screen. Left alone, since this\nwas scoped to the onboarding route. The three watch_tutorial* locale keys\nare orphaned for now and kept until that one is settled.\n\n* chore: remove the Postiz tutorial video from the remaining surfaces\n\nFollows 75cbec56, which took it out of onboarding. youtube.com/embed/\nBdsCVvEYgHU is Postiz''s tutorial and was still embedded in two more places.\n\nBilling screen, the free tier upsell: the showYouTube handler and the\ntrigger behind it, a YouTube icon reading \"See the power of Postaryx\n(click here)\". Drops what only that used: the modals binding and the\nuseModals and SafeImage imports.\n\nREADME: the \"Watch the YouTube Tutorials\" link, and the \"See the leading\nPostaryx features\" block, which was a clickable thumbnail with the same\nvideo behind it. That also drops an upstream github user-attachments\nimage, so if a static Postaryx screenshot is wanted there, that block is\nwhere it goes.\n\nPure deletions, 44 lines, nothing added. A repo-wide sweep for\nBdsCVvEYgHU, youtube.com/embed, youtu.be and iframe now returns nothing.\n\nThe watch_tutorial, watch_tutorial_title and watch_tutorial_description\nkeys are left orphaned in all sixteen locales plus i18n.lock. Clearing\nthem touches seventeen files including a lockfile, which is a different\nkind of change from pulling a video.\n\n* chore(i18n): drop the orphaned watch_tutorial keys\n\nCompletes 75cbec56 and 0a3590b4, which removed the Postiz tutorial video\nfrom onboarding, the billing screen and the README. The keys that labelled\nit had no call sites left:\n\n  watch_tutorial\n  watch_tutorial_title\n  watch_tutorial_description\n\nRemoved from the fifteen locales that carried them, three lines each, plus\ntheir three hashes in i18n.lock. ka_ge never had them; it is a partial\ntranslation at 505 keys against the others'' 691.\n\nLine-based removal rather than a json round trip, so formatting is\nuntouched and the diff is 48 deletions with nothing added. Every locale\nre-parses as JSON and each of the fifteen lost exactly three keys. A\nrepo-wide grep for watch_tutorial now returns nothing.\n\nLeft alone: \"back\" and \"get_started\", which the removed step also used but\nwhich are still called from third-party.media-library.tsx and the\nonboarding CTA respectively.\n\nAlso noticed but not removed: \"continue\" is now orphaned too, since\n75cbec56 moved the onboarding CTA from it to get_started. It is a generic\nlabel worth keeping for reuse, and it is outside what this change is for.\n\n* fix(billing): ground the onboarding billing copy in what the code does\n\nThe page a FREE tier user lands on at /launches?onboarding=true, which is\nFirstBillingComponent replacing the shell rather than the onboarding modal,\ncarried inherited claims. Each was checked against the implementation\nbefore rewriting.\n\nFalse, removed:\n\n- \"To confirm credit card information Postaryx will hold $2 and release it\n  immediately\". No such code exists. A specific, checkable and wrong\n  statement about charging a customer''s card, shown in sixteen languages.\n- \"Join Over 20,000+ Entrepreneurs\". Unverifiable social proof.\n- \"proudly open-source ... will live forever\". Cannot be substantiated from\n  here, and inherited from upstream.\n- \"100% No-Risk Free Trial\" and \"Pay NOTHING for the first 7-days\".\n\nTrue, and now stated plainly:\n\n  7 day trial            stripe.service.ts:473,534 trial_period_days: 7\n  card required up front checkout.sessions.create, mode: ''subscription''\n  access to period end   stripe.service.ts:356 cancel_at_period_end: true\n  Stripe processes       database.module.ts:77, Polar is parked\n  named platforms        all present in the 33 registered providers\n\nHero becomes \"Grow Your Social Presence with Postaryx\". Trial bullets state\nthe length, that a payment method is required with no charge during the\ntrial, and that cancelling is self serve. The FAQ now answers the trial\ncharge, cancellation, and trust questions factually, and gains a \"Can I\ncancel anytime?\" entry matching cancel_at_period_end.\n\nChanging only the English fallbacks would have left the other fifteen\nlanguages still serving the $2 claim, since every claim-bearing key has\nlocale values. So these use new keys and the twelve superseded ones are\ndeleted from all sixteen locales and i18n.lock. The new keys have no locale\nentries yet, so every language renders the accurate English fallback until\nthe i18n pipeline is re-run. That is deliberate: accurate English beats\ninaccurate localised billing terms.\n\nAlso drops isGeneral ? ''Postaryx'' : ''Postaryx'', dead since the rename, and\nthe useVariables import it needed.\n\nLayout, pricing cards, FAQ accordion and dark theme are untouched.\n\nThe copy now asserts things the Terms and Refund Policy should agree with.\nVerified against code, not against those pages.\n\n* feat(header): hide the Developers entry point behind a flag\n\nThe developer portal is not exposed publicly yet, so the \"Developers\" item\nin the header should not render. Nothing is deleted.\n\nGuarded inside DeveloperIconComponent with SHOW_DEVELOPER_PORTAL = false\nand an early return, rather than commenting out the call site. It mounts in\nexactly one place today, the billing and onboarding header in\nfirst.billing.component.tsx; the main app header never had it. Guarding at\nthe component keeps it hidden in any layout that mounts it later too, which\nis what hiding it consistently actually needs. Both hooks run before the\nearly return, so hook order is unchanged.\n\nFlipping the constant to true restores it.\n\nUntouched: developer.component.tsx and the modal it fills, the public API\ncomponent, apps/backend/src/public-api and its routes, API keys, OAuth apps,\nMCP and the CLI docs. Header design, logo, theme toggle, language selector\nand every other nav item are also unchanged.\n\nNot touched, and worth a decision: Settings has a second \"Developers\" entry\nat settings.component.tsx:107, gated on user.tier.public_api && isGeneral,\nwhich opens the same public API surface. This change was scoped to the\nheader, but the same reasoning applies to that tab.\n\n* style(billing): soften the FAQ card border to the app''s standard token\n\nThe FAQ accordion used border-tableBorder, which resolves through two\naliases to a value that is only heavy in dark:\n\n  tableBorder -> --color-table-border -> --new-table-border\n                                         #c2410c dark, #e7e3db light\n\nAgainst the card''s #24211c that is contrast 3.10 at 88% saturation, a hard\norange outline next to every other dark card.\n\nSwitched to newBorder, #4e2f1f dark and #e7e3db light, giving 1.34 against\nthe same background, which sits next to the canonical card''s 1.42 against\n#1f1c17. That is why the two now read as one system. newBorder is also the\nmost used border token in the app, 24 call sites against tableBorder''s 17,\nso this is reuse rather than a new FAQ-specific value.\n\nLight is byte identical: both tokens resolve to #e7e3db there.\n\nUnchanged: layout, accordion behaviour, text, spacing, typography,\nrounded-[8px], and bg-sixth, which resolves to --new-table-header, the same\nsurface the third-party and plugs cards already use. No hover or open-state\naccent was added; there is none today and adding one would be a redesign.\n\nNot touched, same defect: twenty-three other files still use\nborder-tableBorder, including the calendar, comments, date picker and the\nprovider panels, so they carry the same #c2410c outline in dark.\n\n* style(billing): bring the pricing cards onto the design system\n\nThe billing page read as an older internal layout mostly because of the\npricing card, which carried three problems in one className.\n\nRadius: rounded-[4px]. global.scss only remaps 8, 12 and 16px onto the\n--app-radius-* scale, so 4px rendered literally and every card sat almost\nsquare next to the 12px cards everywhere else. Now rounded-[12px].\n\nBorder: border-customColor6, a deprecated --color-custom* token that\nCLAUDE.md flags, resolving to #6f3f2c in dark. Against the card''s #24211c\nthat is 1.85, heavier than any other dark card. Now border-newBorder,\n#4e2f1f, 1.34, the same token and weight as the canonical card.\n\nSelected state: there was none. currentPackage was already computed for the\nbutton logic but nothing showed it. The current plan now takes\nborder-cardAccentBorder, rgba(194, 65, 12, 0.3), the same subtle accent the\nauth card uses. Orange is therefore confined to CTAs and the active state\nrather than being the default card outline.\n\nBoth tokens already existed; nothing new was introduced, and clsx was\nalready imported.\n\nThe FAQ needed nothing: this page renders the same FAQComponent fixed in\n842cd5c8, where the border went from tableBorder #c2410c at 3.10 to\nnewBorder at 1.34.\n\nLogout was checked and deliberately left alone. Spacing is not the problem,\nthere is already about 60px of separation. LogoutComponent renders a bare\ndiv with unstyled text, so it reads as stray copy, and it is shared with the\nheader, which puts a proper fix outside a presentation-only change here.\n\nNo billing logic, Stripe, checkout, pricing data, purchase action, toggle or\nFAQ content was touched; the diff is one className.\n\n* feat(nav): hide the Affiliate item from the sidebar\n\nPostaryx is not running an affiliate programme yet, so the entry should not\nrender. Nothing is deleted.\n\nThe menu already had the mechanism for this: MenuItem declares hide?:\nboolean and both filter passes, firstMenu at line 330 and secondMenu at\n358, return false on it. So this is one flag on the Affiliate entry rather\nthan commenting out fifty-eight lines, most of which are its inline svg.\nAffiliate sits in secondMenu; the flag would work in either.\n\nThat covers every nav surface. TopMenu renders once, from\nnew-layout/layout.component.tsx, and there is no separate mobile nav. The\nonly other consumer is title.tsx, which resolves the page heading by\nmatching the route against item.path, and Affiliate''s path is an external\nurl that no route matches.\n\nUntouched: analytics, media, plugs, integrations, UGC, billing, settings.\n\nTwo things found while doing this. There is no affiliate functionality to\npreserve: frontend routes, components, backend and the prisma schema are\nall empty of it, and this menu entry was the only reference in the repo\noutside the locale files. And the entry''s path points at\ngithub.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza rather than an affiliate page,\ninherited from upstream and repointed during the rename, so it needs a real\ndestination before it is ever shown again. Both are noted in the comment.\n\nThe affiliate translation key stays in all sixteen locales, unused but\nready if the item is re-enabled.\n\n* feat(settings): hide the Developers tab behind a flag\n\nCompletes 282563d3, which hid the header entry point. Settings offered a\nsecond route to the same public API surface via its Developers tab.\n\nGated the arr.push on SHOW_DEVELOPER_PORTAL = false, matching the header\nflag''s name and shape, with each comment pointing at the other so the pair\nis re-enabled together.\n\nGating the push alone is enough. tab is useState(''global_settings'') and its\nonly writer is setTab(tabKey) on a tab click, with no url sync or other\nentry point, so with ''api'' absent from the list it can never become active.\nThe tab body is left exactly as written and is simply unreachable.\n\nNothing deleted: PublicComponent, developer.component.tsx,\napps/backend/src/public-api, the tab body, API keys, OAuth apps and MCP are\nall intact. Global Settings, Teams, Webhooks, Auto Post, Sets, Signatures\nand Approved Apps are untouched.\n\nThere are now two independent SHOW_DEVELOPER_PORTAL constants, here and in\ndeveloper/developer.icon.component.tsx. Kept local rather than sharing one\nexport, since the alternatives were importing a constant from an icon\ncomponent or adding a file for a single boolean. They can drift; a small\nfeature-flags module would consolidate them if more of these appear.\n\n* docs(security): rewrite the security policy for Postaryx\n\nThe file was upstream''s verbatim. It introduced itself as \"Postiz\n(gitroomhq)\", scoped itself to github.com/gitroomhq/postiz-app, pointed\nreporters at upstream''s GitHub Security Advisories, and named an upstream\nmaintainer''s personal address, egelhaus@ennogelhaus.de, as the urgent\ncontact.\n\nThat is a security defect rather than a branding one: anyone finding a flaw\nin Postaryx would have disclosed it to a third party, and the address is\nnot ours to publish.\n\nRewritten for Postaryx, operated by Lunark Dynamics LLC. Every identifier\nasserted is one already established in the repo:\n\n  app.postaryx.com                       .env.example:45\n  api.postaryx.com                       .env.example:31\n  github.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza  22 references\n  ghcr.io/aitechnologysys-sys            docker-compose.yaml:28\n  Lunark Dynamics LLC                    docs/12-AUG-3 and docs/2.\n\nTwo judgement calls.\n\nNo security address was given, so this uses security@postaryx.com,\nfollowing the support@postaryx.com convention in .env.example:33. The\nmailbox has to exist and be monitored before this is published: a policy\npointing at a dead address is worse than none, because reporters will\nassume they have told us and may publish when we do not answer.\n\nAll response timelines are gone and nothing replaces them. Upstream\ncommitted to 72 hour acknowledgement, 7 day triage, 90 and 180 day\nremediation and 24 hour CVE publication; none of those are ours to\npromise. \"What happens next\" describes the sequence without a clock. Add\nreal numbers once we know what we can honour.\n\nScope now names our four surfaces and rules out self-hosted infrastructure\nand the third-party platforms we integrate with, which matters with 33\nproviders or researchers will send us Instagram bugs. Email is the primary\nchannel with advisories as an alternative, since advisories are useless to\nan external reporter if the repository is private. Also adds a line asking\nresearchers not to test against other users'' accounts, and an offer of\ncredit.\n\nNo application code touched.\n\n* docs(readme): clear inherited upstream references and broken links\n\nRemoved, all upstream''s and two of them untrue:\n\n- opencollective.com/postiz, a live donation link on our README paying\n  upstream. .github/FUNDING.yaml was neutralised earlier but this was\n  missed.\n- The whole Sponsor section. Its pitch claimed \"almost 3m downloads and 20k\n  views per month\" and \"Website has 20k hits\", which are upstream''s\n  numbers presented as ours, the same class of claim removed from billing\n  in be75e9fd. FUNDING.yaml is deliberately all-commented, so there is no\n  Postaryx funding destination to point at either.\n- The G2 badge, which collected product reviews for Postiz''s G2 page.\n- The Snyk badge, served from snyk-labs/secure-developer-sample-repo. That\n  is a sample repository''s badge, not a scan of this project, so it was a\n  misleading security signal.\n- \"Join Our Discord (devs only)\", which linked to postaryx.com rather than\n  any Discord, and NEXT_PUBLIC_DISCORD_SUPPORT is empty so no server\n  exists.\n\nRepointed:\n\n- The fourteen social icons. They pointed at\n  github.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/svgs/socials/*.svg, but svgs/ does\n  not exist in this repo, it is upstream''s, and that url form is not a raw\n  path in any case. A rename had swapped the org without checking the\n  target, leaving fourteen broken images. Now repo-relative paths to\n  apps/frontend/public/icons/platforms/*.png, which exist and render on\n  GitHub without depending on repo visibility or branch.\n- Star History, which charted postaryx/postiz-app. That repo does not\n  exist, so the chart was also broken. Now aitechnologysys-sys/veroza.\n- The Hostinger sponsor link, off Postiz''s landing page to hostinger.com,\n  keeping ?ref=postaryx since that suggests a real affiliate code.\n\nVerified afterwards: no Postiz or Gitroom string remains, all fifteen\nimage sources resolve, and all thirteen relative doc links resolve.\n\nLicense attribution and installation instructions are untouched.\n\nWorth confirming separately: Hostinger and Virlo were both inherited from\nupstream''s sponsor list, so the table should go if they do not actually\nsponsor Postaryx.\n\n* docs(security): point disclosures at a mailbox that exists\n\n07fae5ac used security@postaryx.com, inferred from the\nsupport@postaryx.com convention in .env.example since no address had been\ngiven. That mailbox does not exist. A disclosure policy naming a dead\naddress is worse than none: reporters assume they have told us and may\npublish when nothing comes back.\n\nOf the two addresses that do exist, admin@ rather than support@. A\nvulnerability report should not land in a customer support queue, where it\ncan be triaged as an ordinary ticket by someone without the context or\nauthority to act, and where the ticket system widens who can read an\nunpatched exploit.\n\nWorth adding later: security@ is the address researchers look for by\nconvention, and what security.txt and most disclosure tooling expect. An\nalias to admin@ costs nothing and catches anyone who guesses it.\n\n* docs(contributing): rewrite for Postaryx and drop dead upstream links\n\nEvery destination the page pointed at was upstream''s, and none has a\nPostaryx equivalent anywhere in the repo:\n\n  docs.postiz.com/developer-guide   x2, the \"read this first\" link\n  contribute.postiz.com/p/postiz    a contribution form we do not run\n  discord.postiz.com                x2, NEXT_PUBLIC_DISCORD_SUPPORT is empty\n  docs.postiz.com/support           a support page we do not run\n  git clone .../postiz.git          wrong repository name\n\nSince there is genuinely no public contribution workflow, no docs site, no\nchat and no form, the page now says so in the opening paragraph rather\nthan implying infrastructure we do not have. It then describes only what\nworks today: GitHub issues, and SECURITY.md for vulnerabilities. Links go\nto documents that exist, CLAUDE.md, docs/LOCAL-DEVELOPMENT.md and\ndocs/RUNNING-DEV-AND-PROD.md, all six verified to resolve.\n\nUpstream''s \"under 3 lines, just send it\" heuristic is replaced by asking\nfor an issue before substantial work, since that rule relied on a Discord\nwe do not run.\n\nKept: the fork, branch, pull request mechanics, with the clone url fixed\nto veroza.git, and the existing stance on AI-generated pull requests,\nreworded but not softened, since changing that policy was not asked for.\nAdded an explicit note that contributions are licensed AGPL-3.0.\n\nFlagged separately, not changed here: CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:63 still routes\nconduct reports to nevo@gitroom.com, upstream''s founder. That is the same\ndefect fixed in SECURITY.md by 07fae5ac and wants the same treatment. This\npage links to the Code of Conduct because contributors should know one\napplies.\n\n* chore(git): drop the stale gitroomhq public-api submodule\n\n.gitmodules declared a submodule at libraries/plugins/src/list/public-api\npointing at git@github.com:gitroomhq/public-api.git. Nothing in this repo\nuses it:\n\n- libraries/plugins does not exist on disk\n- no gitlink (mode 160000) in the index, and zero tracked files under\n  that path\n- .git/config has no [submodule] section and there is no .git/modules\n- git submodule status is empty\n- no source file imports @gitroom/plugins\n- no CI workflow checks out with submodules\n\nSo `git submodule update --init` was a no-op that only ever produced a\nfailed clone for anyone who ran it.\n\nLeft in place deliberately, as they are a separate concern: the dead\n@gitroom/plugins path aliases in tsconfig.base.json and\napps/orchestrator/.swcrc, and the .gitignore entry for\nlibraries/plugins/src/plugins.ts.\n\nRecorded in docs/UPSTREAM-SYNC.md so a merge that restores the file is\nresolved as a delete/modify conflict rather than silently reinstating\nthe submodule.\n\n* chore(config): drop the dead @gitroom/plugins path aliases\n\nBoth tsconfig.base.json and apps/orchestrator/.swcrc mapped\n@gitroom/plugins/* to libraries/plugins/src/*, a directory that does not\nexist in this repo. It went away with the gitroomhq/public-api submodule\nremoved in the previous commit; nothing imports through the alias, so the\nmappings only resolved to a missing path.\n\nVerified: zero occurrences of @gitroom/plugins outside these two files,\nand both `pnpm build:backend` and `pnpm build:orchestrator` succeed.\n\nStill dead, left for a separate pass: apps/orchestrator/.swcrc also\naliases @gitroom/cron and @gitroom/workers to apps/cron and apps/workers\n(neither exists) and sets baseUrl to an absolute path from an upstream\ndeveloper''s machine. The whole file is unused anyway — apps/orchestrator/\nnest-cli.json does not set the swc builder, so `nest build` compiles with\ntsc. .gitignore also still ignores libraries/plugins/src/plugins.ts.\n\n* docs(readme): drop the inherited product showcase sections\n\nThree blocks carried over from upstream, none of which describe this\nfork:\n\n- \"✨ Features\" — a 2x2 table of four upstream product screenshots\n  hosted on github.com/user-attachments.\n- \"Our Sponsors\" — Hostinger and Virlo, upstream''s sponsors rather than\n  ours. Both referral links had been caught by the blanket rename and\n  read ?ref=postaryx, a code neither company issued.\n- The \"check out Postaryx agent CLI! perfect for OpenClaw and other\n  agents\" banner. No such CLI exists here — apps/ is backend, commands,\n  extension, frontend, orchestrator, sdk, and \"OpenClaw\" appeared\n  nowhere else in the tree. Another blanket-rename artefact, pointing at\n  postaryx.com rather than at any CLI.\n\nVerified afterwards: every remaining local image and link target\nresolves on disk (14 platform icons, 15 doc/file links), and no\nreference to the removed sections survives.\n\n.github/sponsors/hostinger.png is now unreferenced; left in place as\nthis commit touches README.md only.\n\n* docs(readme): use the Postaryx logo and strip the inherited hero\n\nThe header still served the purple Postiz wordmark from\ngithub.com/user-attachments behind an alt of \"Postaryx Logo\". Both\nscheme variants now point at the logo assets already in the repo.\nRasterised both to confirm the pairing rather than trusting the\nfilenames: \"Dark\"/\"Light\" names the background the asset is drawn for,\nthe same convention the app''s logo component uses.\n\nHero link rows removed in full — \"Explore the docs\", \"Register / Public\nAPI\", and \"NodeJS SDK / N8N custom node / Make.com integration\". All\nthree entries in that last row pointed at the same apps/sdk/README.md;\nthere is no N8N node and no Make.com integration in this repo.\n\nIntro now claims only what the product does:\n\n- dropped the \"alternative to Buffer.com, Hypefury, Twitter Hunter\"\n  positioning line\n- dropped \"exchange or buy posts\" — the marketplace does not exist here,\n  no reference in the frontend nav or the backend\n- dropped \"no difference between the hosted version to the self-hosted\n  version\", which is false: isBillingEnabled() gates channel, credit and\n  team-member limits, permission checks, the public API and the\n  publisher\n- \"automation with N8N, Make.com, Zapier\" -> the public API and the\n  NodeJS SDK, which is what actually ships\n\nVerified: no occurrence of postiz, gitroom or user-attachments remains,\nall 16 local image references and all 19 link targets resolve.\n\nLicense badge, LICENSE link, Tech Stack, Quick Start, Compliance and the\ndeployment runbook are untouched.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsYtQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOlcQAHIglx0dwnZi7cEEA3XFF29i\nu+4WK2Ak//fCBw6tUy38thudi5aYDmTkanIudaMORdA9A2TYwxB47TvJoBoQgjxq\nnjciGWW8GE6mUL8Oo0rH7lUXgJJN9g2C5KHznVojd+oPqt8Iee8gB5FQGJp2EY22\n9CpQ34QyS08iWNgCycryLkjIBvjqNzXYDE5K1nbI/81IxU87YaHsjnluaaxurbNq\nIT7H2LLTDJ2uI+CtC3Ed8cyCliWNfjqMVxrNbhxE9E++CaJYik+Em472vYwrUp6V\n9IyDG20wBfmw7Jd1BJmNWwSXoxJa+ZfGx15DQO0nRsGiaWyvGpbat3gPcunqIXUs\ncxvV56M2uJZwQ4ySFE9Vgy8aFiHT/fSNrxwBPC/xYs6XLSPbDKwFvRVdTgQ35IG0\nxZnsgQQ0e/UhBKDnyLwIWUT5rmjLIEQlRtno9PbrKwA+JCpdkr7nNQgYPaPrPn7K\nrP0HUryc//IlO0QV0UmIf5/Jwpi6qNwXPofXptTfeWQtLjz6ManXz0ZwYO9dAJ/R\nmXAprNA7jUpXIiO/yYPlyjJtm7G/fqTJgKNmUTdaMtcyq8PwsEIMZqEKPrjdbS4F\n78keGJPHiT0zosTd0D8pByn0iaulFLHiwnKnbQ9rxmlc3obi7dGDyc2Pt3O6wdMx\nrbR6SGup0JWPc/PweDth\n=oACx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T19:53:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admi