pi.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/8214279444b68704e67468f55084055d78390f48"}],"sha":"ec16d6d4674661fa4bbb4da1bb4e148cdfc1902b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/ec16d6d4674661fa4bbb4da1bb4e148cdfc1902b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44846872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qwertyz15","id":44846872,"login":"qwertyz15","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODQ2ODcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qwertyz15","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/8214279444b68704e67468f55084055d78390f48/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T17:18:02Z","email":"44846872+qwertyz15@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Fahim Shahriar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T17:18:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Chore/rebrand #5 (#11)\n\n* style: replace purple accents with orange\n\n* style: align create post buttons with product design system\n\n* style: align developers page typography with design system\n\n* fix the plug tab\n\n* integration tab fixed\n\n* fix(privacy): erase credentials on disconnect and media on delete\n\nDisconnecting a channel set deletedAt and nothing else, leaving a live\nplaintext access token and refresh token in Postgres indefinitely.\nDeleting media retired the row but never removed the object: removeFile()\nwas implemented on both providers and called from nowhere, and on R2 it\nwas a commented-out stub that resolved without doing anything.\n\n- Clear token, refreshToken and tokenExpiration in the same write as\n  deletedAt, so a disconnect cannot half-apply\n- Attempt upstream revocation before the erase, via an optional\n  revokeToken hook on the provider; implemented for YouTube and Facebook,\n  skipped silently elsewhere\n- Remove the stored object and its thumbnail before retiring a media row\n- Implement removeFile on R2, and map the stored public URL back to a\n  path on disk for local storage, refusing anything that resolves\n  outside the upload directory\n- Add DeletionService with the revoke-then-erase and purge primitives an\n  account or workspace deletion flow will need\n\nRevocation and storage removal are best-effort and logged: neither can\nblock the local erase. Token stays non-nullable and is blanked, so no\nschema migration is required.\n\n* chore(rebrand): replace Postiz logos and favicon with Postaryx\n\nSwap the remaining Postiz brand marks for the official Postaryx assets,\nadded under apps/frontend/public/logos.\n\n- The sidebar/OAuth/billing icon and the auth + billing wordmark were\n  inline Postiz SVGs, not file references. Both now use the Postaryx\n  assets and pick the variant that contrasts with the surface via the\n  .dark/.light body class.\n- The post preview header used a recoloured Postiz mark plus an inline\n  Postiz wordmark; replaced with the single Postaryx lockup.\n- favicon.ico and favicon.png regenerated from the Postaryx app icon.\n- Drop unreferenced Postiz assets that were still publicly servable:\n  logo.svg, logo-text.svg, postiz-text.svg, postiz-fav.png and\n  postaryx.svg (which was the Postiz mark recoloured, not a Postaryx logo).\n\nDimensions, classes and spacing are unchanged.\n\n* style(rebrand): recolour illustrations from Postiz purple to Postaryx orange\n\nEmpty-state and marketing illustrations still carried the Postiz purple\npalette.\n\n- #8155DD -> #C2410C (brand primary, from the logo assets)\n- #6C63FF -> #A9711F (brand amber, from the logo assets)\n- #E7DDFE -> #F4E7DF (light surface token, --new-boxFocused)\n- #DACBFB -> #F2D5CA (22% tint of #C2410C)\n\nThe branding files have no second light orange far enough from #F4E7DF to\nkeep the tile hierarchy in no-channels-colors.svg, so the deeper tint is\nderived from the brand primary: hue 16.5 deg against the brand''s 17.5, and\na 4.5pp lightness gap matching the original 4.1pp.\n\nAlso covers NoMediaIcon, an inline copy of the same artwork rendered by\nthe media page, which the file-level change did not reach.\n\nOnly colour values changed: masking every hex and diffing against the\nprevious revision is identical, so path data, dimensions, gradients and\nopacity are untouched. Third-party brand purples are deliberately kept\n(Stripe #635BFF, Farcaster #7C65C1).\n\n* fix(media): use the button radius on the upload buttons\n\nThe Upload button was on rounded-[8px], which is --radius-control (the\nradius for inputs), not --radius-button. Most bg-btnSimple/bg-btnPrimary\nbuttons in the app are rounded-[10px].\n\nAlso fixes the ThirdPartyMediaLibrary button, which renders directly\nbeside Upload in the same flex row with identical classes, so changing\nonly one would have left two adjacent buttons with different corners.\n\nThe search input beside them stays at 8px, which is correct for a control.\n\n* chore: track Postaryx brand logos, ignore local uploads\n\nAdd postaryx-logos/ as the master brand asset set. These are currently\nbyte-identical to apps/frontend/public/logos/, which is the copy the\nfrontend actually serves.\n\nIgnore /uploads/, the media directory written at runtime. The pattern is\nroot-anchored so the api/uploads route under apps/frontend is unaffected.\nOne upload had already been committed, so it is untracked here as well,\notherwise the ignore would not apply to it. The file stays on disk.\n\n* fix(theme): give cards a visible hover in dark mode on plugs and integrations\n\nThe cards on both pages use bg-newTableHeader hover:bg-boxHover, and in\nthe dark block --new-table-header and --new-box-hover are both #24211c.\nThe hover painted the card its own colour, so it was a no-op: contrast\nratio 1.000 against 1.081 in light, which is why only dark looked broken.\n\nAdd a --new-card-hover token rather than hardcoding a hex in the\ncomponents or retuning --new-box-hover, which is shared with about\n25 buttons. In light it is #f4f1ea, the value --new-box-hover already\nhad, so light renders identically. In dark it is #2e2a24, hue 36deg,\nmatching the existing dark surface ramp (#1f1c17 and #24211c at 38deg,\n#2a2620 at 36deg) so the elevation stays warm rather than grey.\n\nContrast against the rest state:\n\n  card          light 1.081 -> 1.081 (unchanged)\n  card          dark  1.000 -> 1.125\n  selector item light 1.128 -> 1.128 (unchanged)\n  selector item dark  1.059 -> 1.191\n\nDark sits slightly above light, which is what dark surfaces need to read\nas the same step.\n\nAlso brings the plugs card in line with the integrations card, which\nalready had cursor-pointer and a transition; the plugs card is clickable\nbut showed a plain arrow and snapped instantly.\n\nNo layout, dimension, spacing or typography changes.\n\n* style(settings): align the settings page with the design system\n\nThe settings page was not drifting from the app generally, it was\ndrifting from its own developers tab. 03bbad33 aligned that tab; the\nother seven still used the pre-alignment pattern, so moving between\nGlobal Settings and Developers crossed two visual languages inside one\npage. That commit is the reference used here.\n\nCards, 11 containers across nine tabs:\n\n  bg-sixth border-fifth rounded-[4px] p-[24px]\n  -> bg-newBgColorInner border border-newBorder rounded-[12px] p-[20px]\n\nmatching the developers tab and --radius-card. A redundant\nmy-[16px] mt-[16px] is collapsed to my-[16px]; internal gaps are left as\nthey were.\n\nMuted text, 14 occurrences: text-customColor18 -> text-textItemBlur.\n--color-custom18 is #5f5b52 in dark but #191712 in light, so every\ndescription line rendered near black in the light theme, as prominent as\nthe label above it. textItemBlur is #5f5b52 in both. CLAUDE.md already\nmarks --color-custom* deprecated.\n\nShell: sidebar gains gap-[15px] and the text-[20px] font-[500] heading\nthat plugs and integrations both have; tab hover and active state move\nfrom bg-boxHover to bg-cardHover, which is a no-op in dark; the free-tier\nmodal wrapper moves onto the canonical card.\n\nApproved apps: row border-fifth rounded-[4px] -> border-newBorder\nrounded-[8px], and the avatar chip bg-fifth -> bg-newColColor, since\nbg-fifth is #6f3f2c in dark and held #5f5b52 initials at about 1.4:1.\n\nSidebar tab dimensions are unchanged: SVGLine is a fixed 52px svg, so\nthose rows already matched plugs and integrations at 52px.\n\nModal internals opened from settings are left alone, as are the\nstructural header and body split of the canonical card and\ngithub.component, which onboarding owns.\n\n* fix(theme): restore the radius scale and soften the dark card border\n\nRadius, app-wide. global.scss remaps three tailwind utilities onto custom\nproperties:\n\n  .rounded-[8px]  { border-radius: var(--app-radius-control) }\n  .rounded-[12px] { border-radius: var(--app-radius-card) }\n  .rounded-[16px] { border-radius: var(--app-radius-panel) }\n\nand builds those at :root from --radius-*. But --radius-* was declared\ninside .dark and .light, which sit on body, a descendant of :root. Custom\nproperties inherit downward, so at :root the variable did not exist, the\nfallback-less var() made the declaration invalid at computed-value time,\nand border-radius fell back to its initial value of 0.\n\nMeasured in chrome against the compiled stylesheet:\n\n  before   card=0px    ctl=0px   btn=10px   panel=0px\n  after    card=12px   ctl=8px   btn=10px   panel=16px\n\nButtons were unaffected because they use rounded-[10px], which is never\nremapped. That asymmetry, rounded buttons next to square cards, is what\npointed at the cause.\n\nThe values are identical in both themes, so they were never\ntheme-dependent; they move to :root where they are read. The per-theme\ncopies stay, overriding with the same values, so the hooks remain if\ntheme-specific radii are ever wanted. No markup changed: the cards\nalready asked for rounded-[12px] and the request was being dropped.\n\nThis reaches 108 rounded-[8px], 53 rounded-[12px] and 14 rounded-[16px]\nusages across the app, not just settings. Settings only made it obvious\nbecause that is where the large cards are. Worth a look at a couple of\nother pages before this ships.\n\nBorder: --new-border in dark goes from #c2410c to #4e2f1f. Against the\ncard background that is 3.28 down to 1.42, against 1.28 for the light\ntheme, which was already a soft hairline and is untouched. #4e2f1f is\nalready in the palette as --new-ai-btn, --color-seventh, --color-custom4\nand --color-custom30, at hue 20.4deg against the brand''s 17.5, so the\norange identity is kept rather than replaced with a neutral. --new-border\nfeeds only newBorder, used as card borders and dividers, never as an\nactive or accent indicator.\n\nAlso rounds the signature and autopost editors, which were square and\n4px, to the 8px control radius, and moves their wrappers and the teams\nbadge off the legacy custom* border tokens.\n\n* chore(rebrand): clear the last user-facing Postiz branding\n\ngrep -R \"Postiz\" over the frontend now returns nothing. Of the 40\noccurrences audited across src and the shared libraries, four were actual\nproduct branding:\n\n- the developers tab label, N8N Node (Postiz-compatible) ->\n  (Postaryx-compatible). The linked package is still n8n-nodes-postiz, so\n  the wording describes compatibility rather than ownership, which is\n  accurate until a Postaryx node is published.\n- the sentry app context name, Postiz Frontend -> Postaryx Frontend. This\n  is a display field; the service: ''frontend'' tag that alerts filter on is\n  untouched and grouping is by dsn.\n- the linkedin url placeholder, which still showed the upstream org\n  linkedin.com/company/gitroom.\n- the testimonial marquee on sign in and sign up, removed. Eight of the\n  sixteen quotes named Postiz and all sixteen are attributed to named\n  people with avatars, so rewriting the product name inside them would\n  have put words in real people''s mouths. Removing the block was chosen\n  instead of fabricating endorsements.\n\nDeliberately left, none of it branding: eight i18n keys that are live in\nall sixteen locale files and whose displayed text already reads Postaryx;\nthree POSTIZ_* env vars that are already back-compat fallbacks behind\nPOSTARYX_*; four external identifiers that would break if renamed, being\nthe @postiz/wallets import, the n8n npm url, the chrome web store listing\nand the postiz-agent skill; and one comment documenting the deliberate\ndivergence from upstream billing.\n\nRemoving the marquee orphans testimonial.component.tsx, testimonial.tsx,\nthe shared testomonials.tsx and seventeen avatars. They are left in place\nso the component can come back with real Postaryx quotes.\n\n* fix(auth): serve /logos through the proxy so the sign in logo loads\n\nThe logo showed a broken image placeholder on sign in and sign up. The\npath was already correct; the middleware was eating the request.\n\nproxy.ts redirects any non-/auth path without an auth cookie to /auth, and\nits matcher only exempts files at the root of /public:\n\n  ''/((?!api/|_next/|_static/|_vercel|[\\w-]+\\.\\w+).*)''\n\n[\\w-]+\\.\\w+ matches favicon.ico but not logos/x.svg, so the request\nreached the middleware, found no cookie on the logged-out auth page, and\nwas redirected. The img element received html instead of an svg.\n\nThis is a regression from 84b85bc6. The old logo sat at /postaryx.svg, at\nthe root, where the matcher exempted it; moving it into /logos/ lost that\nexemption. It only shows on sign in and sign up because that is the only\nplace a user has no cookie.\n\nFixed by adding /logos/ to the early-return allowlist a few lines up,\nwhere /icons/ already sits for the same reason. Verified against the\nsource: /logos/* is now allowlisted and served to a logged-out user.\n\nThe matcher will catch any future subdirectory under public the same way.\n/form/ is the only other one outside the allowlist and nothing references\nit. A general fix would be exempting .*\\.\\w+$ so files at any depth are\nskipped.\n\n* style(auth): centre the auth card and drop the empty hero column\n\nRemoving the testimonial marquee in 1b7c0f52 left the right-hand column\nholding only its heading, and a large empty area below it. The column and\nthe heading are removed, and the card is centred on both axes.\n\n  page wrapper  + items-center justify-center, - gap-[12px]\n  card column   - h-full\n\nh-full existed to fill a panel that stretched to full height; with the\npanel now sized by its content it resolved to auto anyway. gap-[12px] only\never spaced the two columns.\n\nMeasured in chrome:\n\n  1440x900   card x=420 w=600   420 left / 420 right   y=164 h=573  164 / 163\n  390x844    card x=12  w=366    12 / 12 gutters       y=136 h=573  136 / 135\n\nDesktop centres the fixed 600px card; below lg the card still takes the\nfull width with the 12px page gutter, since lg:flex-none does not apply\nthere. The card itself is untouched.\n\nThis layout is shared with forgot password, activate and login-required,\nwhich get the same centring.\n\nThe page stays hard-coded dark, as before: ModeComponent mounts only in\nthe app shell and the first-billing screen, never under /auth, so the body\nkeeps the server-rendered dark class whatever the mode cookie says.\nGiving the auth page a real light appearance means replacing those two\nhard-coded backgrounds, which is a redesign rather than a layout change.\n\n* style(auth): brand the sign in background with a contained orange halo\n\nThe page used neutral blacks, #0E0E0E behind #1A1919, both at hue 0. That\nis why it felt disconnected: nothing on it came from the Postaryx ramp.\n\nSurfaces move onto existing tokens:\n\n  page   bg-[#0E0E0E] -> bg-newBackdrop      #191712  hue 43\n  card   bg-[#1A1919] -> bg-newBgColorInner  #1f1c17  hue 38\n\nSwitching the card onto bg-newBgColorInner also picks up\n--preview-box-shadow, since global.scss already applies it to\n.bg-newBgColorInner.rounded-[12px] and the card was already rounded-[12px].\nThe brand surfaces have less raw separation than the old blacks, 1.055\nagainst 1.100, so the depth comes from that shadow and the outline rather\nthan a luminance step.\n\nTwo new tokens, both composited from rgb(194, 65, 12), which is\n--new-btn-primary, so the outline, the halo and the Sign In button are the\nsame orange:\n\n  --new-card-accent-border  rgba(..., 0.3), mapped as cardAccentBorder\n  --auth-ambient            the radial gradient, consumed by .auth-ambient\n\nThe border lands at contrast 1.33 against the card, between the 1.42 that\nread as too strong and the 1.13 that lost the brand entirely.\n\nThe halo is sized in px rather than left to farthest-corner. At the\ndefault, 100% is the viewport corner, 849px on 1440x900, so a stop at\n\"transparent 80%\" still reached 679px and tinted almost the whole page.\nWith ellipse 500px 380px the card edge sits at 68% and the falloff is\ndone by 250px out. Measured at mid-height, card spanning x=380..1060:\n\n  x=8    (25,23,18)   flat backdrop\n  x=280  (28,24,18)   warmth begins\n  x=375  (37,24,16)   peak, against the card\n  x=1220 (25,23,18)   flat backdrop\n\nAll four corners measure #191712 exactly. Five stops with a long tail to\ntransparent, so there is no visible ellipse edge.\n\nCard width goes 600 -> 680 with the inner form cap 440 -> 500, both about\n13%, so the gutters stay proportional and the form widens with the card\ninstead of gaining padding. Position, typography, form structure and\nbutton colours are unchanged.\n\n* chore(i18n): drop the last Gitroom strings from the ar and bn locales\n\nThe \"gitroom\" key is Arabic and Bengali transliterations of Gitroom, جيت روم\nand গিটরুম, while the other fourteen locales already resolve it to Postaryx.\nBoth now match.\n\nFound by scanning translation values rather than source: a grep over src\nonly sees the keys, which are identifiers, and every key whose name\ncontains postiz or gitroom already had a Postaryx value. These two were the\nonly values in any locale still carrying the old brand.\n\nNothing renders the key today, no call site passes ''gitroom'' to t(), so\nthis is dormant rather than live. Fixed anyway because it is translation\ndata that would surface the old name the moment the key is used, and\nbecause it was the last old-brand string left in the frontend.\n\n* fix(sidebar): match the app icon to the theme and drop its tile\n\nTwo problems with the sidebar icon.\n\nIt was paired the wrong way round: 03, the dark-theme icon, rendered in the\nlight theme and 04 in the dark one. That came from picking on tile-versus-\nbackground contrast, which is the wrong rule for a tiled app icon. The tile\nis meant to settle into the surrounding chrome and let the mark carry the\ncontrast, so maximising it put a white square on the dark sidebar. Now the\nasset named for a theme renders in that theme, the same convention the\nwordmark in logo-text.component.tsx already used.\n\nThe tiles then had to go. On the white sidebar 04''s white tile disappears\nand only its hairline shows, but on the dark sidebar 03''s #191712 tile\nreads as a distinct darker square against #1f1c17.\n\nAdds two transparent derivatives:\n\n  07_Postaryx_App_Icon_Dark_Transparent   03 minus its #191712 tile\n  08_Postaryx_App_Icon_Light_Transparent  04 minus its white fill and its\n                                          #E6E3DD border rect, which is a\n                                          second rect, not part of the first\n\nEach differs from its source by those rects alone; mark geometry, clip path\nand brand colours are byte-identical, and both land at 1346 bytes. Switching\ntheme now changes only the ink, not the icon''s form.\n\n03 and 04 are left untouched. They are the real app icons and the tile is\nthe point of them for the favicon, the PWA manifest and store listings.\n\n* fix(calendar): make the past-slot hatch visible in dark mode\n\n.repeated-strip was already token-driven, so it looked theme-aware, but in\ndark the two bands resolved to the same colour:\n\n  --new-bgColorInner  #1f1c17 dark / #ffffff light\n  --new-big-strips    #1f1c17 dark / #f4f1ea light\n\nThe gradient alternated #1f1c17 with #1f1c17 and painted a flat fill.\nContrast against the cell was 1.0000 in dark against 1.1280 in light, so\npast slots lost their unavailable treatment entirely rather than merely\nbeing faint. Same shape as the dark hover bug in 526398e9.\n\nRetuning --new-big-strips would have been the smaller diff but it is also\nbg-bigStrip on the signature editor textarea, so its dark value is load\nbearing elsewhere. Added --new-past-strip instead, which only\n.repeated-strip reads:\n\n  dark   #2a2620   ratio 1.1292\n  light  #f4f1ea   ratio 1.1280, the value --new-big-strips already resolved\n                   to, so light is byte identical\n\n#2a2620 is already in the palette, shared with --new-col-color,\n--new-blockSeparator and --new-boxFocused, and sits at hue 36 against the\nsurface ramp''s 38, so the hatch stays warm rather than reading as grey. Its\nratio lands within 0.001 of light''s, so neither theme carries more texture\nthan the other.\n\nDirection 135deg and the 4px/8px density are unchanged, no component file\nis touched, and calendar.tsx still gates the class on isBeforeNow alone, so\nonly past slots are affected.","tree":{"sha":"931910673998ff557ea3c95222dde98a0a001a2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/trees/931910673998ff557ea3c95222dde98a0a001a2e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/commits/8214279444b68704e67468f55084055d78390f48","verification":{"payload":"tree 931910673998ff557ea3c95222dde98a0a001a2e\nparent cfa091248ccfec5c92857d854c8688fca50e1988\nauthor Fahim Shahriar <44846872+qwertyz15@users.noreply.github.com> 1789838282 +0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789838282 +0600\n\nChore/rebrand #5 (#11)\n\n* style: replace purple accents with orange\n\n* style: align create post buttons with product design system\n\n* style: align developers page typography with design system\n\n* fix the plug tab\n\n* integration tab fixed\n\n* fix(privacy): erase credentials on disconnect and media on delete\n\nDisconnecting a channel set deletedAt and nothing else, leaving a live\nplaintext access token and refresh token in Postgres indefinitely.\nDeleting media retired the row but never removed the object: removeFile()\nwas implemented on both providers and called from nowhere, and on R2 it\nwas a commented-out stub that resolved without doing anything.\n\n- Clear token, refreshToken and tokenExpiration in the same write as\n  deletedAt, so a disconnect cannot half-apply\n- Attempt upstream revocation before the erase, via an optional\n  revokeToken hook on the provider; implemented for YouTube and Facebook,\n  skipped silently elsewhere\n- Remove the stored object and its thumbnail before retiring a media row\n- Implement removeFile on R2, and map the stored public URL back to a\n  path on disk for local storage, refusing anything that resolves\n  outside the upload directory\n- Add DeletionService with the revoke-then-erase and purge primitives an\n  account or workspace deletion flow will need\n\nRevocation and storage removal are best-effort and logged: neither can\nblock the local erase. Token stays non-nullable and is blanked, so no\nschema migration is required.\n\n* chore(rebrand): replace Postiz logos and favicon with Postaryx\n\nSwap the remaining Postiz brand marks for the official Postaryx assets,\nadded under apps/frontend/public/logos.\n\n- The sidebar/OAuth/billing icon and the auth + billing wordmark were\n  inline Postiz SVGs, not file references. Both now use the Postaryx\n  assets and pick the variant that contrasts with the surface via the\n  .dark/.light body class.\n- The post preview header used a recoloured Postiz mark plus an inline\n  Postiz wordmark; replaced with the single Postaryx lockup.\n- favicon.ico and favicon.png regenerated from the Postaryx app icon.\n- Drop unreferenced Postiz assets that were still publicly servable:\n  logo.svg, logo-text.svg, postiz-text.svg, postiz-fav.png and\n  postaryx.svg (which was the Postiz mark recoloured, not a Postaryx logo).\n\nDimensions, classes and spacing are unchanged.\n\n* style(rebrand): recolour illustrations from Postiz purple to Postaryx orange\n\nEmpty-state and marketing illustrations still carried the Postiz purple\npalette.\n\n- #8155DD -> #C2410C (brand primary, from the logo assets)\n- #6C63FF -> #A9711F (brand amber, from the logo assets)\n- #E7DDFE -> #F4E7DF (light surface token, --new-boxFocused)\n- #DACBFB -> #F2D5CA (22% tint of #C2410C)\n\nThe branding files have no second light orange far enough from #F4E7DF to\nkeep the tile hierarchy in no-channels-colors.svg, so the deeper tint is\nderived from the brand primary: hue 16.5 deg against the brand''s 17.5, and\na 4.5pp lightness gap matching the original 4.1pp.\n\nAlso covers NoMediaIcon, an inline copy of the same artwork rendered by\nthe media page, which the file-level change did not reach.\n\nOnly colour values changed: masking every hex and diffing against the\nprevious revision is identical, so path data, dimensions, gradients and\nopacity are untouched. Third-party brand purples are deliberately kept\n(Stripe #635BFF, Farcaster #7C65C1).\n\n* fix(media): use the button radius on the upload buttons\n\nThe Upload button was on rounded-[8px], which is --radius-control (the\nradius for inputs), not --radius-button. Most bg-btnSimple/bg-btnPrimary\nbuttons in the app are rounded-[10px].\n\nAlso fixes the ThirdPartyMediaLibrary button, which renders directly\nbeside Upload in the same flex row with identical classes, so changing\nonly one would have left two adjacent buttons with different corners.\n\nThe search input beside them stays at 8px, which is correct for a control.\n\n* chore: track Postaryx brand logos, ignore local uploads\n\nAdd postaryx-logos/ as the master brand asset set. These are currently\nbyte-identical to apps/frontend/public/logos/, which is the copy the\nfrontend actually serves.\n\nIgnore /uploads/, the media directory written at runtime. The pattern is\nroot-anchored so the api/uploads route under apps/frontend is unaffected.\nOne upload had already been committed, so it is untracked here as well,\notherwise the ignore would not apply to it. The file stays on disk.\n\n* fix(theme): give cards a visible hover in dark mode on plugs and integrations\n\nThe cards on both pages use bg-newTableHeader hover:bg-boxHover, and in\nthe dark block --new-table-header and --new-box-hover are both #24211c.\nThe hover painted the card its own colour, so it was a no-op: contrast\nratio 1.000 against 1.081 in light, which is why only dark looked broken.\n\nAdd a --new-card-hover token rather than hardcoding a hex in the\ncomponents or retuning --new-box-hover, which is shared with about\n25 buttons. In light it is #f4f1ea, the value --new-box-hover already\nhad, so light renders identically. In dark it is #2e2a24, hue 36deg,\nmatching the existing dark surface ramp (#1f1c17 and #24211c at 38deg,\n#2a2620 at 36deg) so the elevation stays warm rather than grey.\n\nContrast against the rest state:\n\n  card          light 1.081 -> 1.081 (unchanged)\n  card          dark  1.000 -> 1.125\n  selector item light 1.128 -> 1.128 (unchanged)\n  selector item dark  1.059 -> 1.191\n\nDark sits slightly above light, which is what dark surfaces need to read\nas the same step.\n\nAlso brings the plugs card in line with the integrations card, which\nalready had cursor-pointer and a transition; the plugs card is clickable\nbut showed a plain arrow and snapped instantly.\n\nNo layout, dimension, spacing or typography changes.\n\n* style(settings): align the settings page with the design system\n\nThe settings page was not drifting from the app generally, it was\ndrifting from its own developers tab. 03bbad33 aligned that tab; the\nother seven still used the pre-alignment pattern, so moving between\nGlobal Settings and Developers crossed two visual languages inside one\npage. That commit is the reference used here.\n\nCards, 11 containers across nine tabs:\n\n  bg-sixth border-fifth rounded-[4px] p-[24px]\n  -> bg-newBgColorInner border border-newBorder rounded-[12px] p-[20px]\n\nmatching the developers tab and --radius-card. A redundant\nmy-[16px] mt-[16px] is collapsed to my-[16px]; internal gaps are left as\nthey were.\n\nMuted text, 14 occurrences: text-customColor18 -> text-textItemBlur.\n--color-custom18 is #5f5b52 in dark but #191712 in light, so every\ndescription line rendered near black in the light theme, as prominent as\nthe label above it. textItemBlur is #5f5b52 in both. CLAUDE.md already\nmarks --color-custom* deprecated.\n\nShell: sidebar gains gap-[15px] and the text-[20px] font-[500] heading\nthat plugs and integrations both have; tab hover and active state move\nfrom bg-boxHover to bg-cardHover, which is a no-op in dark; the free-tier\nmodal wrapper moves onto the canonical card.\n\nApproved apps: row border-fifth rounded-[4px] -> border-newBorder\nrounded-[8px], and the avatar chip bg-fifth -> bg-newColColor, since\nbg-fifth is #6f3f2c in dark and held #5f5b52 initials at about 1.4:1.\n\nSidebar tab dimensions are unchanged: SVGLine is a fixed 52px svg, so\nthose rows already matched plugs and integrations at 52px.\n\nModal internals opened from settings are left alone, as are the\nstructural header and body split of the canonical card and\ngithub.component, which onboarding owns.\n\n* fix(theme): restore the radius scale and soften the dark card border\n\nRadius, app-wide. global.scss remaps three tailwind utilities onto custom\nproperties:\n\n  .rounded-[8px]  { border-radius: var(--app-radius-control) }\n  .rounded-[12px] { border-radius: var(--app-radius-card) }\n  .rounded-[16px] { border-radius: var(--app-radius-panel) }\n\nand builds those at :root from --radius-*. But --radius-* was declared\ninside .dark and .light, which sit on body, a descendant of :root. Custom\nproperties inherit downward, so at :root the variable did not exist, the\nfallback-less var() made the declaration invalid at computed-value time,\nand border-radius fell back to its initial value of 0.\n\nMeasured in chrome against the compiled stylesheet:\n\n  before   card=0px    ctl=0px   btn=10px   panel=0px\n  after    card=12px   ctl=8px   btn=10px   panel=16px\n\nButtons were unaffected because they use rounded-[10px], which is never\nremapped. That asymmetry, rounded buttons next to square cards, is what\npointed at the cause.\n\nThe values are identical in both themes, so they were never\ntheme-dependent; they move to :root where they are read. The per-theme\ncopies stay, overriding with the same values, so the hooks remain if\ntheme-specific radii are ever wanted. No markup changed: the cards\nalready asked for rounded-[12px] and the request was being dropped.\n\nThis reaches 108 rounded-[8px], 53 rounded-[12px] and 14 rounded-[16px]\nusages across the app, not just settings. Settings only made it obvious\nbecause that is where the large cards are. Worth a look at a couple of\nother pages before this ships.\n\nBorder: --new-border in dark goes from #c2410c to #4e2f1f. Against the\ncard background that is 3.28 down to 1.42, against 1.28 for the light\ntheme, which was already a soft hairline and is untouched. #4e2f1f is\nalready in the palette as --new-ai-btn, --color-seventh, --color-custom4\nand --color-custom30, at hue 20.4deg against the brand''s 17.5, so the\norange identity is kept rather than replaced with a neutral. --new-border\nfeeds only newBorder, used as card borders and dividers, never as an\nactive or accent indicator.\n\nAlso rounds the signature and autopost editors, which were square and\n4px, to the 8px control radius, and moves their wrappers and the teams\nbadge off the legacy custom* border tokens.\n\n* chore(rebrand): clear the last user-facing Postiz branding\n\ngrep -R \"Postiz\" over the frontend now returns nothing. Of the 40\noccurrences audited across src and the shared libraries, four were actual\nproduct branding:\n\n- the developers tab label, N8N Node (Postiz-compatible) ->\n  (Postaryx-compatible). The linked package is still n8n-nodes-postiz, so\n  the wording describes compatibility rather than ownership, which is\n  accurate until a Postaryx node is published.\n- the sentry app context name, Postiz Frontend -> Postaryx Frontend. This\n  is a display field; the service: ''frontend'' tag that alerts filter on is\n  untouched and grouping is by dsn.\n- the linkedin url placeholder, which still showed the upstream org\n  linkedin.com/company/gitroom.\n- the testimonial marquee on sign in and sign up, removed. Eight of the\n  sixteen quotes named Postiz and all sixteen are attributed to named\n  people with avatars, so rewriting the product name inside them would\n  have put words in real people''s mouths. Removing the block was chosen\n  instead of fabricating endorsements.\n\nDeliberately left, none of it branding: eight i18n keys that are live in\nall sixteen locale files and whose displayed text already reads Postaryx;\nthree POSTIZ_* env vars that are already back-compat fallbacks behind\nPOSTARYX_*; four external identifiers that would break if renamed, being\nthe @postiz/wallets import, the n8n npm url, the chrome web store listing\nand the postiz-agent skill; and one comment documenting the deliberate\ndivergence from upstream billing.\n\nRemoving the marquee orphans testimonial.component.tsx, testimonial.tsx,\nthe shared testomonials.tsx and seventeen avatars. They are left in place\nso the component can come back with real Postaryx quotes.\n\n* fix(auth): serve /logos through the proxy so the sign in logo loads\n\nThe logo showed a broken image placeholder on sign in and sign up. The\npath was already correct; the middleware was eating the request.\n\nproxy.ts redirects any non-/auth path without an auth cookie to /auth, and\nits matcher only exempts files at the root of /public:\n\n  ''/((?!api/|_next/|_static/|_vercel|[\\w-]+\\.\\w+).*)''\n\n[\\w-]+\\.\\w+ matches favicon.ico but not logos/x.svg, so the request\nreached the middleware, found no cookie on the logged-out auth page, and\nwas redirected. The img element received html instead of an svg.\n\nThis is a regression from 84b85bc6. The old logo sat at /postaryx.svg, at\nthe root, where the matcher exempted it; moving it into /logos/ lost that\nexemption. It only shows on sign in and sign up because that is the only\nplace a user has no cookie.\n\nFixed by adding /logos/ to the early-return allowlist a few lines up,\nwhere /icons/ already sits for the same reason. Verified against the\nsource: /logos/* is now allowlisted and served to a logged-out user.\n\nThe matcher will catch any future subdirectory under public the same way.\n/form/ is the only other one outside the allowlist and nothing references\nit. A general fix would be exempting .*\\.\\w+$ so files at any depth are\nskipped.\n\n* style(auth): centre the auth card and drop the empty hero column\n\nRemoving the testimonial marquee in 1b7c0f52 left the right-hand column\nholding only its heading, and a large empty area below it. The column and\nthe heading are removed, and the card is centred on both axes.\n\n  page wrapper  + items-center justify-center, - gap-[12px]\n  card column   - h-full\n\nh-full existed to fill a panel that stretched to full height; with the\npanel now sized by its content it resolved to auto anyway. gap-[12px] only\never spaced the two columns.\n\nMeasured in chrome:\n\n  1440x900   card x=420 w=600   420 left / 420 right   y=164 h=573  164 / 163\n  390x844    card x=12  w=366    12 / 12 gutters       y=136 h=573  136 / 135\n\nDesktop centres the fixed 600px card; below lg the card still takes the\nfull width with the 12px page gutter, since lg:flex-none does not apply\nthere. The card itself is untouched.\n\nThis layout is shared with forgot password, activate and login-required,\nwhich get the same centring.\n\nThe page stays hard-coded dark, as before: ModeComponent mounts only in\nthe app shell and the first-billing screen, never under /auth, so the body\nkeeps the server-rendered dark class whatever the mode cookie says.\nGiving the auth page a real light appearance means replacing those two\nhard-coded backgrounds, which is a redesign rather than a layout change.\n\n* style(auth): brand the sign in background with a contained orange halo\n\nThe page used neutral blacks, #0E0E0E behind #1A1919, both at hue 0. That\nis why it felt disconnected: nothing on it came from the Postaryx ramp.\n\nSurfaces move onto existing tokens:\n\n  page   bg-[#0E0E0E] -> bg-newBackdrop      #191712  hue 43\n  card   bg-[#1A1919] -> bg-newBgColorInner  #1f1c17  hue 38\n\nSwitching the card onto bg-newBgColorInner also picks up\n--preview-box-shadow, since global.scss already applies it to\n.bg-newBgColorInner.rounded-[12px] and the card was already rounded-[12px].\nThe brand surfaces have less raw separation than the old blacks, 1.055\nagainst 1.100, so the depth comes from that shadow and the outline rather\nthan a luminance step.\n\nTwo new tokens, both composited from rgb(194, 65, 12), which is\n--new-btn-primary, so the outline, the halo and the Sign In button are the\nsame orange:\n\n  --new-card-accent-border  rgba(..., 0.3), mapped as cardAccentBorder\n  --auth-ambient            the radial gradient, consumed by .auth-ambient\n\nThe border lands at contrast 1.33 against the card, between the 1.42 that\nread as too strong and the 1.13 that lost the brand entirely.\n\nThe halo is sized in px rather than left to farthest-corner. At the\ndefault, 100% is the viewport corner, 849px on 1440x900, so a stop at\n\"transparent 80%\" still reached 679px and tinted almost the whole page.\nWith ellipse 500px 380px the card edge sits at 68% and the falloff is\ndone by 250px out. Measured at mid-height, card spanning x=380..1060:\n\n  x=8    (25,23,18)   flat backdrop\n  x=280  (28,24,18)   warmth begins\n  x=375  (37,24,16)   peak, against the card\n  x=1220 (25,23,18)   flat backdrop\n\nAll four corners measure #191712 exactly. Five stops with a long tail to\ntransparent, so there is no visible ellipse edge.\n\nCard width goes 600 -> 680 with the inner form cap 440 -> 500, both about\n13%, so the gutters stay proportional and the form widens with the card\ninstead of gaining padding. Position, typography, form structure and\nbutton colours are unchanged.\n\n* chore(i18n): drop the last Gitroom strings from the ar and bn locales\n\nThe \"gitroom\" key is Arabic and Bengali transliterations of Gitroom, جيت روم\nand গিটরুম, while the other fourteen locales already resolve it to Postaryx.\nBoth now match.\n\nFound by scanning translation values rather than source: a grep over src\nonly sees the keys, which are identifiers, and every key whose name\ncontains postiz or gitroom already had a Postaryx value. These two were the\nonly values in any locale still carrying the old brand.\n\nNothing renders the key today, no call site passes ''gitroom'' to t(), so\nthis is dormant rather than live. Fixed anyway because it is translation\ndata that would surface the old name the moment the key is used, and\nbecause it was the last old-brand string left in the frontend.\n\n* fix(sidebar): match the app icon to the theme and drop its tile\n\nTwo problems with the sidebar icon.\n\nIt was paired the wrong way round: 03, the dark-theme icon, rendered in the\nlight theme and 04 in the dark one. That came from picking on tile-versus-\nbackground contrast, which is the wrong rule for a tiled app icon. The tile\nis meant to settle into the surrounding chrome and let the mark carry the\ncontrast, so maximising it put a white square on the dark sidebar. Now the\nasset named for a theme renders in that theme, the same convention the\nwordmark in logo-text.component.tsx already used.\n\nThe tiles then had to go. On the white sidebar 04''s white tile disappears\nand only its hairline shows, but on the dark sidebar 03''s #191712 tile\nreads as a distinct darker square against #1f1c17.\n\nAdds two transparent derivatives:\n\n  07_Postaryx_App_Icon_Dark_Transparent   03 minus its #191712 tile\n  08_Postaryx_App_Icon_Light_Transparent  04 minus its white fill and its\n                                          #E6E3DD border rect, which is a\n                                          second rect, not part of the first\n\nEach differs from its source by those rects alone; mark geometry, clip path\nand brand colours are byte-identical, and both land at 1346 bytes. Switching\ntheme now changes only the ink, not the icon''s form.\n\n03 and 04 are left untouched. They are the real app icons and the tile is\nthe point of them for the favicon, the PWA manifest and store listings.\n\n* fix(calendar): make the past-slot hatch visible in dark mode\n\n.repeated-strip was already token-driven, so it looked theme-aware, but in\ndark the two bands resolved to the same colour:\n\n  --new-bgColorInner  #1f1c17 dark / #ffffff light\n  --new-big-strips    #1f1c17 dark / #f4f1ea light\n\nThe gradient alternated #1f1c17 with #1f1c17 and painted a flat fill.\nContrast against the cell was 1.0000 in dark against 1.1280 in light, so\npast slots lost their unavailable treatment entirely rather than merely\nbeing faint. Same shape as the dark hover bug in 526398e9.\n\nRetuning --new-big-strips would have been the smaller diff but it is also\nbg-bigStrip on the signature editor textarea, so its dark value is load\nbearing elsewhere. Added --new-past-strip instead, which only\n.repeated-strip reads:\n\n  dark   #2a2620   ratio 1.1292\n  light  #f4f1ea   ratio 1.1280, the value --new-big-strips already resolved\n                   to, so light is byte identical\n\n#2a2620 is already in the palette, shared with --new-col-color,\n--new-blockSeparator and --new-boxFocused, and sits at hue 36 against the\nsurface ramp''s 38, so the hatch stays warm rather than reading as grey. Its\nratio lands within 0.001 of light''s, so neither theme carries more texture\nthan the other.\n\nDirection 135deg and the 4px/8px density are unchanged, no component file\nis touched, and calendar.tsx still gates the class on isBeforeNow alone, so\nonly past slots are affected.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrsPKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj2oQAKw0WvlziyNg+2tNJ2Gm0840\na/g3ZcL4AkuLvOpo5JmUcTsORE8I+a8sfndCzCp0nSilh3/WpWoWHwQpz70D4EHA\nKoD+iOVZT2YhS3CFvLXP2g9dKRdRxYTe7N+rkT1rFb/KVD6vhCYt3NOq0zz6S6rg\nIc6LCd8I+w2vTANEj8q7LjLnXQhUW1T8hTwXG8NKqg0HU9n32J3x3vCOD3ZIjTe1\ntXJhtI/1guhHlqlHEP0SwA1Wqs14rezc36PjQWu7xtQVqDJEUKSxsmIydJFt6F69\nEi8ja7+hn0FKJzVgghtsMef55tA8vPj1z96L4fQL3emA64fx32gL9P3APqRLyrzk\nim6uS/Qlz3SHu/BbRDLwQqYKVK2vkEFLApzj4lBfrRro4PKw7WxqOP8oCPVvxlcL\nuRurAIOhcX1rCxZyLQHUD9jE7X1on3kDLYTGlUAtlVuwa+gcBa8veJ0p5J2teDDZ\nUVlR708HFr2S9qU8vD2a2QqfmNwFLT6CHDWAICMkGnGLklywimLfpDvtYK37pg05\nZbbP1G7Z4HZKmtegkaJlNLqKH+KtkNonOFCkC9shvQksMTN4KrjLUWRmDDHYTxgs\n5kb058Wkpayy/A/1pN6sgBIRZnflDqgfkrzRmvyHuvLHnve1/SvK2u0x3FBXCTX8\nK0wyoBdLIKO2qj+shIn5\n=JzEe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verif