22800d7f4a6bdb5c4976be16a0c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/26c1f1d4844922800d7f4a6bdb5c4976be16a0c6"}],"sha":"f958b548ab804e91a0d6ec9da18dd46803658a76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/f958b548ab804e91a0d6ec9da18dd46803658a76"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270152128?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aitechnologysys-sys","id":270152128,"login":"aitechnologysys-sys","node_id":"U_kgDOEBoxwA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/26c1f1d4844922800d7f4a6bdb5c4976be16a0c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T14:20:40Z","email":"ai.technology.sys@gmail.com","name":"aitechnologysys-sys"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T14:20:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: security - rename- temporal waiting - loopback (#6)\n\n* docs: add security hardening checklist, document config sources\n\nSECURITY-HARDENING-TODO.md — findings from an audit on 8 Aug 2026, ordered\nP0 (live exposure) to P3 (hygiene), each with commands and a verification\nstep. Written to be picked up in a fresh session.\n\nThe audit''s own findings, not a generic checklist:\n- P0: .env.prod is readable in public history (commit 1195455e); Postgres\n  and Temporal passwords are hardcoded in the committed compose file;\n  secret scanning is off; the collaborator list is unverified (the gh CLI\n  here lacks push access, so only the owner can check)\n- P1: docker-compose.dev.yaml publishes SIX ports on 0.0.0.0 — Postgres,\n  Redis with no password, pgAdmin and RedisInsight web UIs. Production\n  binds all three of its ports to 127.0.0.1, so this is dev-only, but on\n  untrusted Wi-Fi it exposes the database and two admin UIs to the LAN.\n  Redis also has no requirepass and no maxmemory\n- P2: public registration is open; security headers only cover /uploads/\n- P3: log caps, dropping Elasticsearch, backup rehearsal, dependency audit\n\nIncludes the verified pg-bridge recipe for pointing DBeaver at the local\nprod stack (Postgres publishes no host port by design), and the\nloopback-publish + SSH-tunnel pattern for production, mirroring how\ntemporal-ui is already exposed.\n\nAlso records what was checked and found sound — CORS, cookie flags,\nproduction port bindings, no secrets in the image, rate limiting — so it\ndoes not get re-audited.\n\nREADME: new \"Where configuration comes from\" subsection in §3. The docs\nexplained how the image is built and deployed but never said where env\nactually enters the container, which made the CI-built image look like it\nmust be carrying secrets. It carries four env vars, none of them secret.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(compose): wait for Temporal before starting the app\n\nThe backend opens its Temporal connection during Nest module init, before\napp.listen(). With Temporal unreachable it dies there:\n\n  code: 14\n  details: ''Name resolution failed for target dns:temporal:7233''\n     at NestApplication.callInitHook\n\npm2 then does NOT restart it — it supervises the `pnpm` wrapper, which\nstays alive, so pm2 reports the process \"online\" with 0 restarts while\nnothing listens on :3000. The frontend keeps serving, so the only visible\nsymptom is nginx logging `111: Connection refused` for every /api/*\nrequest. Hit this twice while testing.\n\nCause: `postiz` depended only on postiz-postgres and postiz-redis, and\n`temporal` had no healthcheck to depend on. Nothing ordered the app after\nTemporal was ready.\n\nAdds a healthcheck to `temporal` and `condition: service_healthy` to the\napp''s depends_on. Uses `namespace describe default` rather than\n`cluster health` because it proves both that the frontend is serving and\nthat the `default` namespace exists — the namespace the backend connects\nto. Addressed as `temporal:7233`, not 127.0.0.1: Temporal binds the\ncontainer interface and loopback is refused (verified inside the\ncontainer, with a dead-port negative control).\n\nVerified by a full `down` + cold `up -d`:\n- compose now reports `temporal Healthy` before `postiz Started`\n- backend answered on :3000 within 10s with no manual intervention\n- through nginx: / -> 307, /api/user/self -> 401\nBefore this change the same cold start left the API dead indefinitely.\n\nThis matters most on the VM, where a reboot cold-starts everything at once\nwith nobody watching and the app would silently return with a dead API.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: added docs\n\n* chore: remove duplicate docs\n\n* chore: rename to postaryx for infra and local upload directory now relative\n\n* chore: parameterize Postgres/Redis/Temporal passwords via .env and document the required setup steps\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: loopback\n\n* chore: update stale docs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Koushik Deb <koushik.imon@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f8c8310a1c5afe1f0a13fba1b5059c65a667a7e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/trees/f8c8310a1c5afe1f0a13fba1b5059c65a667a7e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/commits/26c1f1d4844922800d7f4a6bdb5c4976be16a0c6","verification":{"payload":"tree f8c8310a1c5afe1f0a13fba1b5059c65a667a7e6\nparent c018abbf08866007270e34132e735d561cf05e93\nauthor aitechnologysys-sys <ai.technology.sys@gmail.com> 1786890040 +0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786890040 +0600\n\nchore: security - rename- temporal waiting - loopback (#6)\n\n* docs: add security hardening checklist, document config sources\n\nSECURITY-HARDENING-TODO.md — findings from an audit on 8 Aug 2026, ordered\nP0 (live exposure) to P3 (hygiene), each with commands and a verification\nstep. Written to be picked up in a fresh session.\n\nThe audit''s own findings, not a generic checklist:\n- P0: .env.prod is readable in public history (commit 1195455e); Postgres\n  and Temporal passwords are hardcoded in the committed compose file;\n  secret scanning is off; the collaborator list is unverified (the gh CLI\n  here lacks push access, so only the owner can check)\n- P1: docker-compose.dev.yaml publishes SIX ports on 0.0.0.0 — Postgres,\n  Redis with no password, pgAdmin and RedisInsight web UIs. Production\n  binds all three of its ports to 127.0.0.1, so this is dev-only, but on\n  untrusted Wi-Fi it exposes the database and two admin UIs to the LAN.\n  Redis also has no requirepass and no maxmemory\n- P2: public registration is open; security headers only cover /uploads/\n- P3: log caps, dropping Elasticsearch, backup rehearsal, dependency audit\n\nIncludes the verified pg-bridge recipe for pointing DBeaver at the local\nprod stack (Postgres publishes no host port by design), and the\nloopback-publish + SSH-tunnel pattern for production, mirroring how\ntemporal-ui is already exposed.\n\nAlso records what was checked and found sound — CORS, cookie flags,\nproduction port bindings, no secrets in the image, rate limiting — so it\ndoes not get re-audited.\n\nREADME: new \"Where configuration comes from\" subsection in §3. The docs\nexplained how the image is built and deployed but never said where env\nactually enters the container, which made the CI-built image look like it\nmust be carrying secrets. It carries four env vars, none of them secret.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(compose): wait for Temporal before starting the app\n\nThe backend opens its Temporal connection during Nest module init, before\napp.listen(). With Temporal unreachable it dies there:\n\n  code: 14\n  details: ''Name resolution failed for target dns:temporal:7233''\n     at NestApplication.callInitHook\n\npm2 then does NOT restart it — it supervises the `pnpm` wrapper, which\nstays alive, so pm2 reports the process \"online\" with 0 restarts while\nnothing listens on :3000. The frontend keeps serving, so the only visible\nsymptom is nginx logging `111: Connection refused` for every /api/*\nrequest. Hit this twice while testing.\n\nCause: `postiz` depended only on postiz-postgres and postiz-redis, and\n`temporal` had no healthcheck to depend on. Nothing ordered the app after\nTemporal was ready.\n\nAdds a healthcheck to `temporal` and `condition: service_healthy` to the\napp''s depends_on. Uses `namespace describe default` rather than\n`cluster health` because it proves both that the frontend is serving and\nthat the `default` namespace exists — the namespace the backend connects\nto. Addressed as `temporal:7233`, not 127.0.0.1: Temporal binds the\ncontainer interface and loopback is refused (verified inside the\ncontainer, with a dead-port negative control).\n\nVerified by a full `down` + cold `up -d`:\n- compose now reports `temporal Healthy` before `postiz Started`\n- backend answered on :3000 within 10s with no manual intervention\n- through nginx: / -> 307, /api/user/self -> 401\nBefore this change the same cold start left the API dead indefinitely.\n\nThis matters most on the VM, where a reboot cold-starts everything at once\nwith nobody watching and the app would silently return with a dead API.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: added docs\n\n* chore: remove duplicate docs\n\n* chore: rename to postaryx for infra and local upload directory now relative\n\n* chore: parameterize Postgres/Redis/Temporal passwords via .env and document the required setup steps\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: loopback\n\n* chore: update stale docs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Koushik Deb <koushik.imon@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgcc4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ3YQAFu5ka+/FP1wrmcx8bNfdvBV\naJYEXncgXcUv2fUVhPVCbHIxMg06GI+f/xgmI2IP8jqbwCpVZBmVWib2NEkFaCPO\nbVUylsm33PUPWRcndDiE9VAOzCkrRfy7QQf2M67CxpMdr5zvjDzzTGAkAmN1XviM\nGDcyG6mci2V5f1nUu2eHCzmCXj6wuPgyN8vSnu2XywRp4j7e89wmF06+fE0Bi5R7\nmfG+7qEJ8zdbUFwnv40WIXjo5kgKaeCP6heSrwOzOXIepQhDcDG7g0Lksm64ZYIu\nJ2iRucp5ZpOgNDreEhX7/uMrYZazR9AjC+zYbrn2Q6GUR6aRu+3/O/wS3kEJKU4b\nj24B2mxqAUCvv0qtbSPUCvVctZuGFchBvUf7GnjaFnnxt/j32hSyotBF8Ij6DjDq\n+oqSpCs2g5xhUrszgkylV0EJy5oJpmz0lkTBqQySVWRBBsFC1EFTPAc2BNLI7rSj\nxhGdP+lFWbXinVBnf8OZn/7JeW5GdXgrpckvxJRwZ605pAXBWUH0DVBuzgaZaspN\nsuCwiVMrx7dPI/iO7bJDgdTquVM4xtSK/JZI6EvkPFtPfpd0SXhaR8NATIpNU5sp\nokkp2wq4E4hxpdN+OmnTcoyWA7tSvYb+TO+bXdt1qNpqMj0PUfJ10AflgLTezC82\nwcKw/OEBWdSLRRPx/c9S\n=eRvQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-16T14:20:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commit/26c1f1d4844922800d7f4a6bdb5c4976be16a0c6","node_id":"C_kwDOTGyzLNoAKDI2YzFmMWQ0ODQ0OTIyODAwZDdmNGE2YmRiNWM0OTc2YmUxNmEwYzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commit/c018abbf08866007270e34132e735d561cf05e93","sha":"c018abbf08866007270e34132e735d561cf05e93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/c018abbf08866007270e34132e735d561cf05e93"}],"sha":"26c1f1d4844922800d7f4a6bdb5c4976be16a0c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/26c1f1d4844922800d7f4a6bdb5c4976be16a0c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270152128?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aitechnologysys-sys","id":270152128,"login":"aitechnologysys-sys","node_id":"U_kgDOEBoxwA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/c018abbf08866007270e34132e735d561cf05e93/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T16:03:51Z","email":"ai.technology.sys@gmail.com","name":"aitechnologysys-sys"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T16:03:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix/ci workflow triggers #5 (#5)\n\n* fix(ci): drop pnpm version input that conflicts with packageManager pin\n\nThe ESLint workflow failed at \"Install pnpm\", before it ever linted:\n\n  Error: Multiple versions of pnpm specified:\n    - version 10 in the GitHub Action config with the key \"version\"\n    - version pnpm@10.6.1 in the package.json with the key \"packageManager\"\n\npnpm/action-setup@v4 refuses that ambiguity. I copied `version: 10` from\nbuild.yml without noticing build.yml is still on action-setup@v2, which\npredates the check. Removing the input makes the action read the\npackageManager pin, so CI uses exactly pnpm@10.6.1.\n\nNote this failure happened at a step BEFORE the `continue-on-error` on the\nlint step, so the job went red even though linting is intentionally\nnon-blocking until the eslint@8 / eslint-config-next@16 mismatch is fixed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): stop Build running twice per commit\n\nUpstream''s build.yml has a bare `push:`, which matches every branch. With\n`pull_request:` also present, an open PR means the same commit builds twice\n— once for the push event, once for the pull_request event. Observed on\nfeat/integration-fixes_#3:\n\n  Build  ev=pull_request  success  24dbc7f\n  Build  ev=push          success  24dbc7f   <- same commit\n\nRestrict push to the default branch: feature branches build once via the\nPR, main builds once directly. Same coverage, half the runs.\n\nThis is a deliberate divergence from upstream, so it is recorded in\nUPSTREAM-SYNC.md''s conflict-hotspot table alongside build-containers.yml\nand eslint.yml.\n\nNote main still runs both Build and Build image per merge. Those are not\nredundant — one is a fast check, the other produces the deployable image —\nso they are left alone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Koushik Deb <koushik.imon@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"56ef9ad1961db8d3e9061c5524e4b5a21b852238","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/trees/56ef9ad1961db8d3e9061c5524e4b5a21b852238"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/commits/c018abbf08866007270e34132e735d561cf05e93","verification":{"payload":"tree 56ef9ad1961db8d3e9061c5524e4b5a21b852238\nparent 4c239dede10239c66e93d39506a0c40765a70242\nauthor aitechnologysys-sys <ai.technology.sys@gmail.com> 1786205031 +0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786205031 +0600\n\nFix/ci workflow triggers #5 (#5)\n\n* fix(ci): drop pnpm version input that conflicts with packageManager pin\n\nThe ESLint workflow failed at \"Install pnpm\", before it ever linted:\n\n  Error: Multiple versions of pnpm specified:\n    - version 10 in the GitHub Action config with the key \"version\"\n    - version pnpm@10.6.1 in the package.json with the key \"packageManager\"\n\npnpm/action-setup@v4 refuses that ambiguity. I copied `version: 10` from\nbuild.yml without noticing build.yml is still on action-setup@v2, which\npredates the check. Removing the input makes the action read the\npackageManager pin, so CI uses exactly pnpm@10.6.1.\n\nNote this failure happened at a step BEFORE the `continue-on-error` on the\nlint step, so the job went red even though linting is intentionally\nnon-blocking until the eslint@8 / eslint-config-next@16 mismatch is fixed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): stop Build running twice per commit\n\nUpstream''s build.yml has a bare `push:`, which matches every branch. With\n`pull_request:` also present, an open PR means the same commit builds twice\n— once for the push event, once for the pull_request event. Observed on\nfeat/integration-fixes_#3:\n\n  Build  ev=pull_request  success  24dbc7f\n  Build  ev=push          success  24dbc7f   <- same commit\n\nRestrict push to the default branch: feature branches build once via the\nPR, main builds once directly. Same coverage, half the runs.\n\nThis is a deliberate divergence from upstream, so it is recorded in\nUPSTREAM-SYNC.md''s conflict-hotspot table alongside build-containers.yml\nand eslint.yml.\n\nNote main still runs both Build and Build image per merge. Those are not\nredundant — one is a fast check, the other produces the deployable image —\nso they are left alone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Koushik Deb <koushik.imon@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqd1NnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXpoQAFsHaxQdsO5fP/EVhz64HZzv\ndqVHtLltFL4sgzNCtTgXqfRAIm3MJRlfhPB/IPOMF4BydjPDeisF300GWiE+pR99\nEBaZM+7/aKOZw+OEwBaf8JXuJmgx/OvjlqB8OPFAbV2DPiV1q8UfTjRQaA9cs0L2\ncqzX76AAm5MfvT1PU/mT4j8GYs051uZ4y08FkPL7iSzEcD05gwdT5+UifJyqKwPm\nmJIlI11GTqrVdWTeWF4m11LRD4eF+G/4s3t3q+RTZt8YOV8fvi6MJPkXUH/dRweU\nZeTSy1Bs98r9A0eknWowz4FWkJ8FQg+K5iS31bHS8sJN1iCAkXIoKCAzMR78RROd\nM4ezdzm9ldy+5UirD8vMnEhFWKoOMPSfRiwOPPWL/oEjtWJsuWwRraOjPvzzaxM3\nvDJ2B0J5ngsXaDPU5tIutqpxjLqBC9v5gng+ZN8lUcP67tQr9bKVetitFYWc4dhC\n8tGPS/XZbFYOuOKP7EfCPjBepzsEr0zDzpy79RHXPvcJtn4H5AjPPuSgXeRaBN/D\nArsmVaDGuLekHol8P1JqduMtJY1NrZ4+kqL0m9/AHQvb7llCFRPW8eVynBqdagna\nBdDLUmcEd6x+VWYXDE9nGSpGxXuAjPikboLdbhF9H8NqdiqaAAIrHxv4yKe09rAP\nhoIboyBzTXAyk15iW3kU\n=jjkY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-08T16:04:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commit/c018abbf08866007270e34132e735d561cf05e93","node_id":"C_kwDOTGyzLNoAKGMwMThhYmJmMDg4NjYwMDcyNzBlMzQxMzJlNzM1ZDU2MWNmMDVlOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commit/4c239dede10239c66e93d39506a0c40765a70242","sha":"4c239dede10239c66e93d39506a0c40765a70242","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/4c239dede10239c66e93d39506a0c40765a70242"}],"sha":"c018abbf08866007270e34132e735d561cf05e93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/c018abbf08866007270e34132e735d561cf05e93"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270152128?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aitechnologysys-sys","id":270152128,"login":"aitechnologysys-sys","node_id":"U_kgDOEBoxwA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aitechnologysys-sys","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/commits/4c239dede10239c66e93d39506a0c40765a70242/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T14:45:18Z","email":"ai.technology.sys@gmail.com","name":"aitechnologysys-sys"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T14:45:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Chore/deployment system #4 (#4)\n\n* chore(ci): build image in GitHub Actions, pull on the server\n\nDockerfile.dev builds all three apps with a 4 GB Node heap, spiking a\n12 GB box to ~11.4 GB and risking an OOM of the running stack. Build in\nCI instead; the server only pulls. See CONTAINMENT-DEPLOYMENT-PLAN.md §6.\n\nImage build:\n- rewrite build-containers.yml rather than adding a second workflow: it\n  already did this job but pushed to gitroomhq''s namespace, triggered on\n  tags only, and built an amd64 image we have no target for\n- arm64 only, pushing to ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}\n- :latest moves on the default branch ONLY, so a manual run on a feature\n  branch cannot become production''s next deploy\n- prune to the 20 newest package versions (hygiene; public package, so\n  storage is free)\n\nVerified safe to build off-box: NEXT_PUBLIC_* are read in server\ncomponents and threaded to the client at runtime, so nothing\nenvironment-specific is baked into the image.\n\ndocker-compose.yaml:\n- pull ${POSTIZ_IMAGE}:${POSTIZ_IMAGE_TAG} instead of building, so\n  rollback and local-image runs never edit a tracked file on the server\n\nWorkflow cleanup:\n- delete stale.yml and issue-label-triggers.yml (upstream-only; the\n  latter would have auto-closed our issues pointing at Postiz''s site)\n- delete both extension workflows (publish to Postiz''s Chrome listing)\n- rename `eslint` -> `eslint.yml`: with no extension GitHub never loaded\n  it, so it had never run. Retargeted at the root flat config, left\n  non-blocking because `pnpm eslint .` currently crashes on an\n  eslint@8 / eslint-config-next@16 mismatch\n\nDocs:\n- new CI-BUILD-CUTOVER.md: one-time post-merge steps, how to test, and\n  the GHCR private-by-default warning\n- README: dev/deploy runbook, tag table, package visibility\n- fix 11 stale `up -d --build` instructions across five docs, including\n  ORACLE-VM-DEPLOYMENT.md §6 which told you to build on the server\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(ci): group GITHUB_OUTPUT writes to satisfy shellcheck SC2129\n\nactionlint (rhysd/actionlint) reported SC2129 on the metadata step''s\nindividual >> redirects. Collect the values into variables and emit them\nin one grouped redirect. build-containers.yml is now actionlint-clean;\nthe only remaining report in the repo is upstream''s build.yml:37.\n\nVerified the tag logic is unchanged: main -> :<sha> + :latest, any other\nbranch -> :<sha> + :branch-<sanitised-name>.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: upstream isolation and sync guides\n\nTwo questions that kept coming up: does anything of ours reach Postiz,\nand how do we take their fixes.\n\nUPSTREAM-ISOLATION.md — nothing leaks, with the verification commands:\n- our repo is NOT a GitHub fork (isFork:false, parent:null), so we do not\n  share a commit store with upstream. That matters: commits pushed to a\n  public *fork* are readable from the parent repo even with no PR. Never\n  re-create this repo via the Fork button\n- closed the one real gap: the upstream remote had a working push URL, so\n  `git push upstream main` would have tried. Push URL now DISABLED, fetch\n  still works. NOTE: local .git/config only, so it does not travel with\n  clones — hence the doc\n- verified no telemetry: fetch-gtm.mjs only contacts googletagmanager and\n  skips without NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID; track.service.ts makes no HTTP calls\n- workflows reference only secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN\n- lists where we still *point at* Postiz (FUNDING.yaml collects for them,\n  the SDK defaults to api.postiz.com, agency emails hardcode postiz.com,\n  UI links to their terms/privacy) — branding, not leakage\n\nUPSTREAM-SYNC.md — how to pull their work in:\n- we are 205 commits behind, 19 ahead, last common commit 29 May 2026\n- cherry-pick vs merge, and when each is right\n- the 22 files both sides changed, grouped by resolution rule, with the\n  command to recompute the list since it drifts\n- flags vk.provider.ts as a delete/modify conflict that silently restores\n  a sanctioned provider if resolved carelessly; check-banned-providers is\n  the net\n- post-merge verification, incl. treating a schema change as a migration\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: disable inherited Sponsor button that collected for upstream\n\n.github/FUNDING.yaml carried upstream''s `open_collective: postiz`, so the\nSponsor button on our repo sent people to https://opencollective.com/postiz.\nConfirmed live before the change:\n\n  gh api graphql -f query=''{repository(owner:\"aitechnologysys-sys\",\n    name:\"veroza\"){fundingLinks{platform url}}}''\n  => [{\"platform\":\"OPEN_COLLECTIVE\",\"url\":\"https://opencollective.com/postiz\"}]\n\nAll entries commented out, so no funding link is published and GitHub hides\nthe button. Kept the file rather than deleting it: upstream still ships one,\nand deleting ours would make every future upstream change to it a\ndelete/modify conflict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Koushik Deb <koushik.imon@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"681d2c5f24c59f3561278f04704ab6504e583969","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/trees/681d2c5f24c59f3561278f04704ab6504e583969"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitechnologysys-sys/veroza/git/commits/4c239dede10239c66e93d39506a0c40765a70242","verification":{"payload":"tree 681d2c5f24c59f3561278f04704ab6504e583969\nparent 65ed8caca6c718bf4336456d2e6a61ec1267145a\nauthor aitechnologysys-sys <ai.technology.sys@gmail.com> 1786200318 +0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786200318 +0600\n\nChore/deployment system #4 (#4)\n\n* chore(ci): build image in GitHub Actions, pull on the server\n\nDockerfile.dev builds all three apps with a 4 GB Node heap, spiking a\n12 GB box to ~11.4 GB and risking an OOM of the running stack. Build in\nCI instead; the server only pulls. See CONTAINMENT-DEPLOYMENT-PLAN.md §6.\n\nImage build:\n- rewrite build-containers.yml rather than adding a second workflow: it\n  already did this job but pushed to gitroomhq''s namespace, triggered on\n  tags only, and built an amd64 image we have no target for\n- arm64 only, pushing to ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}\n- :latest moves on the default branch ONLY, so a manual run on a feature\n  branch cannot become production''s next deploy\n- prune to the 20 newest package versions (hygiene; public package, so\n  storage is free)\n\nVerified safe to build off-box: NEXT_PUBLIC_* are read in server\ncomponents and threaded to the client at runtime, so nothing\nenvironment-specific is baked into the image.\n\ndocker-compose.yaml:\n- pull ${POSTIZ_IMAGE}:${POSTIZ_IMAGE_TAG} instead of building, so\n  rollback and local-image runs never edit a tracked file on the server\n\nWorkflow cleanup:\n- delete stale.yml and issue-label-triggers.yml (upstream-only; the\n  latter would have auto-closed our issues pointing at Postiz''s site)\n- delete both extension workflows (publish to Postiz''s Chrome listing)\n- rename `eslint` -> `eslint.yml`: with no extension GitHub never loaded\n  it, so it had never run. Retargeted at the root flat config, left\n  non-blocking because `pnpm eslint .` currently crashes on an\n  eslint@8 / eslint-config-next@16 mismatch\n\nDocs:\n- new CI-BUILD-CUTOVER.md: one-time post-merge steps, how to test, and\n  the GHCR private-by-default warning\n- README: dev/deploy runbook, tag table, package visibility\n- fix 11 stale `up -d --build` instructions across five docs, including\n  ORACLE-VM-DEPLOYMENT.md §6 which told you to build on the server\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(ci): group GITHUB_OUTPUT writes to satisfy shellcheck SC2129\n\nactionlint (rhysd/actionlint) reported SC2129 on the metadata step''s\nindividual >> redirects. Collect the values into variables and emit them\nin one grouped redirect. build-containers.yml is now actionlint-clean;\nthe only remaining report in the repo is upstream''s build.yml:37.\n\nVerified the tag logic is unchanged: main -> :<sha> + :latest, any other\nbranch -> :<sha> + :branch-<sanitised-name>.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: upstream isolation and sync guides\n\nTwo questions that kept coming up: does anything of ours reach Postiz,\nand how do we take their fixes.\n\nUPSTREAM-ISOLATION.md — nothing leaks, with the verification commands:\n- our repo is NOT a GitHub fork (isFork:false, parent:null), so we do not\n  share a commit store with upstream. That matters: commits pushed to a\n  public *fork* are readable from the parent repo even with no PR. Never\n  re-create this repo via the Fork button\n- closed the one real gap: the upstream remote had a working push URL, so\n  `git push upstream main` would have tried. Push URL now DISABLED, fetch\n  still works. NOTE: local .git/config only, so it does not travel with\n  clones — hence the doc\n- verified no telemetry: fetch-gtm.mjs only contacts googletagmanager and\n  skips without NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID; track.service.ts makes no HTTP calls\n- workflows reference only secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN\n- lists where we still *point at* Postiz (FUNDING.yaml collects for them,\n  the SDK defaults to api.postiz.com, agency emails hardcode postiz.com,\n  UI links to their terms/privacy) — branding, not leakage\n\nUPSTREAM-SYNC.md — how to pull their work in:\n- we are 205 commits behind, 19 ahead, last common commit 29 May 2026\n- cherry-pick vs merge, and when each is right\n- the 22 files both sides changed, grouped by resolution rule, with the\n  command to recompute the list since it drifts\n- flags vk.provider.ts as a delete/modify conflict that silently restores\n  a sanctioned provider if resolved carelessly; check-banned-providers is\n  the net\n- post-merge verification, incl. treating a schema change as a migration\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: disable inherited Sponsor button that collected for upstream\n\n.github/FUNDING.yaml carried upstream''s `open_collective: postiz`, so the\nSponsor button on our repo sent people to https://opencollective.com/postiz.\nConfirmed live before the change:\n\n  gh api graphql -f query=''{repository(owner:\"aitechnologysys-sys\",\n    name:\"veroza\"){fundingLinks{platform url}}}''\n  => [{\"platform\":\"OPEN_COLLECTIVE\",\"url\":\"https://opencollective.com/postiz\"}]\n\nAll entries commented out, so no funding link is published and GitHub hides\nthe button. Kept the file rather than deleting it: upstream still ships one,\nand deleting ours would make every future upstream change to it a\ndelete/modify conflict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Koushik Deb <koushik.imon@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqd0D+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg7MQABa+PpbSMVmeznKrpHcfTpUe\nONkmXoaWOc2t/WC/8XbmtQtksyEZP8D5BEqCYlDfPX2XDUUgs6/hgp2hqX1j+em8\nu4meAwV/M0aMBieG0n5hn7a4OHz4DmUbsxrAybGKgAVgRV5fh41XNdYIA5LkmO0e\nnQrCJnqQ69PYpqFlcuYaovA2tk1kwz+tizFprhztyMUhFIlBNrIcrqlqE2amB9wo\nmZ2xuWq+TrMwti+waS7aqdE0hczOe5yRkxyJFwNXsEhuOhp8ayAO2dt8aMp5IjEo\nMzlQCHAkpcAv3nhudQ1qguG/VQDM4b3Y5WeHAv2MCj+IxvjQ4TiOA6iWZtOzpmMy\nj2A3mNLZ4WvoMZ9+0OXNDJFBamTotgfXGCu9RzXGYsia9rQ04/dpsRsH9LHYjP9p\nz2C5ZM0qhmdn5be1xqDZDjRUWLVg8ea31S0q4z83g+lJ1A+MVPeAb79hiN+e5p4o\nqJQikeGRbLBihqP60FJePq4ExaItUgWTCnbiMyJKZixT4gUZVTbCir6jS/9/ySFC\nLwJKbMCk+Y5GFdoTMXIkPX3Iqb5I+fVxdCLETCq9TOgt6vd3gNfiSXW8ATwloSqI\nz4RTWVbJEp7PUg2swOk3xlAEOxWg/9WARAwI1u//8O/6a66TSjtTIb66xPcbcaha\nSqQ5ki2wqxFZrHgqool+\n=8l21\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-08T14:45:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/